pulation': 'NVIDIA', 'measure': 'revenue', 'scope': 'company', 'period': 'FY2027 Q1'}, 'basis': 'reported', 'scenario': 'reported', 'kind': 'source', 'value': 81.62, 'low': None, 'high': None, 'bound': None, 'unit': 'USD billions', 'evidence': 'NVIDIA reported fiscal Q1 2027 revenue of $81.62 billion.', 'expression': '$81.62 billion', 'component': 'value', 'inputs': None, 'operation': None, 'signs': None, 'relation': None, 'disputed': None, 'bridge': None, 'basis_text': None, 'rests_on': None, 'adjusts': None, 'converts': None}]\n[{'view_id': 'v4', 'shape': 'forecast', 'outcome': '$398.1 billion', 'rung': 2, 'reference': {'figure': 'Analyst consensus of $411 billion for FY2027 (e4333, e5204); it sits in rung 2 ($392 billion to below $431.2 billion).', 'unavailable': None}, 'reasons': \"The reference is analyst consensus of $411 billion, in rung 2. My quarter-based estimate is about $398.1 billion: reported Q1 and Q2, the $108 billion Q3 guidance midpoint, and Q4 estimated by carrying forward analysts' 65% year-over-year Q4 growth expectation. The estimate remains in rung 2, below consensus. The estimate reconstructs the FY2026 Q4 comparison base from the FY2026 annual total, reported FY2027 growth comparisons for Q1 and Q2, and the stated FY2026 Q3 figure. Management's stated 70% full-year growth would imply about $367 billion from the FY2026 base, but that does not fit the reported first-half revenue plus Q3 guidance and the Q4 growth expectation; I therefore weight the quarterly run-rate more heavily. The forecast is below the total-revenue consensus rather than an assumption that consensus is the outcome.\", 'why': None, 'cites': ['e4273', 'e111', 'e2649', 'e2652', 'e3346', 'e3280', 'e5162', 'e4333', 'e5204', 'e3399', 'e3406'], 'pushes': [{'evidence_id': 'e111', 'push': 'toward_last'}, {'evidence_id': 'e2649', 'push': 'toward_last'}, {'evidence_id': 'e2652', 'push': 'toward_last'}, {'evidence_id': 'e5162', 'push': 'toward_last'}, {'evidence_id': 'e3280', 'push': 'toward_first'}, {'evidence_id': 'e2691', 'push': 'toward_first'}], 'theme_pushes': [{'view_id': 'v16', 'push': 'toward_first'}, {'view_id': 'v22', 'push': 'toward_first'}, {'view_id': 'v26', 'push': 'toward_first'}, {'view_id': 'v27', 'push': 'toward_first'}, {'view_id': 'v6', 'push': 'toward_first'}, {'view_id': 'v7', 'push': 'toward_first'}, {'view_id': 'v9', 'push': 'toward_first'}]}]\nretries 2 ['unit', 'arm', 'draw', 'attempt', 'request_sha256', 'cost_usd', 'data', 'status', 'errors', 'recorded', 'published', 'decision'] {'unit': 'pair-old-1', 'arm': 'joint', 'draw': 1, 'attempt': 2, 'request_sha256': 'c4a40d74944ccf35c4500fdd3bab6e38400a9424e11acc7b5c6e290ecd498fa8', 'cost_usd': 0.007869, 'status': 'answered', 'recorded': [], 'published': None, 'decision': 'refused'}\n[['C7', 'fy2026_q1_base_est refers to Reconstruct the prior-year quarter as FY2027 Q1 revenue divided by (1 + reported 85% year-over-year growth)., which is not defined'], ['C7', 'fy2026_q2_base_est refers to Reconstruct the prior-year quarter as FY2027 Q2 revenue divided by (1 + reported 106% year-over-year growth)., which is not defined'], ['C7', 'fy2026_q4_base_est: difference takes 2 operands, not 4'], ['C7', 'fy2026_q4_base_est: signs must give one +1 or -1 per operand of a sum or roll_forward'], ['C7', 'fy2027_q3_guidance: a figure needs either a value or a complete range with low at most high']]\n[{'id': 'fy2026_total', 'what': {'population': 'NVIDIA', 'measure': 'revenue', 'scope': 'company', 'period': 'FY2026'}, 'basis': 'reported', 'scenario': 'actual', 'kind': 'source', 'value': 215.9, 'low': None, 'high': None, 'bound': None, 'unit': '$ billion', 'evidence': 'e4273', 'expression': '$215.9 billion', 'component': 'value', 'inputs': None, 'operation': None, 'signs': None, 'relation': None, 'disputed': None, 'bridge': None, 'basis_text': None, 'rests_on': None, 'adjusts': None, 'converts': None}, {'id': 'fy2027_q1_total', 'what': {'population': 'NVIDIA', 'measure': 'revenue', 'scope': 'company', 'period': 'FY2027 Q1'}, 'basis': 'reported', 'scenario': 'actual', 'kind': 'source', 'value': 81.62, 'low': None, 'high': None, 'bound': None, 'unit': '$ billion', 'evidence': 'e111', 'expression': '$81.62 billion', 'component': 'value', 'inputs': None, 'operation': None, 'signs': None, 'relation': None, 'disputed': None, 'bridge': None, 'basis_text': None, 'rests_on': None, 'adjusts': None, 'converts': None}]\n[{'view_id': 'v4', 'shape': 'forecast', 'outcome': 'NVIDIA FY2027 company revenue: approximately $403.7 billion.', 'rung': 2, 'reference': {'figure': 'Analyst consensus of $411 billion for FY2027 (e4333, also e5204); this reference is in rung 2.', 'unavailable': None}, 'reasons': 'I forecast about $403.7 billion, in rung 2 ($392 billion to below $431.2 billion), below the $411 billion consensus reference. Q1 and Q2 were reported at $81.62 billion and $96.2 billion. For Q3, the $108 billion guidance midpoint remains the strongest company forecast, but the specific estimate of roughly $113.6 billion is supported by the reported pattern of guidance beats, including a 3.1% average beat over the prior four quarters. For Q4, I apply the analyst expectation of 65% year-over-year growth to the reconstructed FY2026 Q4 base, yielding about $112.3 billion. Summing the four quarters gives about $403.7 billion. The Q4 estimate is less certain than the near-term guided quarter, and the Q3 estimate is above guidance rather than a reported outcome.', 'why': None, 'cites': ['e111', 'e2649', 'e2652', 'e3346', 'e4273', 'e4333', 'e5054', 'e5055', 'e5056', 'e5162'], 'pushes': [{'evidence_id': 'e2693', 'push': 'toward_first'}, {'evidence_id': 'e2776', 'push': 'toward_last'}], 'theme_pushes': [{'view_id': 'v16', 'push': 'toward_first'}, {'view_id': 'v22', 'push': 'toward_first'}, {'view_id': 'v26', 'push': 'toward_first'}, {'view_id': 'v27', 'push': 'toward_first'}, {'view_id': 'v6', 'push': 'toward_first'}, {'view_id': 'v7', 'push': 'toward_first'}, {'view_id': 'v9', 'push': 'toward_first'}]}]\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
