{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_13","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '326,388p' AGENTS.md; sed -n '10957,10992p;11083,11130p' docs/DECISIONS-log.md; sed -n '188,201p' docs/prd/10-filing-phase.md; rg -n 'judging-v13|D731' docs/CURRENT_STATE.md\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_13","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '326,388p' AGENTS.md; sed -n '10957,10992p;11083,11130p' docs/DECISIONS-log.md; sed -n '188,201p' docs/prd/10-filing-phase.md; rg -n 'judging-v13|D731' docs/CURRENT_STATE.md\"","aggregated_output":"### 7.3 Iterating\n\n- **One class at a time** (Alex, 2026-10-29: \"你一类一类改，快速迭代然后测regression\"). Count the misses by mechanism; take the largest\n  class; trace it to the sentence that causes it; change one thing aimed at that class; run the whole bench (a prompt change alters every\n  request) against the previous version; read every regression to its raw answer. The pages that showed the failure locate its\n  mechanism; only the whole bench (every set, every draw) accepts the change.\n- **Name the effect on the judgement first.** Every proposed change states the effect it is expected to have on a reader or on the final\n  judgement, and is tested there where possible; a step's own counts do not decide it alone. A fix that keeps moving its error to\n  neighbouring cases stops being tuned on that set (Alex, 2026-11-09: \"感觉现在一直在修一些mknor的原地打转，你是不是要思考下现在具体还差什么high priority big impact 的需要做？\";\n  he approved this rule the same day, D391).\n- **A model call is a sampler.** Re-send a stored request before calling its answer a defect. Totals and acceptance come from at least\n  three samples beside a fresh control; a bar the control fails against itself judges nothing. A direct-read pass\n  (one send per article, every answer read beside its source; D238) locates mechanisms; its counts are one draw and are labelled so.\n- **A written log.** One row per arm: hypothesis, change, numbers against the control (regressions first), kept or not. Refuted arms and\n  your own mistakes stay in it; the next session starts from its last row.\n- **Own the loop, within what Alex agreed.** When the direction is agreed and no stop is in force (`CURRENT_STATE.md`), push your own\n  hypotheses through $0 checks and probes of a few cents on stored cases without asking. A registered test, an end-to-end run, or\n  anything that departs from the agreed plan starts on his word; a result that contradicts the hypothesis stops the line and goes to him\n  (D355: \"如果有什么不符合hypothesis 的地方你需要终止然后和我说我们重新评估\"). While he is not active (D439), \"his word\" is the council's\n  recorded consensus, and a stopped line goes to the council for re-assessment.\n- **Council before every change is sent.** A prompt, schema, code or criterion change, including one found by reading a probe, is a new\n  arm. It goes to an independent Codex read and a challenge round before its first send, and its result goes to a challenge round\n  before the next change. Reading the traces and the model's own account locates a fix; it does not review it (Alex, 2026-11-08:\n  \"你这些改动有我你有好好的跑council 再下手\").\n  Every round's reasoning and decisions are reflected on in the council until there is a consensus; the decision is recorded, and\n  the next test goes straight ahead, held to the PRD and its quantified goals, with every trace read by you yourself and not only\n  by readers (Alex, 2026-11-10: \"你应该跑council loop 来reflect 你每一轮的思路还有决策，需要你打成共识，记录决策，向前直行测试。不要drift,我们有PRD和量化目标，\n  你自己作为llm 下去看所有trace\").\n- **Small first, then one run.** A hypothesis is first validated the simplest way, on a few stored cases and a few cents, and shown to\n  work at a high level before any full analysis or stability test is built (Alex, 2026-11-04: \"don't overspend resources on wasting time.\n  We need to validate the hypothesis in a very simple way and to make sure that it works on a high level before we dive into do the full\n  analysis stability test. This is a principle you should remember\"). A day or week slice before any whole-corpus run; preflight on\n  stored data before any paid run (§5); no edit while a run is live (§9). A paid run measures a configuration; it never tries a fix.\n  Before each send, write what it can still change in the decision and which risk the cheaper check left uncovered; a replicate or\n  control that only re-measures noise or a settled comparison is not sent, and a fix is not sent before the model's own account and the\n  request locate where the decision is made (Alex, 2026-10-30: \"你跑这么多次真的有意义吗\"; \"我感觉你在为了跑而跑\"). Several fixes on one\n  base are each proved on stored data in minutes and then run together once (Alex, 2026-11-02: \"快速验证。不要drift,不要跑超级繁琐的全方位验证，先poc 改，能work,有结论，全部改动放到一起再跑完整\"; D266).\n- **One recommendation, one test.** What reaches Alex as the next step of work is one recommendation and one test of it, reached after\n  rounds of review (Claude's own, Codex's, an independent reader's) on the traces until a round finds nothing serious; never a menu of\n  arms or options, never a conclusion the next probe overturns (a choice that changes what the system does still goes to him with its\n  options and a recommendation, Authority and scope) (Alex, 2026-11-04: \"就测试一种，一次 … 你就没有自己看5轮review，能不能自己有个超级自信的定论和证据再给我提建议？\").\n  An agreed recommendation is first challenged by an independent reader on the concrete evidence behind it (\"why you give\n  recommendations for this. What did you see exactly?\"). A review round reads a rule as its author meant it; only a send shows how the\n  model applies it: before a registered test, the changed request is sent on the cases that motivated it, a few cents.\n- **A failed arm is diagnosed before the next one.** When an arm fixes its class and regresses another, write the root cause first: the\n  process error (what grew, what the small sample did not guard) and the mechanism, traced to the raw answers and the model's account,\n  never a guess stated as the cause. A small sample guards every class the change can move, not only its own. When a fix keeps moving\n  another class, the call is doing several jobs: move the rule to its owner (a field's definition sits in the schema beside the field)\n  rather than add a sentence (Alex, 2026-10-30: \"那你这些修改都是失败的呀，为什么，根因，你要检讨然后再接着尝试。我觉得你已经陷入deep loop 了\").\n  A failed step of a plan is fixed and re-run at that same step: its failures are the work list, and nothing later in the plan and no\n  substitute plan starts before it passes (Alex, 2026-11-04: \"你为什么要drift? 你现在明明还有这么多的问题要fix,你到底知不知道你要fix什么？\").\n  Before a fix is proposed, write which goal the mechanism still serves and what the product already gives for it; a measurement that\n  removes the reason a mechanism exists retires the mechanism instead of starting its repair (Alex, 2026-11-04: \"I told you to think about\n  it and you're giving me suggestions that you reject yourself\").\n- **Before a version is rejected, the rejection is checked.** Every failed or refused answer behind a \"did not pass\" is read against its\n  source and put down as the model's error or the measuring rule's or check's error; a rule or check that refuses right answers is fixed,\n  and a version that already meets the goal (what it was built to fix is fixed, nothing that was right turned wrong) is not dropped for a\n  stricter rule a later review added. Alex, 2026-11-05: \"你到底是不是再搬石头砸自己的脚？各种reject自己，你确定是正确的rejection 吗？你又下去看trace吗？\";\n  \"你不能每次都这样判错然后浪费我时间，我需要你深度看完所有失败trace给我准信下一步你要跑什么才能收敛\".\n- **Correct, then cheap.** Make the pipeline right and stable before any cost, speed or throughput work; report cost as a baseline only\n  (Alex, 2026-10-25).\n\n## 8. Product thinking\n## D725 · 2026-11-22 · Council round 45/45b: the number answers fail because related numbers have no shared, checked calculation; one judge version and one test recommended to Alex\n\n- **Alex's words** (2026-11-22): \"work with counsel and have a look at the traces of this problem … what is wrong with the system design\n  overall … look at the code, look at the traces, deeply battle it out with counsel … because I think it's the most important thing\n  that we don't hallucinate with the numbers, and I want you to get this right\".\n- **The record:** `docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/` (`RESULT.md`).\n  - Claude's reflection was written before Codex's.\n  - Codex ran an independent investigation (fresh thread `01a20501…`) and a challenge round.\n  - Consensus. One wording point stays open: the $146B is arithmetically a residual, but the order of the judge's choices is unknown.\n- **Diagnosis:**\n  1. Answers are prose; code ties no figure to a source and recomputes nothing. The production check passes contradictory or invented\n     figures.\n  2. Related questions compute the same quantities separately. The unit is one question, with 0 dependencies.\n  3. Filing and the evidence in view split their inputs. The previous conclusion carries figures without provenance.\n  4. Opening's bands amplify an error.\n- **Measured:**\n  - Data Center Q4 above company Q4 on at least 13 of 26 days in old-1;\n  - Data Center's full year above the total's on 20 consecutive days in old-2;\n  - different Q3 bases on 17 of 18 paired days;\n  - shared evidence between total and Data Center 8% in old-2;\n  - 17 of the 24 double-rejected answers from unchecked arithmetic.\n- **Recommended design** (a new judge version, Alex's to open):\n  - one judging call per related family, each question keeping its answer from one calculation;\n  - figures labelled by the judge (source, calculation, assumption; scope and period);\n  - code checks only identity and arithmetic (figure in quote, recompute, part within whole, one value per shared quantity, a sourced\n    reference);\n  - unreconciled forecasts shown as unresolved;\n  - extraction unchanged;\n  - families declared for the test.\n- **Interim for a first release:** number questions shown as \"Forecast unavailable\" until they pass the checks.\n- **The test:** a $0 gate (hand reconstructions of five stored cases, four gold controls, three planted errors), then a paid gate\n  (36 calls; joint against separate on the three draws' 09-20 pair, plus O, S and E singletons). Pass and stop lines are in `RESULT.md`.\n- **Not done:** nothing built, sent or changed.\n\n## D726 · 2026-11-22 · Alex opens a judge version for related number questions ($0 gate first) and agrees to \"Forecast unavailable\" as the first-release interim\n\n## D731 · 2026-11-22 · judging-v13's paid-gate harness is ready to send (council round 47h); the first attempt is scored on both arms; the ceiling is Alex's\n\n- **What was built (D730):** `research/2026-11-22-number-answers/paid_gate.py` (plan, send, recover, packets, verdict, replay),\n  `paid_rehearsal.py` (the provider stubbed at urllib beneath the real budget transport), `paid_mutants.py`; the plan is pinned\n  (`paid-plan.sha256`, 6f81dae5…). Record: `PAID-GATE.md` §3 to §3h.\n- **Council rounds 47 to 47h** (Codex thread `01a20501…`, read-only): each round's findings were checked against the code and fixed\n  with a rehearsal case and a mutant; round 47h answered \"READY TO SEND (once Alex names the ceiling)\".\n- **Decided by the council (D725's lines unchanged):**\n  - The first attempt is scored on both arms. D725 registers the arms \"under the same format and checks\" and says nothing about\n    retries. A joint retry can repair a cross-card conflict that the separate arm sees only after both calls end, so scoring the\n    final answers would credit the joint arm with a second chance the separate arm cannot have. Retries are sent after every first\n    attempt and read for diagnosis only (`attempts.md`, `retries.jsonl`).\n  - The readers' packets hold only what their four questions need, per card the scored answer's passages, figures, recomputed\n    outcome, assumptions and card. No attempt history, code decision or check code (a cross-member code would reveal the arm).\n  - The text the readers receive commits to the packet-to-unit mapping: a salted key's sha256 is its first line. The verdict renders\n    every packet again from the run and refuses any mismatch.\n  - The separate arm's two answers are reconciled one to one: a declared shared forecast is unified only when each call holds exactly\n    one, with the same value, bounds and unit.\n  - Completeness is judged on the scored attempts. The readings are sealed into the run, the verdict is written once, and `replay`\n    must reproduce it.\n- **Checks:** rehearsal 63 of 63 (three runs); mutants 33 of 33 caught, the control passes; the $0 gate unchanged (87 of 87, gate run 27).\n- **Cost, at `hivemind.model.PRICES` (gpt-6-luna $0.10 input, $0.50 output per million tokens; tokens estimated as characters / 4):**\n  - the 36 first attempts are about $0.17 at 4,000 output tokens each, and at most $0.39 if every answer used its 16,000-token cap;\n  - the budget transport reserves at most $0.039 for one request before sending;\n  - so $0.50 covers every scored attempt. Retries come last, and a ceiling stop among them leaves the scored test complete.\n- **Next:** Alex names the ceiling (proposed $0.50). Nothing has been sent.\n\n## D732 · 2026-11-22 · Alex: the paid gate's ceiling is $0.50\n\n- **The question** (after D731): \"judging-v13 花钱那一关（36 次计分请求，按公开价格约 0.17 美元，最坏 0.39 美元；重试排在最后、只作诊断）已经过理事会，现在可以发。你给多少上限？\"\n  Options:\n  - 0.5 美元 (recommended);\n  - 0.8 美元;\n  - 先不发.\n- **Alex's answer** (2026-11-22): \"0.5 美元 (推荐)\".\n- **Decided (Alex):** `paid_gate.py`'s `APPROVED_CEILING` is 0.5. The gate is sent once, from an empty folder\n  (`poc/data/judging-v13-paid-gate-2026-11-22/`), detached with a log and pid file, after a machine and network check. It is scored by\n  `PAID-GATE.md` §4 on the first attempts.\n| 6 | If passed: to Alex, to decide whether to run three 14-day end-to-end draws; if failed: stop, to Alex | `design-links.md` §8 | Stopped, to Alex |\n| 7 | (D361, Alex: \"按照你的提以来，但是你一定是自己反思多轮之后才给出的行动\") Measure the ceiling first: hand the source passages the gold cites straight to the frozen judgement; the custom-chip, operating-margin and capital-spending questions judged 3 times each at the window end, the custom-chip question as it was 3 times as the control; the fallback sentence is not deleted for now | `reflection-v74l.md`, `oracle-design.md` | Done: operating margin grounded 3/3, capital spending 2/3, custom chips 0/3 (the gap is in interpretation); the next step waits for Alex |\n| 8 | (D362, Alex: \"你继续啊不要scope drift and strongly follow evidence of your discovery and learning\") Two small changes where facts are not delivered, one at a time: ① when a quote is rewritten, code matches it back to the source sentence (changing nothing the model sees; verified by replaying the archive); ② a figure question's description states which figures it is derived from by definition (first sent 3 times each on the article that motivated it) | `delivery-fixes.md` | Stopped: an independent check overturned the first change's code (it would take in wrong figures); the second failed its trial send (1/3). The root: the signed standard's §5.3 does not keep two key facts, treating them as \"a restatement of known facts\" (proposal 6, awaiting approval); to Alex |\n| 9 | **Historical; superseded by D370.** (D363, Alex: \"乙\") At coverage start, record each question's starting figure once from the company's latest earnings report; the daily path still takes no restatements: design, rounds of self-checks and independent checks, validated first on the archive in the simplest way | `baseline-design.md` | Validated on two questions: the frozen extraction does not read the report's tables (0/3); with each question reading the report once on its own, the operating-margin question read its starting figure 2/3 and the capital-spending question 3/3, and the judgement then judged right (2/3, 3/3), about 2.5 cents. All 22 questions tested once (2026-11-05, Alex: \"你充分验证\"; files chosen by code, a same-day control, about $0.43): v10 and v12 judged right 9/9 each; no question already judged right turned wrong; but 5 of the 53 figures read were other quantities (the Vera CPU question and the Blackwell and Rubin question took a larger or neighbouring revenue line), so it failed condition 3, written beforehand. The model itself pointed to the reading instructions' sentence \"write the lines it is computed from, or the line the report uses for it\"; stopped, to Alex. Alex: \"改\"; only this sentence was changed (\"write only the lines it is computed from, or the same quantity under another name; never a broader line or a line next to it\"), tried on 4 questions first, then tested on all 22 (about $0.36): all three conditions passed: v10 and v12 9/9 each, no question judged right turned wrong, and all 46 figures were the questions' own quantities. Checked after an independent reader's challenge: the new sentence made the reading miss the capital-spending line in 3 of 12 reads, and it had been tested only on the one May report; the fourth version (a line-by-line re-check after writing) removed too much and failed; after a census of every failure trace (Alex: \"我需要你深度看完所有失败trace给我准信\"), the third version with the repaired quote check was chosen (D365): 0 wrong figures on the held-out August report; built into the production system (poc-v116; the $0 checks and the tests all pass). The full acceptance, three 14-day draws (Alex: \"跑验收\"; a same-day control; about $4.79): all passed: operating margin and capital spending judged right 3/3 each (the control never judged them), 53 against 45 in total (of 57); for the China-share question, the only one two fewer, both readers found the starting figures did not lead it astray. Alex: \"都做\": poc-v116 became the default (D366); the code was committed and a PR opened |\n\n## 9. Alex's own words on this matter (in time order)\n\n- \"你这个单独开一个专题出来解决 … 是promot，是系统结构设计还是到底哪里有问题挂错一堆东西，机制是不是有问题（一定要挂吗？有没有可能是杂音\" (2026-11-03)\n- \"So if it's a customer problem or other companies that you think is relating NVIDIA and it's the wrong evidence, then what is the standard for it? … from a hedge fund analyst standpoint, are these even relevant? Do you think your ruler is wrong in this aspect?\" (2026-11-04)\n- \"你确定下你接下来要改进的量化目标，以及你要看到端到端我们的管线是要做什么的，不要乱硬优化，要看到目标\" (2026-11-04)\n- \"就测试一种，一次 … 能不能自己有个超级自信的定论和证据再给我提建议\" (2026-11-04)\n- \"这些只是类型题，你需要抽象拔高我们现在的核心问题和卡点。这个很重要这样改下去才是对的\" (2026-11-04)\n- \"你把这个写好成下一阶段核心PRD然后不要drift, 把所有需要的context 全部充分记录，每次开始前都需要revisit, 然后开始做\" (2026-11-04)\n- \"go\" (2026-11-04, on the proposed amendments to §5.2 and §6 and on this test)\n448:**The one next task: Alex names the ceiling for judging-v13's paid gate (D731; proposed $0.50).** The harness is built, rehearsed\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_14","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"python3 -B -c 'import json,pathlib,collections,re,sys,importlib.util\nD=pathlib.Path('\\\\''docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers'\\\\'')\nR=pathlib.Path('\\\\''poc/data/judging-v13-paid-gate-2026-11-22'\\\\'')\nP={(q['\\\\''unit'\\\\''],q['\\\\''arm'\\\\'']):q for q in json.loads((D/'\\\\''paid-plan.json'\\\\'').read_text())}\nJ={n:[(i,r) for i,l in enumerate((R/(n+'\\\\''.jsonl'\\\\'')).open(),1) if (r:=json.loads(l))['\\\\''status'\\\\'']\"'!='\"'\\\\''started'\\\\''] for n in ['\\\\''answers'\\\\'','\\\\''retries'\\\\'']}\ndef arm(r): return r['\\\\''arm'\\\\''] if r['\\\\''arm'\\\\''] in ('\\\\''joint'\\\\'','\\\\''single'\\\\'') else '\\\\''separate'\\\\''\ndef cat(e):\n c,s=e\n if c=='\\\\''C7'\\\\'':\n  if '\\\\''not defined'\\\\'' in s:return c+'\\\\'': dangling'\\\\''\n  if '\\\\''needs either a value'\\\\'' in s:return c+'\\\\'': point/range'\\\\''\n  if '\\\\''signs must'\\\\'' in s:return c+'\\\\'': signs'\\\\''\n  if '\\\\'' operands, not '\\\\'' in s:return c+'\\\\'': arity'\\\\''\n  if '\\\\''is not a figure'\\\\'' in s:return c+'\\\\'': outcome missing'\\\\''\n  if '\\\\'': outcome '\\\\'' in s and '\\\\'' measures '\\\\'' in s:return c+'\\\\'': outcome key'\\\\''\n  return c+'\\\\'': '\\\\''+s\n if c=='\\\\''C1'\\\\'':\n  if '\\\\''was not shown'\\\\'' in s:return c+'\\\\'': evidence'\\\\''\n  if '\\\\''not a complete'\\\\'' in s:return c+'\\\\'': expression'\\\\''\n  return c+'\\\\'': value/unit/etc'\\\\''\n if c=='\\\\''C2'\\\\'':\n  if '\\\\''cannot be evaluated'\\\\'' in s:return c+'\\\\'': eval'\\\\''\n  if '\\\\''gives'\\\\'' in s:return c+'\\\\'': arithmetic'\\\\''\n  return c+'\\\\'': bound'\\\\''\n if c=='\\\\''C8'\\\\'':\n  if '\\\\''time aggregation'\\\\'' in s:return c+'\\\\'': time'\\\\''\n  if '\\\\''roll_forward'\\\\'' in s:return c+'\\\\'': roll_forward'\\\\''\n  if '\\\\''with no bridge'\\\\'' in s:return c+'\\\\'': bridge'\\\\''\n  if '\\\\''states no relation'\\\\'' in s:return c+'\\\\'': relation'\\\\''\n  if '\\\\''share needs'\\\\'' in s:return c+'\\\\'': share'\\\\''\n  return c+'\\\\'': '\\\\''+s\n return c\ndef fields(d):\n for f in d['\\\\''figures'\\\\'']:\n  for k in ('\\\\''evidence'\\\\'','\\\\''bridge'\\\\'','\\\\''disputed'\\\\''):\n   yield k,f.get(k),f\n  for k in ('\\\\''inputs'\\\\'','\\\\''rests_on'\\\\'','\\\\''converts'\\\\''):\n   for v in f.get(k) or []:yield k,v,f\n  yield '\\\\''adjusts.figure'\\\\'',(f.get('\\\\''adjusts'\\\\'') or {}).get('\\\\''figure'\\\\''),f\n for a in d['\\\\''answers'\\\\'']:\n  yield '\\\\''answers[].outcome'\\\\'',a.get('\\\\''outcome'\\\\''),a\n  yield '\\\\''answers[].reference.figure'\\\\'',(a.get('\\\\''reference'\\\\'') or {}).get('\\\\''figure'\\\\''),a\ndef allowed(k,f,p):\n if k=='\\\\''evidence'\\\\'':return p['\\\\''passages'\\\\'']\n if k=='\\\\''rests_on'\\\\'':return set(f)|set(p['\\\\''passages'\\\\''])\n return f\nfor n,js in J.items():\n print('\\\\''\\\\n'\\\\'',n,'\\\\''count/cost'\\\\'',len(js),sum(r['\\\\''cost_usd'\\\\''] for _,r in js))\n misc=collections.defaultdict(set)\n for a in ('\\\\''joint'\\\\'','\\\\''separate'\\\\'','\\\\''single'\\\\'','\\\\''ALL'\\\\''):\n  rr=[r for _,r in js if a==arm(r) or a=='\\\\''ALL'\\\\'']\n  print(a,len(rr),'\\\\''figures'\\\\'',sum(len(r['\\\\''data'\\\\'']['\\\\''figures'\\\\'']) for r in rr),'\\\\''statuses'\\\\'',collections.Counter(r['\\\\''decision'\\\\''] for r in rr))\n  print('\\\\''codes answers'\\\\'',dict(collections.Counter(k for r in rr for k in set(c for c,_ in r['\\\\''errors'\\\\'']))))\n  print('\\\\''codes errors'\\\\'',dict(collections.Counter(c for r in rr for c,_ in r['\\\\''errors'\\\\''])))\n  kc=collections.Counter();ka=collections.Counter();ki=collections.Counter();units=collections.Counter()\n  for r in rr:\n   p=P[r['\\\\''unit'\\\\''],r['\\\\''arm'\\\\'']]; f={f['\\\\''id'\\\\''] for f in r['\\\\''data'\\\\'']['\\\\''figures'\\\\'']}; seen=set()\n   units.update(x['\\\\''unit'\\\\''] for x in r['\\\\''data'\\\\'']['\\\\''figures'\\\\''] if x['\\\\''kind'\\\\'']=='\\\\''source'\\\\'')\n   for k,v,obj in fields(r['\\\\''data'\\\\'']):\n    if v is None or v in allowed(k,f,p):continue\n    if not re.fullmatch(r'\\\\''[\\\\w.:-]+'\\\\'',v):\n     kc[k]+=1;seen.add(k)\n    else:\n     ki[k]+=1;misc[k].add(v)\n   ka.update(seen)\n  print('\\\\''prose'\\\\'',dict(kc),'\\\\''answers affected'\\\\'',dict(ka),'\\\\''idlike dangling'\\\\'',dict(ki),'\\\\''source units'\\\\'',dict(units))\n  print('\\\\''subclasses'\\\\'',dict(collections.Counter(cat(e) for r in rr for e in r['\\\\''errors'\\\\''])))\n print('\\\\''idlike values'\\\\'',dict(misc))\n print('\\\\''other classification'\\\\'')\n for i,r in js:\n  g=collections.Counter(cat(e) for e in r['\\\\''errors'\\\\''])\n  print(i,r['\\\\''unit'\\\\''],r['\\\\''arm'\\\\''],r['\\\\''draw'\\\\''],dict(g))\n'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
