Center revenue of $89 billion as a proxy for AI revenue, reasoning that the segment is overwhelmingly driven by AI computing demand.\\n    Quote: Nvidia expects total revenue to grow about 70% in fiscal 2028, starting from an already enormous base of nearly $100 billion per quarter. The company does not report a stand-alone \\\"AI revenue\\\" figure, but data center revenue ($89 billion in the latest quarter) is a reasonable proxy, since that business is overwhelmingly driven by AI computing demand.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e4717, e5295; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\n- e5263 [party_statement; benzinga.com, reporting Huang's CNBC interview; original source Jensen Huang ; from gnews:7218ec5f13c26358ef736b14 2026-09-18] Huang said NVIDIA Grace Blackwell systems rent for about $16 per GPU hour now, versus roughly $5 under some contracts signed a year earlier.\\n    Quote: Huang also pointed to rising rental prices as evidence of tight demand. He said NVIDIA Grace Blackwell systems can now rent for about $16 per GPU hour, compared with roughly $5 under some contracts signed a year ago.\\n- e5269 [party_statement; CRN, reporting Kapusta\\u2019s interview; original source Chris Kapusta, GDT 2026-09-17; from gnews:35efa49dae24bb21af438112 2026-09-18] GDT executive Chris Kapusta said GDT was selling AI infrastructure and related services to roughly 20 neoclouds.\\n    Quote: In a Thursday interview with CRN before the acquisition was announced , GDT executive Chris Kapusta said the Dallas-based solution provider has been selling AI infrastructure and related services to roughly 20 neoclouds, the new class of cloud services providers that almost exclusively focus on fulfilling demand for AI compute.\\n- e5270 [third_party_view; CRN; original source Gartner ; from gnews:35efa49dae24bb21af438112 2026-09-18] Gartner forecast that neoclouds would represent 20% of the $267 billion AI cloud market by 2030.\\n    Quote: According to research firm Gartner, neoclouds are expected to represent 20 percent of the $267 billion AI cloud market by 2030, underlining their competitiveness against hyperscalers.\\n- e5293 [fact; finance.yahoo.com; original source NVIDIA Corporation ; from gnews:d7c05e7b0777edd1a79bc806 2026-09-18] NVIDIA reported Q2 Data Center revenue of $89 billion, up 117% year over year.\\n    Quote: NVIDIA Corporation (NASDAQ:NVDA)'s data center revenue doubled to $89 billion in Q2 for a 117% bump\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e4178; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\n- e5304 [third_party_view; Benzinga, reporting Brad Gerstner\\u2019s remarks at the All-In Summit; original source Brad Gerstner ; from gnews:4256ae7ea51b8cf4d4bb371b 2026-09-18] Brad Gerstner estimated that Anthropic, OpenAI and xAI had combined annualized revenue of roughly $100 billion based on July figures and need to reach at least $180 billion by year-end 2026.\\n    Quote: Gerstner estimated that Anthropic, OpenAI and SpaceX (NASDAQ: SPCX ), which owns xAI, had a combined run rate of roughly $100 billion based on figures circulating in July. Gerstner said the companies need to reach at least $180 billion by year-end, up about 80% from his July estimate, \\\"just to keep the AI trade intact.\\\"\\n- e5305 [rumour; Benzinga; original source Benzinga, reporting an unspecified source ; from gnews:4256ae7ea51b8cf4d4bb371b 2026-09-18] Anthropic\\u2019s reported revenue run rate was $65 billion in July 2026, up from $47 billion in May 2026.\\n    Quote: Anthropic's revenue run rate reportedly reached $65 billion in July, up from $47 billion in May.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e2204; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\n- e5306 [third_party_view; Benzinga, reporting Brad Gerstner\\u2019s remarks at the All-In Summit; original source Brad Gerstner ; from gnews:4256ae7ea51b8cf4d4bb371b 2026-09-18] Brad Gerstner said Microsoft and Alphabet are building toward $1.5 trillion in annual capital expenditures, which requires AI-lab customers to pay for the capacity.\\n    Quote: \\\"If you're going to build a trillion and a half dollars a year in capex, somebody has to pay for it,\\\" he said.\\n- e5309 [fact; Harsh Chauhan, fool.com; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:ad94c78d09fe41fc3f29bbca 2026-09-18] NVIDIA reported $164 billion of Data Center segment revenue in the first six months of FY2027.\\n    Quote: The company has generated $164 billion in revenue from its data center segment in the first six months of fiscal 2027.\\n- e5310 [third_party_view; Harsh Chauhan, fool.com; original source Harsh Chauhan 2026-09-18; from gnews:ad94c78d09fe41fc3f29bbca 2026-09-18] The author calculated that NVIDIA\\u2019s first-six-month FY2027 Data Center revenue implies a full-year run rate of just under $330 billion.\\n    Quote: That translates into an annual run rate of just under $330 billion for the full year.\\n- e5312 [fact; Zacks.com; original source NVIDIA 2026-08-26; from gnews:57a69374b8fa083ce36ecfb1 2026-09-18] NVIDIA Data Center revenue was $89 billion in FY2027 Q2, up 117% year over year and 18% sequentially.\\n    Quote: The Data Center business remained the key growth driver, with revenues rising 117% year over year and 18% sequentially to $89 billion.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e5003; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\n- e5356 [fact; fool.com author Daniel Sparks; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:5feec912090c2af6467eed38 2026-09-19] NVIDIA reported $89 billion of Data Center revenue in fiscal Q2 2027.\\n    Quote: with $89 billion of that coming from data centers.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e3398; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\n- e5364 [fact; fool.com (Daniel Sparks); original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:e5b9c11e2c8ef9754946a897 2026-09-20] NVIDIA reported FY2027 second-quarter Data Center revenue of $89.0 billion, up 117% year over year.\\n    Quote: Data center revenue climbed 117% to $89.0 billion.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e4848; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\n\\n[Themes in force, 7]\\n- v16 (chip-export-controls, due 2026-12-31) Will the U.S. Senate pass the Remote Access Security Act by December 31, 2026?: now rung 2 No; judged 2026-08-19; reasons: No market consensus is supplied. The deadline reference is passage by December 31, 2026 (rung 1); the alternative is that the Senate has not passed RASA by then (rung 2). RASA had passed the House but was still awaiting Senate action on July 23, and the August 19 report says it had still not passed.\\n- v22 (chip-export-controls, due 2027-01-31) Will Taiwan\\u2019s Ministry of Economic Affairs adopt performance-threshold export controls for advanced chips by January 31, 2027?: now rung 2 No; judged 2026-07-28; reasons: The reference is rung 2: no formal adoption by the deadline is indicated in the available plan or timeline. The consultations and reported consideration make adoption more plausible than before, but the Ministry set no timeline; that evidence does not make formal adoption by January 31, 2027 the mor\\n- v26 (chip-export-controls, due 2027-01-31) Will Taiwan adopt a criminal ban on all AI chip exports to China by January 31, 2027?: now rung 1 No; judged 2026-07-29; reasons: The reference is rung 1: the supplied evidence says Taiwan is considering a ban, not that it has adopted one. That consideration, in the context of an investigation into suspected smuggling, raises the prospect of action, but the evidence gives no adopted measure, legislative stage, or timetable. Th\\n- v27 (chip-export-controls, due 2026-12-31) Will the U.S. Department of Commerce conclude its investigation into Chinese firms\\u2019 access to advanced U.S. chips by December 31, 2026?: now rung 2 No; judged 2026-08-07; reasons: The reference is rung 2 (No): no market consensus or Commerce completion deadline is supplied, and the stated status is a formal investigation, not a scheduled conclusion. The evidence makes non-conclusion by December 31, 2026 more likely: Commerce is still examining access through computing capacit\\n- v6 (ai-capex, due 2027-02-28) How much will the four largest AI hyperscalers spend on data center capital expenditures in calendar 2026?: now rung 4 $700 billion to below $800 billion; judged 2026-09-19; reasons: The market reference for the four companies is roughly $720\\u2013745 billion, which sits in rung 4. The evidence implies about $760 billion for the four: the direct four-company estimate is $760 billion, and the later Amazon and Alphabet figures are consistent with company spending plans already reflecte\\n- v7 (ai-capex, due 2028-02-29) How much will the four largest AI hyperscalers spend on data center capital expenditures in calendar 2027?: now rung 4 $1.1 trillion to below $1.2 trillion; judged 2026-09-19; reasons: The market reference is BofA's $1.08 trillion 2027 estimate for five companies; using the carried Oracle adjustment of roughly $100\\u2013$150 billion, the four-company reference is about $930\\u2013$980 billion, in rung 3. NVIDIA's $1.3 trillion forecast for the top five, adjusted by the same Oracle amount, im\\n- v9 (chip-export-controls, due 2027-01-31) Will China authorize purchases of Nvidia H200 chips by AI companies by January 31, 2027?: now rung 2 Yes; judged 2026-09-20; updated since this thesis was last judged; reasons: The reference is rung 1: no Chinese authorization by the deadline. The evidence favors a narrow, selective authorization by January 31, 2027, rather than no authorization: reports name prospective buyers, and one item says limited H200 imports were recently allowed. This is not a forecast of broad a\\n\\nAnswer per the JSON schema: one calculation for the family and one answer per member.\",\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/paid-plan.json:7509:  \"user\": \"[Family] members:\\nThesis v14 (NVDA, asset, focus \\\"NVIDIA FY2027 total revenue\\\", FY2027, due 2027-02-28): How much total revenue will NVIDIA report for FY2027?\\nLadder: rung 1 Strongly bullish: Total revenue is at least $450 billion. / rung 2 Bullish: Total revenue is at least $400 billion but less than $450 billion. / rung 3 Neutral: Total revenue is at least $350 billion but less than $400 billion. / rung 4 Bearish: Total revenue is at least $300 billion but less than $350 billion. / rung 5 Strongly bearish: Total revenue is less than $300 billion.\\n\\nThesis v9 (NVDA, asset, focus \\\"NVIDIA FY2027 Data Center segment revenue\\\", FY2027, due 2027-02-28): How much Data Center segment revenue will NVIDIA report for FY2027?\\nLadder: rung 1 Strongly bullish: FY2027 Data Center segment revenue is at least $450 billion. / rung 2 Bullish: FY2027 Data Center segment revenue is at least $400 billion and below $450 billion. / rung 3 Neutral: FY2027 Data Center segment revenue is at least $350 billion and below $400 billion. / rung 4 Bearish: FY2027 Data Center segment revenue is at least $300 billion and below $350 billion. / rung 5 Strongly bearish: FY2027 Data Center segment revenue is below $300 billion.\\n\\nRelations: v9 is part of v14.\\nShared quantities, one forecast each per scenario: NVIDIA, revenue, company, FY2027 Q3; NVIDIA, revenue, company, FY2027 Q4.\\nOutcome keys (population | measure | scope | period), to be used exactly: v14 = NVIDIA | revenue | company | FY2027; v9 = NVIDIA | revenue | Data Center | FY2027.\\n\\n[Evidence in view for the family, 237 items]\\n- e195 [third_party_view; Jeran Wittenstein, citing data compiled by Bloomberg; original source Bloomberg ; from gnews:49f225cd79fb22132f3b9ee4 2026-07-10] Bloomberg data project NVIDIA FY2027 sales of $393 billion, up 82%, and profits of $228 billion, up 90%.\\n    Quote: The chipmaker is projected to deliver $228 billion in profits on sales of $393 billion in fiscal 2027, which ends Jan. 31. That would represent an expansion of 90% and 82%, respectively, according to data compiled by Bloomberg.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e572, e669, e800; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\n- e238 [fact; barchart.com (analyst); original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:82472d26336e1982cf8a3eff 2026-07-12] NVIDIA reported fiscal Q1 2027 total revenue of $81.6 billion, up 85% year over year.\\n    Quote: For the first quarter of fiscal 2027, revenue jumped 85% year-over-year (YOY) to $81.6 billion, easily beating analyst expectations.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e223, e248, e268, e967; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\n- e321 [fact; finance.yahoo.com; original source SK Hynix ; from gnews:c73b90b63a733c6ab712fcdd 2026-07-14] SK Hynix is slowing its HBM4 ramp and redirecting capacity to conventional DRAM, where shortages have pushed operating margins above HBM margins.\\n    Quote: SK Hynix is deliberately slowing its HBM4 ramp to redirect capacity into conventional DRAM, where shortages have pushed operating margins above HBM's.\\n- e906 [fact; SK hynix; original source SK hynix and NVIDIA 2026-07-25; from gnews:db759b7fd9bedbcd0f632fe6 2026-07-25] SK hynix and NVIDIA are entering a long-term AI memory partnership intended to give NVIDIA stable supply of next-generation AI memory.\\n    Quote: SK hynix is also entering into a long-term AI memory partnership with NVIDIA. As a follow-up measure to solidify their previous long-term technical partnership, this agreement allows NVIDIA to secure a stable supply of next-generation AI memory, while enabling SK hynix to expand the foundation for growth.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e948, e989, e990; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\n- e1336 [fact; Insider Monkey; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:39deea97b690ac7b56dada0b 2026-07-31] NVIDIA has roughly $1 trillion in confirmed orders for Blackwell and Vera Rubin chips through 2027.\\n    Quote: The company already has roughly $1 trillion in confirmed orders for its Blackwell and Vera Rubin chips through 2027\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e817; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\n- e2421 [third_party_view; CNBC; original source LSEG analysts ; from gnews:58fb7b4d430994417016dc48 2026-08-25] LSEG analysts expected NVIDIA total revenue to grow 83% to $396 billion in FY2027, then grow 44% in FY2028.\\n    Quote: For the full year, analysts expect 83% revenue growth to $396 billion, before slowing to 44% expansion next year, according to LSEG.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e2268, e2697, e3411, e3938; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\n- e2497 [fact; NVIDIA Corporation; original source NVIDIA Corporation 2026-08-26; from nvidianews:nvidia-announces-financial-results-for-second-quarter-fiscal-2027 2026-08-26] NVIDIA reported Q2 FY2027 revenue of $96.2 billion, up 18% quarter over quarter and 106% year over year.\\n    Quote: NVIDIA (NASDAQ: NVDA) today reported revenue for the second quarter ended July 26, 2026, of $96.2 billion, up 18% from the previous quarter and up 106% from a year ago.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e2515, e2573, e2666, e2709, e2722, e2853, e4914; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\n- e2499 [party_statement; NVIDIA Corporation; original source NVIDIA Corporation 2026-08-26; from nvidianews:nvidia-announces-financial-results-for-second-quarter-fiscal-2027 2026-08-26] NVIDIA guided Q3 FY2027 revenue to $108.0 billion, plus or minus 2%, assuming no Data Center compute revenue from China.\\n    Quote: Revenue is expected to be $108.0 billion, plus or minus 2%. NVIDIA is not assuming any Data Center compute revenue from China in its outlook.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e2518, e2566; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\n- e2536 [fact; Colette Kress; original source Amazon Web Services ; from truenorth:transcript:NVDA:2026-08-26 2026-08-26] AWS plans to deploy an additional 2 million NVIDIA GPUs beginning in Q2 FY2027 through Q2 FY2029, alongside Vera CPUs, some integrated with Rubin and some standalone.\\n    Quote: AWS is deploying an additional 2 million GPUs starting this quarter through the second quarter of fiscal '29 along with Vera, CPUs, some integrated with Rubin, other standalone.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e2510, e2729; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\n- e2705 [party_statement; finance.yahoo.com, reporting Huang\\u2019s remarks on the earnings call; original source Jensen Huang, NVIDIA CEO 2026-08-26; from gnews:73b5d87b6d484d8e54c69370 2026-08-26] Jensen Huang said NVIDIA had supply for 70% of current customers\\u2019 demand, while demand was much higher; no period was specified.\\n    Quote: Nvidia currently has supply for 70% of the demand from current customers, said Huang during the call, adding that demand is \\\"much higher than that.\\\"\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e2723; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\n- e2723 [party_statement; Jensen Huang, quoted by Benzinga; original source Jensen Huang 2026-08-26; from gnews:0f6c59de72ffa6b9a2036962 2026-08-26] CEO Jensen Huang said actual demand for NVIDIA chips was far greater than 70%, while memory, power, and data-center capacity constraints were limiting growth to that pace.\\n    Quote: Huang said actual demand for Nvidia's chips is far greater than 70%, but limited memory, power, and data center capacity are holding growth to that pace for now.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e2705; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\n- e2951 [party_statement; finance.yahoo.com; original source NVIDIA CFO Colette Kress 2026-08-27; from gnews:f1af0b706051f98c7b8b3394 2026-08-27] NVIDIA CFO Colette Kress said customer forecasts indicate potential revenue growth near twice the company\\u2019s 70% FY2028 projection, while memory, data-center power and construction bottlenecks cap near-term output.\\n    Quote: CFO Colette Kress explained that customer forecasts actually point to potential growth rates near double the guided 70%, but severe supply chain bottlenecks\\u2014ranging from memory availability to data center power and construction\\u2014are capping the company's near-term output.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e2539, e3384; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\n- e3482 [party_statement; fool.com (analyst); original source Taiwan Semiconductor Manufacturing ; from gnews:a6dd88163443f40d35bdbdee 2026-08-31] Taiwan Semiconductor Manufacturing raised its 2026 capital expenditure guidance by $8 billion to $62 billion.\\n    Quote: For example, Nvidia's foundry partner Taiwan Semiconductor Manufacturing has increased its 2026 capital expenditure guidance by $8 billion to $62 billion.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read it as a later version of e1907 (); both are in force: TSMC planned a 2026 capital expenditure budget of $52 billion to $56 billion, with packaging capex rising toward 20% of the budget.\\n- e3575 [third_party_view; Futurum Group; original source Futurum Group 2026-08-31; from gnews:70fb4524ad11d15f13b9cc63 2026-08-31] Futurum assessed that NVIDIA's Q2 FY2027 AI infrastructure demand was constrained by supply rather than demand.\\n    Quote: NVIDIA\\u2019s Q2 FY 2027 results showed that AI infrastructure demand remains supply-constrained rather than demand-constrained.\\n- e3633 [party_statement; fool.com (analyst); original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:6302783b3fb0f26db4f5d501 2026-09-01] NVIDIA plans to raise prices by about 15% in early 2027 to mitigate rising memory costs.\\n    Quote: Nvidia plans to mitigate those pressures with about a 15% price increase in early 2027.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e2366; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\n- e3902 [third_party_view; fool.com (Geoffrey Seiler); original source SK Hynix ; from gnews:621e1b678a037049c86a70af 2026-09-04] SK Hynix predicted that the DRAM market would remain supply-constrained through at least 2030.\\n    Quote: Rival SK Hynix has predicted that the DRAM market will remain supply-constrained through at least 2030\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e4010, e4613; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\n- e3943 [party_statement; The Motley Fool author; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:89698c9955cf8aa35b642970 2026-09-04] NVIDIA's FY2027 Q3 guidance implied total revenue growth of 12% sequentially at the midpoint.\\n    Quote: In the meantime, Nvidia's fiscal 2027 third-quarter guidance implies 12% sequential growth at the midpoint.\\n- e4012 [party_statement; fool.com (analyst), reporting Micron's guidance; original source Micron Technology ; from gnews:26483af76fc42582dd341a59 2026-09-05] Micron guided that tight memory-market conditions will persist beyond calendar 2027.\\n    Quote: Micron's most recent guidance was that tight conditions will \\\"persist beyond calendar 2027.\\\"\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read it as \n... 956760 bytes omitted ...\nat the DRAM market will remain supply-constrained through at least 2030\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e4010, e4613; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\n- e3943 [party_statement; The Motley Fool author; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:89698c9955cf8aa35b642970 2026-09-04] NVIDIA's FY2027 Q3 guidance implied total revenue growth of 12% sequentially at the midpoint.\\n    Quote: In the meantime, Nvidia's fiscal 2027 third-quarter guidance implies 12% sequential growth at the midpoint.\\n- e4012 [party_statement; fool.com (analyst), reporting Micron's guidance; original source Micron Technology ; from gnews:26483af76fc42582dd341a59 2026-09-05] Micron guided that tight memory-market conditions will persist beyond calendar 2027.\\n    Quote: Micron's most recent guidance was that tight conditions will \\\"persist beyond calendar 2027.\\\"\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read it as a later version of e232 (); both are in force: Micron suggested memory supply may not meaningfully normalize until 2027 and may return gradually to balance by 2028; Kearney\\u2019s PERLab reportedly projected the shortage could last into 2030.\\n- e4061 [third_party_view; fool.com (Harsh Chauhan); original source Analysts ; from gnews:af250f8ec57c04287c3dc180 2026-09-06] Analysts expect NVIDIA revenue of $411 billion in FY2027.\\n    Quote: Analysts expect Nvidia's revenue to land at $411 billion in fiscal 2027, an increase of almost 60x in a decade.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e4097; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\n- e4097 [third_party_view; Keithen Drury, fool.com; original source Wall Street analysts ; from gnews:7bf2e552fe4c58c4aeaf5b2e 2026-09-06] Wall Street analysts expect NVIDIA total revenue of $411 billion in FY2027.\\n    Quote: For FY 2027 (ending in January 2027), Wall Street analysts expect $411 billion in revenue.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e4061, e4134, e5056; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\n- e4115 [fact; finance.biggo.com; original source OpenAI ; from gnews:595a83074fb8af0237f822ce 2026-09-06] OpenAI has committed to approximately 12 gigawatts of NVIDIA compute through 2030.\\n    Quote: OpenAI has committed to approximately 12 gigawatts of Nvidia compute through 2030.\\n- e4117 [party_statement; Jensen Huang, quoted by finance.biggo.com; original source Jensen Huang ; from gnews:595a83074fb8af0237f822ce 2026-09-06] CEO Jensen Huang said NVIDIA's entire supply chain was challenged and running flat out.\\n    Quote: \\\"Our entire supply chain is challenged. And everybody is really running flat out,\\\" he said.\\n- e4120 [party_statement; Jensen Huang, quoted by finance.biggo.com; original source Jensen Huang ; from gnews:595a83074fb8af0237f822ce 2026-09-06] Jensen Huang said NVIDIA revenue growth could be a lot higher absent supply constraints.\\n    Quote: Huang added that growth could be \\\"a lot higher\\\" if the company were not supply-constrained.\\n- e4137 [party_statement; finance.biggo.com; original source TSMC ; from gnews:a1001762888510be822dcfd8 2026-09-06] TSMC raised third-quarter revenue guidance to $44.6 billion\\u2013$45.8 billion, nearly 47% above the prior year, with high-performance computing at 66% of quarterly revenue.\\n    Quote: with third-quarter revenue guidance raised to $44.6 billion to $45.8 billion\\u2014up nearly 47% year over year\\u2014and high-performance computing now accounting for 66% of quarterly revenue.\\n- e4348 [third_party_view; fool.com (analyst); original source Analysts ; from gnews:90f3858225bf7e19b8f38f21 2026-09-10] Analysts estimate NVIDIA revenue of $411 billion in FY2027 and $678 billion in FY2028, implying 65% FY2028 growth.\\n    Quote: Analysts currently project $411 billion in revenue for fiscal 2027, followed by a 65% jump to $678 billion in fiscal 2028.\\n- e4377 [fact; fool.com (Sara Appino); original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:be51df202b76715f3d9023f3 2026-09-10] NVIDIA reported FY2026 revenue of approximately $215.9 billion, up 65.5% year over year.\\n    Quote: According to its latest annual report, in the fiscal year ended Jan. 25, 2026, revenue reached approximately $215.9 billion. This represents a 65.5% increase year over year, driven by intense demand for AI chips.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e577; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\n- e4490 [party_statement; Jensen Huang, as quoted by finance.biggo.com; original source Jensen Huang 2026-09-10; from gnews:8e160db6032cc34164f45e59 2026-09-11] Jensen Huang said NVIDIA-supported projects have roughly $100 billion of contracted customer demand behind them.\\n    Quote: Behind those projects, Huang said, sits roughly $100 billion of contracted customer demand.\\n- e4511 [party_statement; finance.biggo.com; original source Jensen Huang 2026-09-10; from gnews:8e160db6032cc34164f45e59 2026-09-11] Jensen Huang acknowledged supply challenges for NVIDIA in packaging, memory, connectors, voltage regulators, and wafers.\\n    Quote: Constraints remain. Huang acknowledged upstream supply challenges in packaging, memory, connectors, voltage regulators, and wafers.\\n- e4512 [party_statement; finance.biggo.com; original source Jensen Huang 2026-09-10; from gnews:8e160db6032cc34164f45e59 2026-09-11] Jensen Huang said land, electricity, and ready-to-use data-center capacity are the bigger downstream bottlenecks for NVIDIA's business.\\n    Quote: Downstream, land, electricity, and ready-to-use data-center capacity are the bigger bottlenecks.\\n- e4513 [party_statement; finance.biggo.com; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:8e160db6032cc34164f45e59 2026-09-11] NVIDIA is working with companies and data-center operators on Australian plans involving 2 gigawatts of capacity for 2027, valued at about $80 billion.\\n    Quote: He pointed to Australia as an example, where Nvidia is working with companies and data-center operators on plans involving 2 gigawatts of capacity for 2027, valued at about $80 billion.\\n- e4609 [party_statement; fool.com (analyst); original source Micron Technology ; from gnews:91a192187338e1131c5b54e1 2026-09-13] Micron plans to double monthly stacked-memory output to roughly 100,000 wafers by the end of 2026.\\n    Quote: The company plans to double its monthly output of stacked memory to roughly 100,000 wafers by the end of this year.\\n- e4613 [party_statement; fool.com (analyst); original source Micron management and SK Hynix CEO Kwak Noh-jung ; from gnews:91a192187338e1131c5b54e1 2026-09-13] Micron management guided that tight supply conditions would persist beyond calendar 2027, and SK Hynix CEO Kwak Noh-jung said the shortage could last through 2030.\\n    Quote: Management guided that tight supply conditions persist beyond calendar 2027, and SK Hynix CEO Kwak Noh-jung has said the shortage could run through 2030.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e3902; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\n- e4634 [fact; finance.yahoo.com; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:7708a5ba7485f4ee381ccc41 2026-09-14] NVIDIA reported an order backlog of more than $2 trillion in its Q2 release.\\n    Quote: as part of its Q2 release, NVIDIA Corporation (NASDAQ:NVDA) outlined that its order backlog was more than $2 trillion.\\n- e4640 [third_party_view; finance.yahoo.com; original source Seaport Global ; from gnews:7708a5ba7485f4ee381ccc41 2026-09-14] Seaport Global argued that NVIDIA was sold out of capacity and might struggle to produce further upside surprises.\\n    Quote: some, such as those from Seaport Global, have argued that as NVIDIA Corporation (NASDAQ:NVDA) is sold out of capacity, it might find it difficult to generate capacity for additional upside surprises.\\n- e4680 [party_statement; Stephen Guilfoyle, TheStreet; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:2fc71ee9730f9420d6d130bd 2026-09-14] NVIDIA guided current-quarter revenue to $108.0 billion, plus or minus 2%, versus consensus of $104.6 billion.\\n    Quote: For the current quarter, CEO Jensen Huang\\u2019s firm projected revenue of $108.0 billion (+/-2%) vs. consensus for $104.6 billion. That would be good for growth of roughly 90% and Nvidia Is known for beating its guidance.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e3218; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\n- e4702 [third_party_view; Zacks.com; original source Zacks.com 2026-09-14; from gnews:1d3bc1ba4c2df5e998884bdb 2026-09-14] Zacks consensus estimates NVIDIA FY2027 total revenue growth of 87.4% year over year and EPS growth of 93.5%.\\n    Quote: The Zacks Consensus Estimate for NVDA\\u2019s current fiscal 2027 revenues and EPS indicates a year-over-year surge of 87.4% and 93.5%, respectively.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read it as a later version of e751 (2026-07-22); both are in force: Zacks consensus estimates NVIDIA FY2027 revenue growth of 80% year over year.\\n- e4704 [fact; TradingView; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:3da38213d30cedb4fc122748 2026-09-14] NVIDIA reported that three direct customers accounted for 44% ($78.2 billion) of its $177.8 billion revenue in the first half of FY2027, versus two customers accounting for 35% a year earlier.\\n    Quote: Three direct customers generated 44% ($78.2 billion) of Nvidia\\u2019s $177.8 billion revenue in the first half of fiscal 2027\\u2014up from two customers driving 35% a year earlier.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e2622; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\n- e4761 [third_party_view; Manali Pradhan, CFA; original source Manali Pradhan, CFA 2026-09-15; from gnews:9fd93b942948c5002e13eb0b 2026-09-15] Manali Pradhan forecast NVIDIA fiscal Q3 2027 revenue of around $113 billion to $114 billion.\\n    Quote: However, I think Nvidia could report third-quarter revenue of around $113 billion to $114 billion.\\n- e4762 [third_party_view; Manali Pradhan, CFA; original source Manali Pradhan, CFA 2026-09-15; from gnews:9fd93b942948c5002e13eb0b 2026-09-15] Manali Pradhan said NVIDIA exceeded the high end of revenue guidance in each of the past 12 quarters, averaging 3.1% above the high end over the past four quarters.\\n    Quote: Nvidia has exceeded the high end of its revenue guidance in each of the past 12 quarters. Over the past four quarters, actual revenue has averaged 3.1% above the high end of guidance.\\n- e4769 [party_statement; fool.com (analyst); original source NVIDIA management ; from gnews:9fd93b942948c5002e13eb0b 2026-09-15] NVIDIA management expects supply to remain constrained through FY2028 and said higher memory prices are adding pressure.\\n    Quote: Management expects supply to remain constrained through fiscal 2028, while higher memory prices are also adding pressure.\\n- e4772 [party_statement; fool.com (analyst); original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:9fd93b942948c5002e13eb0b 2026-09-15] NVIDIA's fiscal Q3 2027 revenue guidance assumes zero Data Center compute revenue from China.\\n    Quote: Nvidia's third-quarter revenue guidance also assumes no Data Center compute revenue from China.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e2349; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\n- e4773 [fact; NVIDIA Corporation; original source University of Manchester ; from nvblog:uk-air-pollution-research-earth-2 2026-09-16] University of Manchester professor David Topping applied NVIDIA\\u2019s Earth-2 models and tools to explore air-pollution forecasting.\\n    Quote: David Topping, a professor in the University of Manchester\\u2019s department of Earth and environmental science, saw that the NVIDIA Earth-2 family of open AI models and tools had cracked a related problem for weather forecasting \\u2014 and asked whether the same generative frameworks could work for pollution fields.\\n- e4774 [fact; NVIDIA Corporation; original source University of Manchester ; from nvblog:uk-air-pollution-research-earth-2 2026-09-16] University of Manchester researchers worked with NVIDIA\\u2019s Earth-2 team and trained Earth-2 CorrDiff for air-pollution modelling on the Isambard-AI supercomputer.\\n    Quote: Working with the NVIDIA Earth-2 team, Topping and colleagues generated training data from existing chemistry-climate simulations, then trained Earth-2 CorrDiff \\u2014 a generative downscaling model \\u2014 on Isambard-AI, the U.K.\\u2019s national AI supercomputer in Bristol.\\n- e4775 [fact; NVIDIA Corporation; original source University of Manchester ; from nvblog:uk-air-pollution-research-earth-2 2026-09-16] The University of Manchester team added Earth-2 StormCast to its pollution workflow and demonstrated its test-training and inference workflows running on NVIDIA DGX Spark.\\n    Quote: The team has since added Earth-2 StormCast, a model that enables time-dependent forecasts that directly use air quality observations, and showed the test-training and inference workflows running on the NVIDIA DGX Spark personal AI supercomputer.\\n- e4776 [fact; NVIDIA Corporation; original source University of Manchester ; from nvblog:uk-air-pollution-research-earth-2 2026-09-16] The University of Manchester\\u2019s generative pollution workflow runs on NVIDIA DGX Spark for inference and smaller training runs.\\n    Quote: The same generative pollution workflow also runs on the NVIDIA GB10 Grace Blackwell superchip-powered DGX Spark desktop AI system for inference and smaller training runs.\\n- e4777 [fact; NVIDIA Corporation; original source Emerald AI, Google and NVIDIA 2026-09-16; from nvblog:ai-energy-management-alliance 2026-09-16] Emerald AI, Google and NVIDIA launched the AI Energy Management Alliance to advance data centers that adjust electricity use in response to grid conditions.\\n    Quote: Today, Emerald AI, Google and NVIDIA announced the launch of the AI Energy Management Alliance (AEMA), a first-of-its-kind coalition advancing data centers that can dynamically manage their electricity use in response to grid conditions.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e4813; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\n- e4782 [fact; finance.yahoo.com author; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:3