nt forecast fiscal Q3 2027 revenue of $108.0 billion.\\n    Quote: Management's forecast for the fiscal third quarter, now underway, is $108.0 billion of revenue -- and growth like that is ultimately a claim about what customers keep spending.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e4260; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\n- e4807 [fact; Zacks.com; original source NVIDIA 2026-08-26; from gnews:bc6926bf31d3a4d8006dce46 2026-09-16] NVIDIA reported total revenue of $96.2 billion in fiscal Q2 2027, up 106% year over year and 18% quarter over quarter.\\n    Quote: The company's consolidated revenues reached $96.2 billion, up 106% year over year and 18% quarter over quarter.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e4711; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\n- e4808 [party_statement; Zacks.com; original source NVIDIA management 2026-08-26; from gnews:bc6926bf31d3a4d8006dce46 2026-09-16] NVIDIA management projected fiscal Q3 2027 revenue of about $108 billion, plus or minus 2%, up 12% sequentially at the midpoint.\\n    Quote: Management projects revenues of around $108 billion, plus or minus 2%, for the fiscal third quarter of 2027, up 12% sequentially at the midpoint.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e4714; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\n- e4812 [third_party_view; John Bromels, The Motley Fool; original source John Bromels 2026-09-16; from gnews:ea516c504dd7e1c928df6d60 2026-09-16] The author calculated that NVIDIA revenue grew 1,150% and net income grew 2,250% over the five years preceding publication.\\n    Quote: Over the last five years, Nvidia's revenue has grown 1,150%, and its net income has soared 2,250%.\\n- e4813 [fact; gurufocus.com (analyst); original source NVIDIA, Google, and Emerald AI ; from gnews:d9a8cf969d7dedc50100397a 2026-09-16] NVIDIA launched the AI Energy Management Alliance with Google and Emerald AI to address electricity constraints on AI infrastructure deployment.\\n    Quote: Nvidia ( NASDAQ:NVDA ), the AI-accelerator and data-center platform leader, launched the AI Energy Management Alliance with Google and Emerald AI on Wednesday, putting one of AI's biggest physical bottleneckselectricitysquarely in its sights.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e4777; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\n- e4824 [fact; Reuters; original source Snap 2026-09-16; from gnews:8e136e16e38f8f20c9c93478 2026-09-16] Snap announced that NVIDIA will power AI in its Specs augmented-reality glasses, enabling them to interpret workers\\u2019 visual environments and retrieve company data.\\n    Quote: Nvidia will power the AI, enabling Specs to interpret a worker's visual environment and retrieve relevant company data\\n- e4832 [third_party_view; trefis.com; original source trefis.com 2026-09-16; from gnews:106a61a1ef10fb3ba6adb1cd 2026-09-16] NVIDIA\\u2019s trailing-twelve-month revenue was $302.97 billion, up 83.4% year over year.\\n    Quote: Revenue over the trailing twelve months is $302.97 billion, up 83.4% from a year earlier.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e4260; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\n- e4833 [third_party_view; trefis.com; original source trefis.com 2026-09-16; from gnews:106a61a1ef10fb3ba6adb1cd 2026-09-16] The author calculated that NVIDIA\\u2019s trailing-twelve-month revenue growth of 83.4% was below its 116.5% average growth over the prior three years.\\n    Quote: That is slower than the 116.5% the company averaged over the past three years\\n- e4837 [party_statement; Jensen Huang, quoted by finance.yahoo.com; original source Jensen Huang, NVIDIA CEO ; from gnews:8593bc8819641cdd48950c75 2026-09-16] NVIDIA CEO Jensen Huang said AI compute demand was accelerating, with multiple frontier labs scaling in parallel and strong momentum across the U.S. and worldwide.\\n    Quote: And demand is accelerating. This time last year, one lab alone was driving the buildout; today, we have a golden age of new AI labs and startups, multiple frontier labs scaling in parallel, a thriving open-model ecosystem and physical AI coming online \\u2014 with strong momentum across the U.S. and around the world.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e2917; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\n- e4851 [fact; CNBC; original source Snap ; from gnews:28eafda87919cbcc2d744118 2026-09-16] Snap is partnering with NVIDIA, AWS and Salesforce in an enterprise sales push for its $2,000 Specs AR glasses.\\n    Quote: Snap is partnering with Nvidia, Amazon Web Services and Salesforce as part of an enterprise sales push centered on its $2,000 Specs augmented reality glasses.\\n- e4861 [fact; fool.com author; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:ea4633ed3e4ad9d71383673f 2026-09-17] NVIDIA revenue increased 106% year over year in the prior quarter; the quarter is not specified.\\n    Quote: revenue increased by 106% year over year last quarter\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e3350; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\n- e4893 [fact; unite.ai; original source Delta Electronics 2026-09-17; from gnews:ddb3b7ef7be1a22d75d64428 2026-09-17] Delta Electronics announced on September 17, 2026, integrated power and cooling infrastructure intended to speed deployment of AI factories based on NVIDIA DSX.\\n    Quote: Delta Electronics on September 17, 2026, announced integrated energy-to-compute power and cooling infrastructure intended to speed deployment of AI factories based on NVIDIA DSX , pairing 800 VDC power delivery the company rates at up to 98% conversion efficiency with liquid-cooling systems scaling to 3 MW.\\n- e4897 [fact; fool.com (analyst); original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:824eb11f9b37d2a3489d6e59 2026-09-18] Fool.com\\u2019s analyst reported that NVIDIA\\u2019s second-quarter revenue was $96 billion, up 106% year over year, and Data Center revenue was $89 billion, up 117% year over year; the quarter\\u2019s fiscal year is not specified.\\n    Quote: The company recently reported terrific second-quarter results, with revenue up 106% year over year to $96 billion, and revenue from data centers up 117% to $89 billion.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e4818; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\n- e4898 [fact; crn.com; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:3a284e233d8b31c62dc66b33 2026-09-18] NVIDIA reported revenue of $96.2 billion for the period ended in June, up 106% year over year.\\n    Quote: The company had reported a 106 percent year-over-year increase in revenue to $96.2 billion for the period that ended in June\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e2515; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\n- e4899 [party_statement; crn.com; original source Colette Kress, NVIDIA CFO ; from gnews:3a284e233d8b31c62dc66b33 2026-09-18] NVIDIA CFO Colette Kress said NVIDIA's revenue could double next year absent significant supplier capacity constraints.\\n    Quote: Nvidia CFO Colette Kress said annual revenue could double next year if it wasn\\u2019t for significant supply constraints felt by its suppliers.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e4924; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\n- e4901 [third_party_view; crn.com; original source crn.com 2026-09-18; from gnews:3a284e233d8b31c62dc66b33 2026-09-18] CRN estimated that NVIDIA could leave more than $100 billion of demand for AI infrastructure gear unfulfilled next year because of supply constraints.\\n    Quote: This suggests that Nvidia could leave demand unfulfilled for more than $100 billion in AI infrastructure gear, which includes its GPUs as well as other kinds of chips it designs, such as CPUs and DPUs, that are becoming more pervasive in its systems.\\n- e4902 [third_party_view; crn.com; original source crn.com 2026-09-18; from gnews:3a284e233d8b31c62dc66b33 2026-09-18] CRN reported that AI-system lead times for channel partners had reached as long as a year, system prices were rising quickly, and some partners were bracing for NVIDIA price increases.\\n    Quote: For channel partners, supply constraints have translated into long lead times, sometimes stretching out to as long as a year. This has also caused fast-rising prices for systems, and some partners said they are now bracing for price increases from Nvidia itself.\\n- e4903 [third_party_view; Richard Rudometkin, vice president of global sales at International Computer Concepts, quoted by crn.com; original source Richard Rudometkin, vice president of global sales at International Computer Concepts ; from gnews:3a284e233d8b31c62dc66b33 2026-09-18] International Computer Concepts' Richard Rudometkin said Dell, MSI, or other vendors quoted 12\\u201316-week delivery times for some systems, while Supermicro offered shipment two weeks from Friday.\\n    Quote: if we have a project and we go to Dell or we go to MSI or [someone else], they\\u2019re telling us 12 to 16 weeks, and Supermicro is saying, \\u2018I can ship two weeks from Friday,\\u2019\\n- e4911 [fact; The Motley Fool author; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:a7b0dfa6b48b220718e5096c 2026-09-18] NVIDIA revenue grew 106% year over year in the second quarter.\\n    Quote: The company grew revenue 106% year over year in the second quarter\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e4635; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\n- e4914 [fact; fool.com (analyst); original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:12a943c49b0c41542e6110b5 2026-09-18] NVIDIA reported total revenue of $96.2 billion for the quarter ended July 26, 2026, up 18% quarter over quarter and 106% year over year.\\n    Quote: For the quarter ended July 26, 2026, Nvidia reported total revenue of $96.2 billion, up 18% from the prior quarter and 106% from a year ago.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e2497; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\n- e4918 [party_statement; finance.yahoo.com; original source NVIDIA CEO Jensen Huang ; from gnews:3337ca32305f307a1439d775 2026-09-18] NVIDIA CEO Jensen Huang said the company expects to sell twice as many chips next year; the comparison baseline and exact period are not specified.\\n    Quote: CEO Jensen Huang talking about selling twice as many chips next year\\n- e4941 [party_statement; benzinga.com; original source Jensen Huang ; from gnews:7218ec5f13c26358ef736b14 2026-09-18] Jensen Huang said the rate of AI token generation increased 25-fold in less than a year.\\n    Quote: Huang said the rate of token generation has increased 25-fold in less than a year.\\n- e4942 [party_statement; benzinga.com; original source Jensen Huang ; from gnews:7218ec5f13c26358ef736b14 2026-09-18] Jensen Huang said open models account for nearly 70% of generated tokens, up from about 30%.\\n    Quote: Open models now account for nearly 70% of generated tokens, up from about 30%.\\n- e4943 [party_statement; benzinga.com; original source Jensen Huang ; from gnews:7218ec5f13c26358ef736b14 2026-09-18] Jensen Huang expects AI testing to become a third major category of infrastructure alongside training and inference.\\n    Quote: In fact, Huang expects testing to become a third major category of AI infrastructure alongside training and inference.\\n- e4944 [party_statement; benzinga.com; original source Jensen Huang ; from gnews:7218ec5f13c26358ef736b14 2026-09-18] Jensen Huang said large AI testing environments will require additional data centers and create another source of compute demand.\\n    Quote: He said large testing environments will require additional data centers, creating another source of compute demand.\\n- e4945 [party_statement; benzinga.com; original source Jensen Huang ; from gnews:7218ec5f13c26358ef736b14 2026-09-18] Jensen Huang said NVIDIA Grace Blackwell systems now rent for about $16 per GPU hour, compared with roughly $5 under some contracts signed a year earlier.\\n    Quote: He said NVIDIA Grace Blackwell systems can now rent for about $16 per GPU hour, compared with roughly $5 under some contracts signed a year ago.\\n- e4946 [party_statement; benzinga.com; original source Jensen Huang ; from gnews:7218ec5f13c26358ef736b14 2026-09-18] Jensen Huang said cloud providers are raising prices as older contracts expire, boosting revenue forecasts and investing in more infrastructure.\\n    Quote: As older contracts expire, cloud providers are raising prices, boosting revenue forecasts and investing in more infrastructure, Huang said.\\n- e4954 [third_party_view; CRN; original source Gartner ; from gnews:35efa49dae24bb21af438112 2026-09-18] Gartner expects neoclouds to account for 20% of the $267 billion AI cloud market by 2030.\\n    Quote: According to research firm Gartner, neoclouds are expected to represent 20 percent of the $267 billion AI cloud market by 2030, underlining their competitiveness against hyperscalers.\\n- e4958 [third_party_view; CRN, quoting GDT executive Chris Kapusta; original source Chris Kapusta, GDT ; from gnews:35efa49dae24bb21af438112 2026-09-18] GDT executive Chris Kapusta said some neoclouds have demand for AI infrastructure but struggle to secure workable financing.\\n    Quote: \\u201cWhere a number of them struggle out of the gate is really on getting the financing and getting the financing to work. So the demand\\u2019s there, the desire\\u2019s there. It usually comes down to the numbers and how the financing works,\\u201d he said.\\n- e4959 [fact; Channel Insider; original source Huawei ; from gnews:7d83454ace7462ccdd8aaeb9 2026-09-18] Huawei unveiled its Atlas 960E SuperPoD AI infrastructure system.\\n    Quote: The AI giant unveiled the Atlas 960E SuperPoD\\n- e4960 [party_statement; Channel Insider, citing Huawei; original source Huawei ; from gnews:7d83454ace7462ccdd8aaeb9 2026-09-18] Huawei moved the planned Ascend 960DT launch to Q1 2027, three quarters earlier than originally scheduled.\\n    Quote: The Ascend 960DT now scheduled for the first quarter of 2027, three quarters earlier than originally planned.\\n- e4961 [party_statement; Channel Insider, citing Huawei; original source Huawei ; from gnews:7d83454ace7462ccdd8aaeb9 2026-09-18] Huawei said its SuperCluster can support up to 512,000 NPUs, with a future multi-rail topology potentially scaling to 1 million NPUs.\\n    Quote: Huawei said multiple SuperPoDs can be connected into a SuperCluster supporting up to 512,000 NPUs, while a multi-rail topology could eventually extend that architecture to 1 million NPUs.\\n- e4962 [third_party_view; Channel Insider, citing Reuters; original source Reuters ; from gnews:7d83454ace7462ccdd8aaeb9 2026-09-18] Reuters reported that Huawei cannot currently produce enough AI computing equipment to meet demand in China.\\n    Quote: Reuters reported that Huawei is already struggling to produce enough AI computing equipment to satisfy demand in China.\\n- e4963 [party_statement; Channel Insider, citing Reuters and Eric Xu; original source Eric Xu ; from gnews:7d83454ace7462ccdd8aaeb9 2026-09-18] Huawei rotating chairman Eric Xu said Huawei has no current plans for large-scale overseas expansion, citing production constraints.\\n    Quote: Rotating chairman Eric Xu said the company therefore has no plans for a large-scale overseas expansion for now.\\n- e4964 [party_statement; Channel Insider, citing Huawei; original source Huawei ; from gnews:7d83454ace7462ccdd8aaeb9 2026-09-18] Huawei said its CANN software platform has more than 5,200 monthly active developers.\\n    Quote: The company said CANN has moved to sustained, community-driven open-source development and now has more than 5,200 monthly active developers.\\n- e4965 [party_statement; Channel Insider, citing Huawei; original source Huawei ; from gnews:7d83454ace7462ccdd8aaeb9 2026-09-18] Huawei said Ascend supports more than 90 third-party open-source projects, including PyTorch, Triton, vLLM, and veRL.\\n    Quote: Huawei also highlighted that Ascend supports more than 90 third-party open-source projects, including PyTorch, Triton, vLLM, and veRL.\\n- e4966 [party_statement; Channel Insider, citing Huawei; original source Huawei ; from gnews:7d83454ace7462ccdd8aaeb9 2026-09-18] Huawei said more than 40 models have been natively pretrained on Ascend and CANN.\\n    Quote: More than 40 models have been natively pretrained on Ascend and CANN.\\n- e4967 [rumour; Channel Insider; original source Channel Insider ; from gnews:7d83454ace7462ccdd8aaeb9 2026-09-18] DeepSeek reportedly plans to deploy 160,000 Huawei AI chips at a data center in Inner Mongolia.\\n    Quote: DeepSeek reportedly plans to deploy 160,000 Huawei AI chips at a data center in Inner Mongolia\\n- e4997 [third_party_view; fool.com (analyst); original source Silicon Analysts ; from gnews:ad94c78d09fe41fc3f29bbca 2026-09-18] Silicon Analysts estimated NVIDIA\\u2019s share of the AI accelerator market at 80%.\\n    Quote: Nvidia controls an estimated 80% of the AI accelerator market, according to semiconductor industry tracker Silicon Analysts.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e3628; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\n- e5001 [fact; Zacks.com (analyst); original source NVIDIA 2026-08-26; from gnews:57a69374b8fa083ce36ecfb1 2026-09-18] NVIDIA reported FY2027 Q2 total revenue of $96.2 billion, up 106% year over year and 18% sequentially.\\n    Quote: According to NVIDIA\\u2019s Aug. 26 press release, the company\\u2019s total revenues reached $96.2 billion in the fiscal second quarter of 2027, up 106% year over year and 18% sequentially.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e4626; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\n- e5004 [party_statement; Zacks.com (analyst); original source NVIDIA 2026-08-26; from gnews:57a69374b8fa083ce36ecfb1 2026-09-18] NVIDIA guided FY2027 Q3 total revenue to $108 billion, plus or minus 2%, approximately 12% above FY2027 Q2 at the midpoint.\\n    Quote: Looking ahead, NVIDIA expects profitability to remain strong and projects revenues to reach $108 billion, plus or minus 2%, in the fiscal third quarter of 2027, up 12% sequentially from the midpoint.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e4714; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\n- e5010 [third_party_view; Luke Lango, InvestorPlace; original source Ali Ghodsi, Databricks CEO ; from gnews:9c06db5aed9ec725f7aa9a81 2026-09-19] Databricks CEO Ali Ghodsi said that two agent systems using the same model can produce bills that differ substantially, with the wrong setup making a task cost roughly twice as much.\\n    Quote: As Databricks CEO Ali Ghodsi explained to TechCrunch , two agent systems built around the same model can produce dramatically different bills. Choose the wrong setup, and the same task may cost roughly twice as much to complete.\\n- e5013 [third_party_view; barchart.com (analyst); original source Cohere ; from gnews:2052184744bec4b89ecab744 2026-09-19] Cohere's annual recurring revenue nearly quadrupled to $240 million in 2025 from $62 million in 2024.\\n    Quote: Annual recurring revenue nearly quadrupled to $240 million in 2025, up from $62 million a year earlier.\\n- e5015 [third_party_view; barchart.com (analyst); original source barchart.com (analyst) 2026-09-19; from gnews:2052184744bec4b89ecab744 2026-09-19] The author calculated NVIDIA's forward GAAP P/E at 21.96x versus a five-year average of 52.15x, and forward P/S at 12.82x versus 19.79x.\\n    Quote: The forward GAAP price-to-earnings (P/E) of 21.96x sits nearly 58% below its 5-year average of 52.15x. Similarly, the forward price-to-sales (P/S) ratio of 12.82x is roughly 35% below its 5-year average of 19.79x.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e1384; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\n- e5016 [third_party_view; barchart.com (analyst); original source Analysts ; from gnews:2052184744bec4b89ecab744 2026-09-19] Analysts expect NVIDIA earnings growth of 95% in 2027, 67% in 2028, 34% in 2029, and 12% in 2030.\\n    Quote: Analysts expect earnings to grow 95% in 2027, 67% in 2028, 34% in 2029, and 12% in 2030.\\n- e5018 [fact; barchart.com (analyst); original source NVIDIA 2026-08-27; from gnews:2052184744bec4b89ecab744 2026-09-19] NVIDIA reported record fiscal 2027 second-quarter revenue of $96.2 billion, more than double the year-earlier quarter.\\n    Quote: Revenue for the quarter rose to a record $96.2 billion, more than double year-over-year (YoY).\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e3897; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\n- e5022 [party_statement; barchart.com (analyst); original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:2052184744bec4b89ecab744 2026-09-19] NVIDIA guided fiscal 2027 Q3 revenue to $108 billion, plus or minus 2% ($106 billion to $110 billion).\\n    Quote: Looking forward, Nvidia expects third-quarter revenue of $108 billion, plus or minus 2%, which implies a range of about $106 billion to $110 billion.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e4760; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\n- e5032 [fact; Tom's Guide / Amanda Caswell; original source Perplexity ; from gnews:37da4d37b73df1fca6c28afa 2026-09-19] Perplexity launched Portable Computer, a system combining a local AI model, agent tools, app connectors and a sandboxed runtime for NVIDIA DGX Spark hardware.\\n    Quote: Perplexity just launched Portable Computer , which packages a local AI model, agent tools, app connectors, and a sandboxed runtime into a single system that runs on DGX Spark hardware.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e1598; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\n- e5033 [third_party_view; BGR author Aaron Greenbaum; original source BGR author Aaron Greenbaum 2026-09-19; from gnews:6a6a5fd7a189eadc287c6cfc 2026-09-19] The outlet reported RTX 5090 asking prices had risen from a $1,999 launch price last year to at least $5,000 at the beginning of September 2026, with Newegg listings around $9,000 and some near $14,000 during the week of September 13, 2026.\\n    Quote: Last year, Nvidia's current flagship graphics card, the RTX 5090 , launched at a semi-respectable price of $1,999. Fast forward to the beginning of this month, and the cost of a 5090 had climbed to at least $5,000. As of the week of September 13, 2026, stores such as Newegg are selling RTX 5090s for around $9,000. Some even now have price tags bordering on $14,000 (I think they were updated while \\n- e5034 [rumour; BGR author Aaron Greenbaum, relaying TechRadar; original source TechRadar ; from gnews:6a6a5fd7a189eadc287c6cfc 2026-09-19] The outlet relayed a rumor, attributed to TechRadar's discussion of possible engineered FOMO, that AI server manufacturers were buying GPUs by the pallet, with images circulating; the item says this rumor was being used to justify high RTX 5090 asking prices.\\n    Quote: TechRadar theorizes this could be the result of engineered FOMO. Rumors have been swirling about AI server manufacturers buying GPUs by the pallet, complete with images, which is justification enough to buy an RTX 5090 at whatever price sellers set.\\n- e5056 [third_party_view; supercarblondie.com; original source Wall Street analysts ; from gnews:01edb4d1fa96705133b29207 2026-09-19] Wall Street analysts expect NVIDIA to generate around $411 billion of revenue in FY2027.\\n    Quote: Wall Street analysts expect Nvidia to generate around $411 billion in revenue in fiscal 2027.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e4097; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\n- e5058 [fact; fool.com (Daniel Sparks); original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:5feec912090c2af6467eed38 2026-09-19] NVIDIA reported fiscal Q2 2027 revenue of $96.2 billion, up 106% year over year, including $89 billion of Data Center revenue.\\n    Quote: Nvidia's revenue in the fiscal second quarter of 2027 (ended July 26) rose 106% year over year to $96.2 billion, with $89 billion of that coming from data centers.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e4569; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\n- e5060 [fact; fool.com (Daniel Sparks); original source Broadcom ; from gnews:5feec912090c2af6467eed38 2026-09-19] Broadcom reported fiscal Q3 2026 AI semiconductor revenue of $16.7 billion, up 221% year over year and 54% quarter over quarter; custom accelerators were 73% of that revenue.\\n    Quote: Its AI semiconductor revenue reached $16.7 billion in the fiscal third quarter of 2026 (ended Aug. 2), 221% higher than a year earlier -- and still accelerating, with growth of 54% from the prior quarter alone. Custom accelerators (chips designed with a single customer) made up 73% of it.\\n- e5061 [party_statement; fool.com (Daniel Sparks); original source Broadcom CEO Hock Tan ; from gnews:5feec912090c2af6467eed38 2026-09-19] Broadcom CEO Hock Tan said the company had secured supply to double AI revenue to about $115 billion in FY2027 and $230 billion in FY2028.\\n    Quote: CEO Hock Tan told analysts earlier this month that Broadcom has secured the supply to double AI revenue to about $115 billion in fiscal 2027 -- and to $230 billion the year after.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e4058; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\n- e5062 [fact; fool.com (Daniel Sparks); original source Marvell ; from gnews:5feec912090c2af6467eed38 2026-09-19] Marvell reported fiscal Q2 2027 revenue of $2.7 billion, while Data Center revenue grew 46%.\\n    Quote: Revenue reached $2.7 billion in its fiscal second quarter of 2027 (ended Aug. 1), and data center revenue grew 46%.\\n- e5063 [party_statement; fool.com (Daniel Sparks); original source Marvell CEO Matt Murphy ; from gnews:5feec912090c2af6467eed38 2026-09-19] Marvell CEO Matt Murphy expected FY2028 revenue of about $18 billion, versus around $12 billion in the current fiscal year, with custom-business revenue more than doubling.\\n    Quote: And CEO Matt Murphy now expects about $18 billion of revenue in fiscal 2028, up from around $12 billion this fiscal year, with the custom business more than doubling along the way.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e4700; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\n- e5071 [fact; fool.com (Daniel Sparks); original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:e5b9c11e2c8ef9754946a897 2026-09-20] NVIDIA reported Q2 FY2027 revenue of $96.2 billion, up 106% year over year.\\n    Quote: Capturing how different today's backdrop is, Nvidia grew revenue 106% year over year in the second quarter of fiscal 2027 (a period that ended July 26), reaching $96.2 billion.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e3399; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\n- e5073 [third_party_view; fool.com (Daniel Sparks); original source Daniel Sparks 2026-09-20; from gnews:e5b9c11e2c8ef9754946a897 2026-09-20] NVIDIA's year-over-year revenue growth rate accelerated for four consecutive quarters, from 62% to 73%, 85%, and 106% in Q2 FY2027.\\n    Quote: The company's year-over-year revenue growth rate has now accelerated for four straight quarters, moving from 62% last fall to 73%, then 85%, and now 106%.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e4599; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\n- e5081 [third_party_view; finance.yahoo.com; original source Elon Musk ; from gnews:a3d42b6d7a8a55a22f4a742b 2026-09-20] Elon Musk estimated that space could become the lowest-cost place for AI computing within two to three years, citing solar power and the projected economics of orbital infrastructure.\\n    Quote: He cites solar power availability in orbit as a crucial advantage, and estimates that within two to three years, space might become the lowest-cost place for AI computing in general, describing the orbital architecture as simpler, less expensive, denser, and lighter than a standard data-center rack.\\n- e5082 [third_party_view; finance.yahoo.com; original source Brad Smith ; from gnews:a3d42b6d7a8a55a22f4a742b 2026-09-20] Microsoft President Brad Smith said he would be surprised if companies transferred computation from land to low-Earth orbit.\\n    Quote: Microsoft President Brad Smith has publicly questioned the broader concept, telling reporters that he would be surprised if companies actually transferred computation from land to low-Earth orbit.\\n- e5083 [third_party_view; finance.yahoo.com; original source Unnamed analysts ; from gnews:a3d42b6d7a8a55a22f4a742b 2026-09-20] Some analyst models estimate that SpaceX accounts for approximately 5% of NVIDIA revenue; the period is unspecified.\\n    Quote: According to some analyst models, SpaceX accounts for approximately 5% of NVIDIA's revenue.\\n- e74 [fact; tradingview.com; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:25d0b1d2a9dfe0bb99432e1a 2026-07-06] NVIDIA\\u2019s Data Center segment generated $75.25 billion in revenue in FY2027 Q1, equal to 92% of total sales, up 92% year over year and 21% sequentially.\\n    Quote: During the first quarter of fiscal 2027, the Data Center segment generated $75.25 billion in revenues, accounting for 92% of total sales. Revenues from the segment surged 92% year over year and grew 21% sequentially, driven by the rapid ramp-up of Blackwell 300 systems and robust networking demand.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e122, e169, e278, e602, e680, e771, e1708, e1716, e1790; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\n- e109 [third_party_view; finance.yahoo.com; original source Amazon and Alphabet ; from gnews:ce5daf57bdca5da657e5f677 2026-07-07] Amazon and Alphabet are extending access to their in-house AI processors, adding competition for NVIDIA\\u2019s AI computing products.\\n    Quote: The move comes as the company faces rising competition from specialized AI chips from cloud providers, including Amazon and Alphabet, which are extending access to in-house processors.\\n- e127 [third_party_view; mlq.ai; original source Industry surveys ; from gnews:9f430c6ce2e8d551fe1f063a 2026-07-07] Industry surveys indicate Chinese firms plan to allocate 46% of their AI-accelerator budgets to domestic suppliers within 12 months, versus roughly 30% currently, potentially reducing demand for NVIDIA accelerators in China.\\n    Quote: Chinese companies are nevertheless accelerating domestic chip adoption. Industry surveys indicate Chinese firms plan to shift 46% of their AI-accelerator budgets to domestic suppliers within 12 months, up from roughly 30% today [5].\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e153; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\n- e153 [third_party_view; Bloomberg, reporting the Bloomberg Intelligence survey; original source Bloomberg Intelligence survey respondents 2026-07-07; from gnews:f3ba15f5e14b15ee61d7fddc 2026-07-08] Chinese company executives surveyed by Bloomberg Intelligence said they plan to allocate 46% of their AI-accelerator budgets to domestic products over the next 12 months, up from 30% currently.\\n    Quote: Executives in the country say they\\u2019ll allocate 46% of their budget for artificial intelligence accelerators to domestic products over the next 12 months, up from 30% today, according to a Bloomberg Intelligence survey released on Tuesday.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e127; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\n- e636 [party_statement; AMD told CNBC; original source AMD ; from gnews:b79717064762299fc9426a13 2026-07-20] AMD said it plans to book tens of billions of dollars in data-center AI revenue starting in 2027, with most of it from Helios.\\n    Quote: AMD told CNBC that it plans to book tens of billions in data center AI revenue starting in 2027, the majority coming from Helios.\\n- e976 [third_party_view; fool.com author Lyle Daly; original source SemiAnalysis ; from gnews:bdd09874d53aef7b27866d44 2026-07-26] SemiAnalysis forecast that NVIDIA Data Center revenue in the second half of FY2027 would exceed analyst estimates by 20%.\\n    Quote: And even though SemiAnalysis reported the delays, it's still bullish on Nvidia, forecasting that the chipmaker's data center revenue will exceed analyst estimates by 20% in the second half of its fiscal 2027.\\n- e2115 [third_party_view; Morningstar; original source Morningstar 2026-08-19; from gnews:7ce47efd62fa17b9aa29e258 2026-08-19] Morningstar estimates NVIDIA Data Center revenue will exceed $300 billion in FY2027 and perhaps $500 billion in FY2028.\\n    Quote: Nvidia should generate well over $300 billion of data center revenue in calendar 2026, which is effectively fiscal 2027, and perhaps over $500 billion in fiscal 2028.\\n- e2471 [third_party_view; CNBC's Jim Cramer; original source Jim Cramer 2026-08-25; from gnews:1218d24ec31f2081cea0f597 2026-08-25] Jim Cramer said high-bandwidth memory shortages are costing NVIDIA sales; no period or amount was specified.\\n    Quote: shortages of high-bandwidth memory that are costing the company sales\\n- e2510 [party_statement; NVIDIA Corporation; original source Amazon Web Services 2026-08-26; from nvidianews:aws-and-nvidia-to-deliver-2-million-additional-gpus-and-next-generation-infrastructure-for-agentic-and-physical-ai 2026-08-26] AWS plans to deploy 2 million additional NVIDIA Blackwell Ultra, Rubin and Rubin Ultra GPUs across its global infrastructure in 2027\\u20132028.\\n    Quote: AWS plans to deploy an additional 2 million NVIDIA Blackwell Ultra, Rubin and Rubin Ultra GPUs in 2027-2028 across AWS Global Infrastructure, including AI factories.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e2536, e2839; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\n- e2517 [fact; NVIDIA; original source NVIDIA 2026-08-26; from extra:2799d8731e89b90c9bd3f108 2026-08-26] NVIDIA reported Q2 FY2027 Data Center revenue of $89.0 billion, up 117% year over year.\\n    Quote: Data Center revenue of $89.0 billion, up 117% from a year ago\\n- e2541 [party_statement; Colette Kress; original source NVIDIA 2026-08-26; from truenorth:transcript:NVDA:2026-08-26 2026-08-26] NVIDIA began production shipments of Vera Rubin in August 2026 and said it had purchase orders from every major hyperscaler, AI cloud, and system OEM.\\n    Quote: We commenced production shipments of Vera Rubin earlier this month, having already received purchase orders from every major hyperscaler, AI cloud and system OEM, we expect Vera Rubin to mark the fastest product ramp in NVIDIA's history.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e2631, e2731, e2793, e3246, e3387; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read it as a later version of e503 (2026-07-16); both are in force: Tom's Hardware reported that Rubin racks were expected to reach volume production in the second half of 2026; NVIDIA said the Noetra facility would support trillion-parameter model training as it expands, suggesting a phased ramp.\\n- e2562 [party_statement; Colette Kress; original source NVIDIA 2026-08-26; from truenorth:transcript:NVDA:2026-08-26 2026-08-26] NVIDIA's forward outlook included no China Data Center compute revenue.\\n    Quote: And given ongoing geopolitical uncertainty, there is no China data center compute revenue in our forward outlook.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e2349, e3676; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\n- e2567 [party_statement; Colette Kress; original source NVIDIA 2026-08-26; from truenorth:transcript:NVDA:2026-08-26 2026-08-26] NVIDIA expected Vera Rubin to account for approximately 20% of Q3 FY2027 Data Center revenue.\\n    Quote: We see Vera Rubin accounting for about 20% of data center revenue in Q3.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e2732, e3500, e3974; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\n- e2572 [party_statement; Jensen Huang; original source NVIDIA 2026-08-26; from truenorth:transcript:NVDA:2026-08-26 2026-08-26] NVIDIA said its available supply supported approximately 70% of expected FY2028 growth, while demand was substantially higher.\\n    Quote: we have supply for 70%. We have more supply than 70%, but about 70%. Our demand is much higher than that.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e2696, e2739, e3526; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\n- e2574 [fact; NVIDIA Corporation; original source NVIDIA Corporation 2026-08-26; from edgar:NVDA:0001045810-26-000073:q2fy27cfocommentary.htm 2026-08-26] NVIDIA reported second-quarter FY2027 Data Center revenue of $89.0 billion, up 117% year over year and 18% sequentially, driven by the Blackwell Ultra ramp.\\n    Quote: Data Center revenue for the second quarter was a record $89.0 billion, up 117% from a year ago and up 18% sequentially, driven by the ramp of our Blackwell Ultra infrastructure.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e2608; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\n- e2844 [party_statement; techcrunch.com; original source Amazon ; from gnews:d949d26fe875780037064b8a 2026-08-26] Amazon reported that its custom-chip business exceeded a $25 billion annualized revenue run rate, driven by $225 billion in total commitments from AI labs including Anthropic and OpenAI.\\n    Quote: Amazon has said its custom chip business is growing, noting on its last earnings call that it crossed a $25 billion annualized revenue run rate, driven by $225 billion in total commitments from AI labs like Anthropic and OpenAI.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e4323, e4324; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\n- e2848 [party_statement; techcrunch.com; original source NVIDIA 2026-08-26; from gnews:d949d26fe875780037064b8a 2026-08-26] NVIDIA guided to third-quarter revenue of $108 billion, with some revenue expected from Rubin GPUs.\\n    Quote: Nvidia said it expects revenue to reach $108 billion in the third quarter, some of which will come from its next-gen Rubin GPUs.\\n- e3216 [third_party_view; fool.com (Daniel Sparks); original source fool.com (Daniel Sparks) 2026-08-28; from gnews:387b486b6e29491b9c8506df 2026-08-28] NVIDIA Data Center revenue rose from 87.9% of total revenue in FY2026 Q2 to 92.5% in FY2027 Q2, increasing each quarter.\\n    Quote: A year ago, in the second quarter of fiscal 2026, data center revenue was 87.9% of Nvidia's total. The share rose to 89.8% the next quarter, then 91.5%, then 92.2%, then 92.5% in the quarter just reported.\\n- e3219 [third_party_view; fool.com (Daniel Sparks); original source fool.com (Daniel Sparks) 2026-08-28; from gnews:387b486b6e29491b9c8506df 2026-08-28] Daniel Sparks calculated that FY2027 Q3 Data Center revenue would be $99.9 billion if its share of total revenue stayed at FY2027 Q2's 92.5%.\\n    Quote: Hold the data center mix at last quarter's 92.5%, and data center revenue works out to $99.9 billion -- about $100 million short of the line.\\n- e3222 [party_statement; fool.com (Daniel Sparks); original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:387b486b6e29491b9c8506df 2026-08-28] NVIDIA said hyperscale-business growth should reaccelerate in FY2027 Q4 as Vera Rubin supply builds.\\n    Quote: And the company said growth in its hyperscale business (sales to the giant cloud computing providers and the biggest consumer internet companies) should reaccelerate in the fiscal fourth quarter as Vera Rubin supply builds.\\n- e3234 [party_statement; Andy Jassy, quoted by fool.com; original source Andy Jassy ; from gnews:6eec748064565c1339694577 2026-08-28] Amazon CEO Andy Jassy said Amazon would lack capacity to meet all demand in 2026 and expected that constraint to continue in 2027; he said demand already visible for 2028 was striking.\\n    Quote: \\u201cEven at that amount, we will still not have enough capacity to meet all the demand we have in 2026, and I believe this dynamic will also be true in 2027, too,\\u201d Jassy said on the call. \\u201cIn fact, the demand we already have for 2028 is striking.\\u201d\\n- e3805 [third_party_view; theguardian.com; original source theguardian.com 2026-09-03; from gnews:774c4b3a90a519fc0d3c9024 2026-09-03] The Guardian reported that Meta, OpenAI, and Microsoft are developing their own AI chips to reduce reliance on NVIDIA processors, and said this could contribute to slower demand for NVIDIA chips.\\n    Quote: For Nvidia, building up its open source business may help it cushion a demand slowdown from customers such as \\u2060Meta, OpenAI and Microsoft, which are developing their own AI chips to cut reliance \\u200bon its costly and \\u200bsupply-constrained processors.\\n- e3975 [third_party_view; fool.com (Adam Spatacco); original source Adam Spatacco 2026-09-04; from gnews:bbd72d5fbff98d39746e6cb9 2026-09-04] The author estimated that Vera Rubin could generate close to $20 billion in sales in its first real quarter of shipments.\\n    Quote: Considering that Nvidia's data center segment makes up more than 90% of the company's total revenue, it's reasonable to forecast Vera Rubin being on track for something close to $20 billion of sales in its first real quarter of shipments.\\n- e4052 [party_statement; calcalistech.com; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:478c25b436f87e8f421d54ed 2026-09-06] NVIDIA forecast most FY2027 Q3 data-center growth to come from ACIE, with hyperscale growth accelerating in Q4 and through FY2028 as Vera Rubin supply expands.\\n    Quote: According to Nvidia\\u2019s forecast, most of the growth in the third quarter is expected to come from ACIE, while growth in hyperscale is expected to accelerate again in the fourth quarter and throughout fiscal 2028 as the supply of the Vera Rubin platform expands.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e4765; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\n- e4185 [party_statement; finance.yahoo.com; original source Broadcom ; from gnews:91e29a08de15b30c95cb66ac 2026-09-07] Broadcom raised its forecast for AI chip revenue in the fiscal year ending October 2027 to about $115 billion, from a prior forecast of over $100 billion.\\n    Quote: it now expects AI chip revenue of about $115 billion in the fiscal year ending October 2027, up from a prior forecast of over $100 billion.\\n- e4250 [party_statement; Michael Intrator, quoted by Yahoo Finance; original source Michael Intrator, CoreWeave CEO ; from gnews:f22b97377c3d9832608a0fc8 2026-09-09] CoreWeave CEO Michael Intrator said the company was struggling to meet demand for GPUs and could sell each GPU it had to multiple clients.\\n    Quote: \\\"We are struggling to meet demand every day,\\\" CoreWeave CEO Michael Intrator told Yahoo Finance from the Goldman Sachs Communacopia & Tech Conference (video above). \\\"Every GPU we have could be sold to multiple different clients. It is a unique moment, and it continues to be.\\\"\\n- e4254 [party_statement; Yahoo Finance; original source CoreWeave management ; from gnews:f22b97377c3d9832608a0fc8 2026-09-09] CoreWeave management raised its 2026 total revenue guidance to $12.4 billion\\u2013$13.2 billion, citing enterprise GPU-compute demand and a $104 billion total revenue backlog.\\n    Quote: Driven by explosive enterprise demand for graphics processing unit (GPU) compute and a massive $104 billion total revenue backlog, management raised its full-year 2026 revenue guidance to a range of $12.4 billion to $13.2 billion.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e1764; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\n- e4311 [party_statement; Jensen Huang; original source Jensen Huang 2026-09-10; from gnews:ab2afd5299068837dcf8eae0 2026-09-10] Jensen Huang said orders for NVIDIA\\u2019s system combining 36 Grace CPUs with 72 Blackwell GPUs were growing 27% month over month.\\n    Quote: He added that orders for just one product, a computer system that combines 36 Grace CPUs with 72 Blackwell GPUs, is currently experiencing 27% month-to-month sales growth.\\n- e4330 [party_statement; Benzinga, reporting Oracle CEO Clay Magouyrk's fiscal 2027 first-quarter earnings-call remarks; original source Clay Magouyrk, Oracle CEO ; from gnews:44f4bd6cc91ff33688f1e69f 2026-09-10] Oracle CEO Clay Magouyrk said Oracle had delivered 850 MW of AI capacity containing more than 300,000 GPUs since the end of the previous quarter.\\n    Quote: Magouyrk also said the company delivered 850 megawatts of AI capacity containing more than 300,000 GPUs since the end of its previous quarter.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e4562; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\n- e4331 [fact; Benzinga; original source Oracle ; from gnews:44f4bd6cc91ff33688f1e69f 2026-09-10] Oracle closed more than $30 billion in additional AI contracts during its fiscal 2027 first quarter without requiring additional capital; GPU utilization was 97.9%.\\n    Quote: Oracle also closed more than $30 billion in additional AI contracts during the quarter without requiring additional capital, while GPU utilization remained extremely high at 97.9%.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e4537, e4563, e4566; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\n- e4534 [party_statement; fool.com (Manali Pradhan); original source OpenAI ; from gnews:ab387b35d7ed1e8494a84d33 2026-09-12] OpenAI said its Jalape\\u00f1o chip, co-developed with Broadcom, is intended to run large AI models more efficiently and is planned for deployment across very large data centers; Reuters reported that reducing reliance on NVIDIA GPUs and operating costs was part of the motivation.\\n    Quote: According to Reuters, OpenAI developed the chip partly to reduce its reliance on Nvidia GPUs and lower operating costs. OpenAI said that Jalape\\u00f1o was built specifically to run large AI models more efficiently and is planned for deployment across very large data centers.\\n- e4555 [party_statement; Elon Musk, quoted from SpaceX's second-quarter earnings call; original source SpaceX ; from gnews:6490e4ac2a408fad6a7e99a1 2026-09-12] SpaceX CEO Elon Musk said SpaceX has decided to build exclusively on Nvidia going forward, citing Vera Rubin and its relationship with Nvidia.\\n    Quote: [G]oing forward, we've decided to build exclusively on Nvidia because we think the Vera Rubin architecture is the best architecture. We think it's the best AI computer, and we greatly value our close cooperation and partnership on many levels with Nvidia. So we're exclusive to Nvidia.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e3513; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\n- e4556 [fact; fool.com (analyst); original source Anthropic and SpaceX ; from gnews:6490e4ac2a408fad6a7e99a1 2026-09-12] Anthropic entered into a SpaceX cloud-services agreement worth $1.25 billion per month through 2029 for access to compute across supercomputers featuring roughly 325,000 Nvidia GPUs.\\n    Quote: Anthropic entered into a cloud services agreement with SpaceX worth $1.25 billion a month through 2029. The deal provides Anthropic with access to compute capacity across SpaceX's supercomputers, Colossus and Colossus II, which feature roughly 325,000 Nvidia GPUs.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e1498; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\n- e4557 [fact; fool.com (analyst); original source Google Cloud ; from gnews:6490e4ac2a408fad6a7e99a1 2026-09-12] Google Cloud committed $920 million per month through mid-2029 for access to roughly 110,000 Nvidia GPUs, CPUs, memory, and related networking equipment.\\n    Quote: Meanwhile, Google Cloud committed $920 million a month for access to roughly 110,000 Nvidia GPUs, CPUs, memory, and related networking kits through the middle of 2029.\\n- e4558 [fact; fool.com (analyst); original source Reflection AI ; from gnews:6490e4ac2a408fad6a7e99a1 2026-09-12] Reflection AI signed a multiyear agreement worth up to $6.3 billion to access Nvidia GB300 chips, at a reported $150 million per month.\\n    Quote: Most recently, Reflection AI signed a multiyear deal worth up to $6.3 billion to access Nvidia GB300 chips at a reported $150 million per month.\\n- e4562 [fact; fool.com (Daniel Sparks); original source Oracle ; from gnews:0c19765ee99d1f808e0834ec 2026-09-12] Oracle delivered 850 megawatts of AI capacity containing more than 300,000 GPUs to customers in fiscal Q1 2027, ended August 31.\\n    Quote: The software and cloud giant delivered 850 megawatts of artificial intelligence (AI) capacity to customers in its fiscal first quarter of 2027 (the period ended Aug. 31). That hardware contained more than 300,000 graphics processing units (GPUs).\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e4330; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\n- e4563 [fact; fool.com (Daniel Sparks); original source Oracle ; from gnews:0c19765ee99d1f808e0834ec 2026-09-12] Oracle reported 97.9% utilization across its GPU fleet in fiscal Q1 2027.\\n    Quote: And Oracle's GPU fleet ran at 97.9% utilization, meaning nearly every chip was busy serving customers.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e4331; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\n- e4571 [party_statement; fool.com (Daniel Sparks), reporting Colette Kress's remarks; original source Colette Kress, NVIDIA CFO ; from gnews:0c19765ee99d1f808e0834ec 2026-09-12] NVIDIA CFO Colette Kress said NVIDIA's compute was fully utilized across every cloud it serves.\\n    Quote: She also said Nvidia's compute was running fully utilized across every cloud it serves.\\n- e4572 [party_statement; fool.com (Daniel Sparks), reporting Colette Kress's remarks; original source Colette Kress, NVIDIA CFO ; from gnews:0c19765ee99d1f808e0834ec 2026-09-12] NVIDIA CFO Colette Kress estimated revenue opportunity per gigawatt at about $18 billion for Hopper, $25 billion for Blackwell, and $40 billion for Vera Rubin.\\n    Quote: A gigawatt of its older Hopper systems meant about $18 billion of revenue opportunity for Nvidia, chief financial officer Colette Kress said on the company's late-August earnings call. Blackwell runs about $25 billion, and the new Vera Rubin platform is about $40 billion.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e3375; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\n- e4574 [third_party_view; Daniel Sparks (fool.com); original source Daniel Sparks (fool.com) 2026-09-12; from gnews:0c19765ee99d1f808e0834ec 2026-09-12] Daniel Sparks judged Oracle's quarter to be strong customer-side evidence that NVIDIA is constrained by manufacturing capacity rather than demand.\\n    Quote: Ultimately, though, I think it's the best customer-side evidence yet that what limits Nvidia is manufacturing capacity rather than appetite.\\n- e4725 [third_party_view; InsiderMonkey; original source InsiderMonkey 2026-09-15; from gnews:a1af1bb8840fa4ec9e52bcb0 2026-09-15] InsiderMonkey reported that Anthropic had agreed to purchase billions of dollars of AI servers from AMD and that Broadcom was involved in efforts to develop custom AI chips for Anthropic.\\n    Quote: More recently, Anthropic agreed to purchase billions of dollars of AI servers from AMD, while Broadcom has been involved in efforts to develop custom AI chips for Anthropic.\\n- e4765 [party_statement; fool.com (analyst); original source NVIDIA management ; from gnews:9fd93b942948c5002e13eb0b 2026-09-15] NVIDIA management said ACIE, about 45% of Data Center revenue, would drive most sequential Data Center revenue growth in fiscal Q3 2027, while hyperscaler demand could accelerate more in Q4 and FY2028.\\n    Quote: ACIE already accounts for about 45% of Nvidia's Data Center revenue. Management expects ACIE to drive most of the sequential revenue growth for Data Center in the third quarter, while hyperscaler demand could pick up more strongly in the fourth quarter and in fiscal 2028.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e4052; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\n- e4778 [fact; SCMP.com; original source Huawei Technologies ; from gnews:f19d2672d18ad2f26e5adeb3 2026-09-16] Huawei introduced near-packaged optics to its SuperPoD architecture for the first time at Huawei Connect 2026, changing the configuration of a competing AI-computing system.\\n    Quote: At the Huawei Connect 2026 conference in Shanghai, the Shenzhen-based firm introduced near-packaged optics (NPOs) \\u2013 a placement structure enabling higher speeds and lower energy use \\u2013 to the company\\u2019s SuperPoD architecture for the first time.\\n- e4779 [fact; SCMP.com; original source Huawei Technologies ; from gnews:f19d2672d18ad2f26e5adeb3 2026-09-16] Huawei unveiled its Atlas 960 SuperPoD computing cluster and an upgraded UnifiedBus interconnect at Huawei Connect 2026, introducing competing AI-computing products relevant to NVIDIA\\u2019s Data Center business.\\n    Quote: Huawei Technologies on Thursday unveiled its latest Atlas 960 SuperPoD computing cluster and an upgraded version of its UnifiedBus interconnect technology, key components of the Chinese tech giant\\u2019s strategy to build advanced artificial intelligence systems despite US semiconductor-related restrictions.\\n- e4783 [fact; finance.yahoo.com author; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:3f21db1f9791e20f80909da8 2026-09-16] NVIDIA reported Q2 FY2027 Data Center segment revenue of $89.02 billion, up 117% year over year.\\n    Quote: Data Center alone at $89.02 billion, up 117%\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e3851; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\n- e4806 [fact; Zacks.com; original source NVIDIA 2026-08-26; from gnews:bc6926bf31d3a4d8006dce46 2026-09-16] NVIDIA reported Data Center revenue of $89 billion in fiscal Q2 2027, up 117% year over year and 18% sequentially.\\n    Quote: NVIDIA's Data Center business remains the primary growth driver, generating $89 billion in the fiscal second quarter of 2027, up 117% from a year ago and 18% sequentially, according to the company's Aug. 26 press release.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e4712; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\n- e4811 [fact; finance.yahoo.com; original source Nokia ; from gnews:3c52e58b83c308775f689177 2026-09-16] Nokia said its AI-RAN platform is advancing from evaluation to live field trials at eight global operators; the report did not name the operators in this statement.\\n    Quote: Nokia ( NYSE:NOK ) stock is rising in early Wednesday trading, up 6% to $10.39 after the company said its artificial intelligence-powered radio access network (AI-RAN) platform is moving from evaluation to live field trials at eight global operators.\\n- e4814 [fact; gurufocus.com (analyst); original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:d9a8cf969d7dedc50100397a 2026-09-16] NVIDIA Data Center revenue was $89 billion in its latest quarter, about 92.5% of total sales.\\n    Quote: Data-center revenue reached $89 billion , roughly 92.5% of Nvidia's latest quarterly sales,\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e4740; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\n- e4816 [fact; gurufocus.com (analyst), relaying The Information; original source Apple and NVIDIA ; from gnews:c25570f36f1535b739bebae6 2026-09-16] Apple has held talks with NVIDIA about using NVLink Fusion to connect chips in its planned AI server.\\n    Quote: has held talks with Nvidia Corp. ( NASDAQ:NVDA ) about using its NVLink Fusion interconnect to link those chips\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e4846; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\n- e4818 [fact; Zacks.com (analyst); original source NVIDIA Corporation ; from gnews:fc6c2e31b8c175953657a182 2026-09-16] NVIDIA reported FY2027 second-quarter revenue growth of 106% year over year and 18% sequentially; Data Center revenue was $89 billion, up 117% year over year and 18% sequentially.\\n    Quote: NVIDIA's second-quarter fiscal 2027 revenue surged 106% year over year and 18% sequentially, while Data Center revenue jumped 117% year over year and 18% sequentially to $89 billion.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e3215, e4897; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\n- e4836 [party_statement; trefis.com; original source NVIDIA management ; from gnews:106a61a1ef10fb3ba6adb1cd 2026-09-16] Management expected Vera Rubin to account for about 20% of NVIDIA Data Center revenue in fiscal Q3 2027.\\n    Quote: management expects that platform to be about 20% of data center revenue in fiscal Q3 2027.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e4767; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\n- e4841 [third_party_view; marketbeat.com; original source marketbeat.com 2026-09-16; from gnews:b98d0a9596b1d1e0a9609645 2026-09-16] MarketBeat reported that Oracle\\u2019s backlog grew to more than $650 billion in Q2.\\n    Quote: Critical players like Oracle (NASDAQ: ORCL), now ubiquitous across cloud instances regardless 