rald AI\\u2019s technology to secure grid capacity for more data centers.\\n    Quote: Grid software unicorn Emerald AI has formed a coalition with Google and Nvidia that will use the startup\\u2019s technology to secure space on the grid for more data centers.\\n- e4865 [third_party_view; TechCrunch; original source AI Energy Management Alliance (AEMA) ; from gnews:4bf9544d82b0d4574011d0a2 2026-09-17] The AI Energy Management Alliance said pausing or shifting data-center compute loads could allow an additional 100 GW of data centers to connect to the grid.\\n    Quote: Pausing noncritical tasks and shifting some compute loads, AEMA says, could allow an additional 100 gigawatts of data centers to connect to the grid.\\n- e4877 [third_party_view; gurufocus.com; original source Huawei ; from gnews:509f491c104308dfdd480587 2026-09-17] Huawei plans to launch its Ascend 960DT in early 2027, about three quarters earlier than previously expected.\\n    Quote: Huawei now plans to launch its Ascend 960DT in early 2027roughly three quarters earlier than previously expected\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e4894, e5040; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\n- e4878 [third_party_view; gurufocus.com; original source Huawei ; from gnews:509f491c104308dfdd480587 2026-09-17] Huawei plans to launch its Ascend 960PR in the third quarter of 2027, following the 960DT.\\n    Quote: followed by the 960PR in the third quarter\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e5041; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\n- e4879 [third_party_view; gurufocus.com; original source Huawei ; from gnews:509f491c104308dfdd480587 2026-09-17] Huawei says its production remains insufficient to satisfy demand in China.\\n    Quote: Huawei says production still cannot satisfy demand inside China\\n- e4880 [fact; gurufocus.com; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:509f491c104308dfdd480587 2026-09-17] NVIDIA Data Center revenue was $89 billion, about 92.5% of its latest-quarter revenue of $96.2 billion.\\n    Quote: Data-center revenue reached $89 billion , accounting for roughly 92.5% of the company's latest $96.2 billion quarter.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e4352; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\n- e4882 [fact; finance.yahoo.com; original source Rackspace Technology ; from gnews:83d2170d7a2b0ef2d1fb730a 2026-09-17] Rackspace entered NVIDIA's Cloud Partner Program to deliver and manage NVIDIA-powered AI computing for regulated and sovereign enterprises; no date or financial commitment was specified.\\n    Quote: The company has entered Nvidia's Cloud Partner Program, aiming to strengthen its role in delivering and managing Nvidia-powered AI computing for regulated and sovereign enterprises.\\n- e4883 [fact; finance.yahoo.com; original source Rackspace Technology ; from gnews:83d2170d7a2b0ef2d1fb730a 2026-09-17] Rackspace introduced its Institutional Sovereign Pod, combining NVIDIA Blackwell technology with Palantir's Foundry and AIP platforms to support governed AI infrastructure; no date or scale was specified.\\n    Quote: Alongside the partnership, Rackspace Technology also introduced its Institutional Sovereign Pod, an architecture that combines Nvidia's Blackwell technology with Palantir's Foundry and AIP platforms to support governed AI infrastructure.\\n- e4894 [party_statement; Huawei spokesperson, quoted by TechCrunch; original source Huawei 2026-09-17; from gnews:d95188870b47d6bc96119e87 2026-09-17] Huawei said its Ascend 960DT AI chip is expected to be ready in Q1 2027, ahead of its previously planned Q3 2027 launch.\\n    Quote: \\u201cThe Ascend 960DT is expected to be ready in Q1 2027. Ascend 960 chips are launching ahead of schedule, doubling performance and advancing year by year,\\u201d the spokesperson said\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e4877; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\n- e4895 [third_party_view; Rui Ma, quoted from her post on X by TechCrunch; original source Rui Ma 2026-09-17; from gnews:d95188870b47d6bc96119e87 2026-09-17] China tech analyst Rui Ma said Huawei\\u2019s newly announced Atlas 960 SuperPoD, described as using 4,096 Ascend 960 chips, is much smaller than the previously stated 15,488-chip configuration.\\n    Quote: \\u201cThe chip itself is coming WAY earlier, but the SuperPoD they announced is much smaller than what they originally laid out,\\u201d Ma wrote.\\n- e4915 [fact; fool.com (analyst); original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:12a943c49b0c41542e6110b5 2026-09-18] NVIDIA's Data Center segment generated about $89 billion in revenue in the quarter ended July 26, 2026.\\n    Quote: About $89 billion of that came from its data center segment.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e3215; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\n- e4916 [party_statement; fool.com (analyst), recounting Colette Kress's earnings-call remarks; original source Colette Kress, NVIDIA CFO ; from gnews:12a943c49b0c41542e6110b5 2026-09-18] NVIDIA CFO Colette Kress said hyperscale revenue was $49 billion, up 13% quarter over quarter, and ACIE revenue was $40 billion, up 25%, in the quarter ended July 26, 2026.\\n    Quote: Hyperscale revenue was $49 billion, up 13% from the prior quarter, while the ACIE side grew even faster to $40 billion, up 25%.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e4051; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\n- e4927 [fact; finance.yahoo.com; original source Nscale ; from gnews:f730ea7bda284baea7749a1c 2026-09-18] Nscale filed publicly for a New York IPO, saying it plans to acquire infrastructure to meet global AI-compute demand.\\n    Quote: London-based AI data center company Nscale has filed publicly for an initial public offering (IPO) in New York to acquire the infrastructure needed to meet the global demand for artificial intelligence compute power.\\n- e4928 [rumour; finance.yahoo.com; original source Bloomberg ; from gnews:f730ea7bda284baea7749a1c 2026-09-18] Bloomberg reported that Nscale is seeking to raise up to $3 billion in its IPO; Nscale did not disclose the offering's size in its filings.\\n    Quote: The company did not disclose the size and scope of its listing in its filings. However, a Bloomberg report cited that the company is seeking to raise as much as $3 billion in the IPO.\\n- e4929 [fact; finance.yahoo.com; original source Nscale ; from gnews:f730ea7bda284baea7749a1c 2026-09-18] Nscale reported revenue of $140.6 million for the six months ended June 30, 2026, versus $10.4 million in the same period of 2025.\\n    Quote: For the six-month period ending June 30, the company generated $140.6 million in revenue, up significantly from $10.4 million during the same period in the prior year.\\n- e4930 [fact; finance.yahoo.com; original source Nscale ; from gnews:f730ea7bda284baea7749a1c 2026-09-18] Nscale reported a net loss of $1.02 billion for the six months ended June 30, 2026, compared with $368.9 million in the same period of 2025.\\n    Quote: However, net losses expanded to $1.02 billion for the period, compared to $368.9 million in the previous year.\\n- e4931 [fact; finance.yahoo.com; original source Nscale ; from gnews:f730ea7bda284baea7749a1c 2026-09-18] Nscale reported control of more than 10 gigawatts of power capacity across its AI hubs as of August 2026.\\n    Quote: Nscale manages hyperscale AI hubs located in Norway, Portugal, Texas, and West Virginia, controlling over 10 gigawatts of power capacity as of August 2026.\\n- e4932 [fact; finance.yahoo.com; original source Nscale ; from gnews:f730ea7bda284baea7749a1c 2026-09-18] Nscale reported about $103 billion in total contract value.\\n    Quote: The firm holds about $103 billion in total contract value.\\n- e4933 [fact; finance.yahoo.com; original source Nscale ; from gnews:f730ea7bd