t AI development did not have to slow down.\\n- e4977 [party_statement; finance.yahoo.com; original source Jensen Huang, NVIDIA CEO ; from gnews:d7c05e7b0777edd1a79bc806 2026-09-18] Jensen Huang said AI labs with safety concerns should delay product launches until those concerns are resolved rather than advocate a broader slowdown in AI development.\\n    Quote: labs with safety concerns should delay launching products until said concerns had been resolved, instead of pushing for a broader slowdown.\\n- e4978 [fact; finance.yahoo.com; original source NVIDIA Corporation ; from gnews:d7c05e7b0777edd1a79bc806 2026-09-18] NVIDIA Data Center revenue doubled to $89 billion in Q2, up 117% year over year.\\n    Quote: NVIDIA Corporation (NASDAQ:NVDA)'s data center revenue doubled to $89 billion in Q2 for a 117% bump\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e4590; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\n- e4980 [third_party_view; finance.yahoo.com; original source Piper Sandler ; from gnews:d7c05e7b0777edd1a79bc806 2026-09-18] Piper Sandler initiated coverage of NVIDIA with an Overweight rating and a $300 price target, citing an estimated 80% share of AI compute and other factors.\\n    Quote: Piper Sandler is quite optimistic about NVIDIA, though, as it initiated coverage with an Overweight rating and a $300 price target on the back of 80% share in AI compute and other factors.\\n- e4981 [fact; benzinga.com; original source Salesforce ; from gnews:cbf072e65acf3391f77465fd 2026-09-18] Salesforce unveiled Koa, its first Agentforce CRM reasoning model, built on NVIDIA Nemotron 3 Super and running inside Salesforce infrastructure.\\n    Quote: Salesforce also unveiled Koa, its first CRM reasoning model for Agentforce, built on Nvidia Nemotron 3 Super and running inside Salesforce infrastructure.\\n- e4982 [third_party_view; Marc Benioff, speaking on Yahoo Finance's Opening Bid; original source Marc Benioff ; from gnews:499375f1d2854d56642e123d 2026-09-18] Salesforce CEO Marc Benioff said NVIDIA\\u2019s business depends on a limited set of customers building enormous data centers.\\n    Quote: He [Jensen] only has a limited set of customers who are just building these enormous data centers that are material to his business.\\n- e4983 [fact; Zacks Investment Ideas author; original source Anthropic ; from gnews:64b3da817a58392d7d1677e7 2026-09-18] Anthropic signed a $13.7 billion compute agreement earlier in September 2026.\\n    Quote: Earlier this month, Anthropic inked a $13.7 billion compute agreement\\n- e4984 [third_party_view; benzinga.com; original source Brad Gerstner ; from gnews:4256ae7ea51b8cf4d4bb371b 2026-09-18] Brad Gerstner estimated that Anthropic, OpenAI and xAI had combined annualized revenue of roughly $100 billion, based on figures circulating in July 2026.\\n    Quote: Gerstner estimated that Anthropic, OpenAI and SpaceX (NASDAQ: SPCX ), which owns xAI, had a combined run rate of roughly $100 billion based on figures circulating in July.\\n- e4985 [third_party_view; benzinga.com; original source Brad Gerstner ; from gnews:4256ae7ea51b8cf4d4bb371b 2026-09-18] Brad Gerstner said Anthropic, OpenAI and xAI need combined annualized revenue of at least $180 billion by the end of 2026 to sustain the AI trade.\\n    Quote: Gerstner said the companies need to reach at least $180 billion by year-end, up about 80% from his July estimate, \\\"just to keep the AI trade intact.\\\"\\n- e4986 [rumour; benzinga.com; original source Unnamed sources cited in the reported figures ; from gnews:4256ae7ea51b8cf4d4bb371b 2026-09-18] Anthropic's reported annualized revenue run rate reached $65 billion in July 2026, up from $47 billion in May 2026.\\n    Quote: Anthropic's revenue run rate reportedly reached $65 billion in July, up from $47 billion in May.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e2181; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\n- e4987 [third_party_view; benzinga.com; original source Brad Gerstner ; from gnews:4256ae7ea51b8cf4d4bb371b 2026-09-18] Brad Gerstner said Anthropic's reported $65 billion annualized revenue run rate fell short of investors' roughly $75 billion expectation.\\n    Quote: He said stocks later consolidated after the $65 billion figure fell short of the roughly $75 billion investors had expected.\\n- e4995 [fact; fool.com (analyst); original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:ad94c78d09fe41fc3f29bbca 2026-09-18] NVIDIA generated $164 billion in Data Center segment revenue in the first six months of FY2027.\\n    Quote: The company has generated $164 billion in revenue from its data center segment in the first six months of fiscal 2027.\\n- e4996 [third_party_view; fool.com (analyst); original source fool.com (analyst) 2026-09-18; from gnews:ad94c78d09fe41fc3f29bbca 2026-09-18] The author calculated an annualized Data Center revenue run rate of just under $330 billion from NVIDIA\\u2019s first-half FY2027 revenue.\\n    Quote: That translates into an annual run rate of just under $330 billion for the full year.\\n- e4999 [fact; TechRadar; original source Emerald AI, Google and NVIDIA ; from gnews:78a58240705bb94d9382a5dd 2026-09-18] Emerald AI, Google and NVIDIA formed the AI Energy Management Alliance to address data-center energy consumption.\\n    Quote: Emerald AI, Google and Nvidia have come together to form the AI Energy Management Alliance (AEMA), and it could be exactly what we need to tackle rising energy consumption within the data center field.\\n- e5000 [rumour; TechRadar, citing SiliconANGLE; original source SiliconANGLE ; from gnews:78a58240705bb94d9382a5dd 2026-09-18] Anthropic is reported to be planning to join the AI Energy Management Alliance as an additional partner.\\n    Quote: SiliconANGLE reports that Anthropic will be one of them.\\n- e5002 [fact; Zacks.com (analyst); original source NVIDIA 2026-08-26; from gnews:57a69374b8fa083ce36ecfb1 2026-09-18] NVIDIA Data Center revenue was $89 billion in FY2027 Q2, up 117% year over year and 18% sequentially.\\n    Quote: The Data Center business remained the key growth driver, with revenues rising 117% year over year and 18% sequentially to $89 billion.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e4712; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\n- e5035 [party_statement; NVIDIA Vice President Ian Buck, quoted in the article; original source Ian Buck ; from gnews:5a42294e229a65208f691101 2026-09-19] NVIDIA Vice President Ian Buck said AgentX benchmark computational demand rose 100-fold on purely numerical tasks; no period was specified.\\n    Quote: In the AgentX benchmark, computational demand has increased by a factor of 100 on purely numerical tasks.\\n- e5036 [party_statement; NVIDIA Vice President Ian Buck, quoted in the article; original source Ian Buck ; from gnews:5a42294e229a65208f691101 2026-09-19] Ian Buck said hourly rental rates for NVIDIA A100 instances have risen rather than declined over time, and described demand as remaining robust; no period or rate was specified.\\n    Quote: In fact, if you track the hourly instance rental rates for the A100\\u2014released at the onset of the COVID\\u201119 pandemic\\u2014you'll find that they have not declined over time but have instead risen, with demand remaining robust.\\n- e5040 [fact; korben.info; original source Huawei ; from gnews:4d60cc40cc0b61c1a9c9fb5d 2026-09-19] Huawei announced that its Ascend 960DT would launch as early as Q1 2027, nine months ahead of plan.\\n    Quote: the Ascend 960DT, would launch as early as Q1 2027, nine months earlier than planned\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e4877; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\n- e5041 [fact; korben.info; original source Huawei ; from gnews:4d60cc40cc0b61c1a9c9fb5d 2026-09-19] Huawei announced that the Ascend 960PR variant would follow in Q3 2027.\\n    Quote: with the 960PR variant following in Q3.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e4878; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\n- e5042 [party_statement; korben.info; original source Huawei ; from gnews:4d60cc40cc0b61c1a9c9fb5d 2026-09-19] Huawei said its planned Atlas 960 SuperPoD would link more than 4,000 accelerators via fiber optics to compensate for the Ascend chips\\u2019 performance gap with U.S. competitors.\\n    Quote: its Atlas 960 SuperPoD, a cluster of more than 4,000 accelerators linked together via fiber optics, is meant to compensate through sheer numbers for what each chip concedes to the American company.\\n- e5043 [party_statement; korben.info; original source Huawei ; from gnews:4d60cc40cc0b61c1a9c9fb5d 2026-09-19] Huawei said it was not producing enough Ascend chips to meet Chinese demand.\\n    Quote: The group even admits it isn't producing enough to meet Chinese demand.\\n- e5044 [party_statement; korben.info; original source Huawei ; from gnews:4d60cc40cc0b61c1a9c9fb5d 2026-09-19] Huawei outlined plans for Ascend 970 in 2028 and Ascend 980 in 2029, saying each generation would double performance.\\n    Quote: Huawei is already promising what's next: an Ascend 970 in 2028, then a 980 in 2029, with a doubling of performance at each generation.\\n- e5045 [fact; korben.info; original source Huawei ; from gnews:4d60cc40cc0b61c1a9c9fb5d 2026-09-19] Huawei is open-sourcing its CANN software, which the article says is already compatible with widely used tools such as PyTorch.\\n    Quote: the company is also open-sourcing its in-house equivalent, CANN, already compatible with widely used tools like PyTorch.\\n- e5072 [fact; fool.com (Daniel Sparks); original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:e5b9c11e2c8ef9754946a897 2026-09-20] NVIDIA Data Center revenue was $89.0 billion in Q2 FY2027, up 117% year over year.\\n    Quote: Data center revenue climbed 117% to $89.0 billion.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e4590; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\n- e5097 [party_statement; moomoo.com, relaying Nscale\\u2019s prospectus; original source Nscale ; from gnews:a7ac49717831582bc5bb87db 2026-09-20] Nscale said that at the end of August 2026, its in-house data centers hosted 7 MW of active computing capacity and 48 MW operated in leased data-center space, under contracts totaling $2.6 billion.\\n    Quote: Nscale stated that, as of the end of August this year, its in-house data centers hosted 7 megawatts of active computing capacity, while an additional 48 megawatts were operating in leased data center space, under contracts totaling $2.6 billion.\\n- e5098 [party_statement; moomoo.com, relaying Nscale\\u2019s prospectus; original source Nscale ; from gnews:a7ac49717831582bc5bb87db 2026-09-20] Nscale said it was preparing 1.3 GW of data-center capacity; the item gives no completion date.\\n    Quote: Furthermore, 1.3 gigawatts of capacity is currently being prepared.\\n- e5099 [party_statement; moomoo.com, relaying Nscale\\u2019s estimate; original source Nscale ; from gnews:a7ac49717831582bc5bb87db 2026-09-20] Nscale estimated that its West Virginia data center, under construction, would begin phased commissioning by the end of 2027 and cost about $70 billion, including a 2 GW natural-gas-fired power plant.\\n    Quote: Nscale estimates that this data center, currently under construction, is expected to begin phased commissioning by the end of next year, with a total cost of approximately US$70 billion, including a 2 GW natural-gas-fired power plant to support its operations.\\n\\n[Themes in force, 9]\\n- v10 (chip-export-controls, due 2027-01-31) Will China's authorities authorize Chinese AI companies to purchase Nvidia H200 chips by 2027-01-31?: now rung 1 Yes; judged 2026-09-20; updated since this thesis was last judged; reasons: The reference sits at rung 2: NVIDIA's Q3 FY2027 guidance assumes no China Data Center compute revenue. That is a sales assumption, not a forecast that Chinese authorities will authorize no purchases. The evidence implies narrow, case-by-case authorization is more likely than no authorization by the\\n- v19 (chip-export-controls, due 2026-12-31) Will the U.S. Senate pass the Remote Access Security Act by 2026-12-31?: now rung 2 No; judged 2026-08-19; reasons: No explicit market consensus or Senate timetable is supplied. The observable reference is that RASA had not passed the Senate as of August 19, which sits at rung 2. The alleged remote-access cases could add pressure for legislation, but the recent evidence reports no Senate action or scheduled vote.\\n- v25 (chip-export-controls, due 2027-01-31) Will Taiwan's Ministry of Economic Affairs introduce performance-threshold export controls for advanced chips by 2027-01-31?: now rung 2 No; judged 2026-07-28; reasons: The required outcome is formal adoption or entry into force by 2027-01-31, not consultation or consideration. Consultations are confirmed, but the Ministry gave no timeline and the controls were only reported as being weighed. That makes adoption by the deadline less likely than no adoption; the evi\\n- v26 (chip-export-controls, due 2027-01-31) Will Taiwan introduce a criminal ban on AI chip exports to China by 2027-01-31?: now rung 2 No; judged 2026-08-25; reasons: The status-quo reference is rung 2, and the evidence still makes no ban by the deadline more likely than a ban. Taiwan is considering a criminal ban, and the alleged export case\\u2014along with lawmakers\\u2019 and experts\\u2019 stated view that the law needs to change\\u2014adds pressure toward legislation. But the supp\\n- v27 (chip-export-controls, due 2027-01-31) Will the U.S. Department of Commerce conclude its investigation into Chinese firms' access to advanced U.S. chips by 2027-01-31?: now rung 2 No; judged 2026-08-25; reasons: The reference is rung 2: the investigation is formally underway and described as likely to remain an ongoing point of contention, with no Commerce deadline or consensus supplied. The access allegations and Taiwanese smuggling enforcement show the issue remains active, but they do not report a Commer\\n- v41 (fed-policy-rate, due 2026-09-30) Will the Federal Reserve raise its policy rate at its September 2026 meeting?: now rung 1 Yes; judged 2026-09-17; reasons: The reference is the fed funds futures market's 86% probability of an increase, which sits at rung 1 (Yes). The later fact says the Federal Reserve raised interest rates on September 17, so the outcome at the meeting is Yes; this is not merely a forecast based on the reference.\\n- v43 (chip-export-controls, due 2027-06-30) Will the required U.S. and EU regulatory reviews of NVIDIA's Hugging Face acquisition be cleared by 2027-06-30?: now rung 1 Yes; judged 2026-09-20; updated since this thesis was last judged; reasons: The stated completion plan falls within the deadline and therefore implies clearance by 2027-06-30. The mandatory U.S. filing and The Register's call for intervention add some risk, but neither supplies a regulator's objection, a delay, or a specific reason the reviews will remain uncleared by the d\\n- v5 (ai-capex, due 2027-03-31) How much will the four largest AI hyperscalers spend on data-center capital expenditures in calendar 2026?: now rung 4 $700 billion to below $800 billion; judged 2026-09-19; reasons: The market reference is roughly $720\\u2013$745 billion for the four companies, which is rung 4. A direct four-hyperscaler estimate of $760 billion and tracking near $745 billion support an implied outcome around $750\\u2013$760 billion. Newer estimates of nearly $800 billion refer to the top five, not these fo\\n- v6 (ai-capex, due 2028-03-31) How much will the four largest AI hyperscalers spend on data-center capital expenditures in calendar 2027?: now rung 4 $1.1 trillion to below $1.2 trillion; judged 2026-09-19; reasons: The market reference is approximately $1.08 trillion for calendar 2027, which is rung 3. The implied estimate remains about $1.19 trillion for the four named hyperscalers: apply the prior approximate four-to-five share proxy (about $730 billion of $800 billion) to NVIDIA\\u2019s $1.3 trillion top-five est\\n\\nAnswer per the JSON schema: one calculation for the family and one answer per member.\",\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r46j.stream:19:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_10\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \\\"nl -ba render_v13.py | sed -n '15,151p'\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"    15\\t\\n    16\\tS, N = {'type': 'string'}, {'type': 'number'}\\n    17\\t\\n    18\\t\\n    19\\tdef nullable(schema):\\n    20\\t    return {'anyOf': [schema, {'type': 'null'}]}\\n    21\\t\\n    22\\t\\n    23\\tdef obj(props, desc=None):\\n    24\\t    out = {'type': 'object', 'properties': props, 'required': list(props), 'additionalProperties': False}\\n    25\\t    if desc:\\n    26\\t        out['description'] = desc\\n    27\\t    return out\\n    28\\t\\n    29\\t\\n    30\\tdef v13_schema(member_ids, evidence_ids, theme_ids):\\n    31\\t    what = obj({k: S for k in ('population', 'measure', 'scope', 'period')},\\n    32\\t               'What the number measures: population, measure (the quantity, such as revenue or units; never its basis), scope, period.')\\n    33\\t    figure = obj({\\n    34\\t        'id': S, 'what': what,\\n    35\\t        'basis': {'type': 'string', 'enum': sorted(cc.BASES), 'description': 'reported: an actual; guidance: the company\\\\'s outlook; consensus: '\\n    36\\t                  'analysts\\\\' average; third_party: one outside party; forecast: this family\\\\'s forecast; prior_forecast: our earlier forecast.'},\\n    37\\t        'scenario': S,\\n    38\\t        'kind': {'type': 'string', 'enum': sorted(cc.KINDS), 'description': 'source: stated in a shown passage; computed: one operation on '\\n    39\\t                 'named figures; estimate: your judgement, stated as yours; prior: our earlier forecast, for comparison only.'},\\n    40\\t        'value': nullable(N), 'low': nullable(N), 'high': nullable(N),\\n    41\\t        'bound': nullable({'type': 'string', 'enum': ['>', '>=', '<', '<=', 'approx', 'approx_below', 'approx_above']}),\\n    42\\t        'unit': S,\\n    43\\t        'evidence': nullable(S),\\n    44\\t        'expression': nullable({'type': 'string', 'description': 'Source only: the complete numeric expression exactly as the passage writes '\\n    45\\t                                'it, qualifiers included (for example \\\"more than $2 billion\\\", \\\"$4.5 billion, plus or minus 3%\\\", \\\"more than triple\\\").'}),\\n    46\\t        'component': nullable({'type': 'string', 'enum': ['value', 'bound', 'midpoint', 'relative', 'low', 'high', 'multiplier']}),\\n    47\\t        'inputs': nullable({'type': 'array', 'items': S}),\\n    48\\t        'operation': nullable({'type': 'string', 'enum': sorted(cc.OPERATIONS)}),\\n    49\\t        'signs': nullable({'type': 'array', 'items': N}),\\n    50\\t        'relation': nullable({'type': 'string', 'enum': ['time_aggregation', 'accounting_parts', 'stated_in_addition', 'overlap_unknown'],\\n    51\\t                              'description': 'Sum and roll_forward: periods of one quantity; declared parts of a whole; a source says they add; '\\n    52\\t                              'unknown overlap (name the disputed figure).'}),\\n    53\\t        'disputed': nullable(S),\\n    54\\t        'bridge': nullable({'type': 'string', 'description': 'Only when no listed identity covers the operation (periods of one quantity, '\\n    55\\t                            'declared parts, a balance and its flows, a stated share or multiplier, a total over a per-unit price): an '\\n    56\\t                            'estimate stating the conversion and listing the operands it converts.'}),\\n    57\\t        'basis_text': nullable(S), 'rests_on': nullable({'type': 'array', 'items': S}),\\n    58\\t        'adjusts': nullable(obj({'figure': S, 'type': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['discount', 'uplift', 'trim']}})),\\n    59\\t        'converts': nullable({'type': 'array', 'items': S}),\\n    60\\t        'pointer': nullable(obj({'view': S, 'day': S})),\\n    61\\t    })\\n    62\\t    push = obj({'evidence_id': {'type': 'string', 'enum': evidence_ids}, 'push': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['toward_first', 'toward_last', 'none']}})\\n    63\\t    theme_push = obj({'view_id': {'type': 'string', 'enum': theme_ids or ['none']},\\n    64\\t                      'push': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['toward_first', 'toward_last', 'none']}})\\n    65\\t    answer = obj({\\n    66\\t        'view_id': {'type': 'string', 'enum': member_ids},\\n    67\\t        'shape': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['forecast', 'unresolved']},\\n    68\\t        'outcome': nullable(S), 'rung': nullable({'type': 'integer'}),\\n    69\\t        'reference': nullable(obj({'figure': nullable(S), 'unavailable': nullable(S)}, 'An external figure, or a calculation from external '\\n    70\\t                              'and reported figures, or unavailable with why; never our earlier forecast.')),\\n    71\\t        'reasons': S, 'why': nullable(S),\\n    72\\t        'cites': {'type': 'array', 'items': {'type': 'string', 'enum': evidence_ids}},\\n    73\\t        'pushes': {'type': 'array', 'items': push}, 'theme_pushes': {'type': 'array', 'items': theme_push},\\n    74\\t        'changed': {'type': 'boolean'}, 'why_changed': S,\\n    75\\t    })\\n    76\\t    return obj({'figures': {'type': 'array', 'items': figure}, 'answers': {'type': 'array', 'items': answer}})\\n    77\\t\\n    78\\t\\n    79\\tdef parts(user):\\n    80\\t    head, rest = user.split('\\\\n\\\\n[Evidence in view', 1)\\n    81\\t    evidence = '[Evidence in view' + rest.split('\\\\n\\\\n[', 1)[0]\\n    82\\t    tail = '\\\\n\\\\n[' + rest.split('\\\\n\\\\n[', 1)[1] if '\\\\n\\\\n[' in rest else ''\\n    83\\t    blocks = {b.split(']', 1)[0]: '[' + b for b in tail.split('\\\\n\\\\n[')[1:]}\\n    84\\t    return head, evidence, blocks\\n    85\\t\\n    86\\t\\n    87\\tdef render(archive_path, calls, family):\\n    88\\t    archive = sqlite3.connect(f'file:{archive_path}?mode=ro', uri=True)\\n    89\\t    heads, lines, seen, themes, earlier = [], [], set(), '', []\\n    90\\t    for view_id, call_id in calls:\\n    91\\t        user = json.loads(archive.execute('select request_json from model_calls where call_id=?', (call_id,)).fetchone()[0])['messages'][1]['content']\\n    92\\t        head, evidence, blocks = parts(user)\\n    93\\t        heads.append(head)\\n    94\\t        for item in evidence.split('\\\\n- ')[1:]:\\n    95\\t            eid = item.split(' ', 1)[0]\\n    96\\t            if eid not in seen:\\n    97\\t                seen.add(eid)\\n    98\\t                lines.append('- ' + item)\\n    99\\t        themes = themes or next((v for k, v in blocks.items() if k.startswith('Themes')), '')\\n   100\\t        prev = next((v for k, v in blocks.items() if k.startswith('Previous')), '').split('\\\\n\\\\nAnswer per the JSON schema')[0]   # [46g.1] v7's output line goes\\n   101\\t        earlier.append(f'- {view_id}: ' + prev.replace('[Previous conclusion, for comparison only]', 'our earlier forecast, not a source:').strip())\\n   102\\t    rel = '; '.join(f'{r[\\\"part\\\"]} is part of {r[\\\"whole\\\"]}' for r in family['relations'] if r['type'] == 'part_of')\\n   103\\t    shared = '; '.join(f'{w[\\\"population\\\"]}, {w[\\\"measure\\\"]}, {w[\\\"scope\\\"]}, {w[\\\"period\\\"]}' for w in family['shared'])\\n   104\\t    user = ('[Family] members:\\\\n' + '\\\\n\\\\n'.join(heads) + f'\\\\n\\\\nRelations: {rel}.\\\\nShared quantities, one forecast each per scenario: {shared}.\\\\n\\\\n'\\n   105\\t            f'[Evidence in view for the family, {len(lines)} items]\\\\n' + '\\\\n'.join(lines) + '\\\\n\\\\n' + themes + '\\\\n\\\\n[Earlier forecasts]\\\\n'\\n   106\\t            + '\\\\n'.join(earlier) + '\\\\n\\\\nAnswer per the JSON schema: one calculation for the family and one answer per member.')\\n   107\\t    return user, sorted(seen), [t.split(' ', 1)[0] for t in themes.split('\\\\n- ')[1:]]\\n   108\\t\\n   109\\t\\n   110\\tdef strict(calc, schema):\\n   111\\t    \\\"\\\"\\\"Fill every optional field with null, as strict structured output returns it.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n   112\\t    fprops = schema['properties']['figures']['items']['properties']\\n   113\\t    aprops = schema['properties']['answers']['items']['properties']\\n   114\\t    figs = [{k: f.get(k) for k in fprops} for f in calc['figures']]\\n   115\\t    for f in figs:\\n   116\\t        f['scenario'] = f['scenario'] or 'base'\\n   117\\t        if f['what'] is None:\\n   118\\t            f['what'] = {'population': '', 'measure': '', 'scope': '', 'period': ''}\\n   119\\t    answers = []\\n   120\\t    for a in calc['answers']:\\n   121\\t        a2 = {k: a.get(k) for k in aprops}\\n   122\\t        if a2['reference'] is not None:\\n   123\\t            a2['reference'] = {'figure': a['reference'].get('figure'), 'unavailable': a['reference'].get('unavailable')}\\n   124\\t        a2['why'] = a.get('why')\\n   125\\t        answers.append(a2)\\n   126\\t    return {'figures': figs, 'answers': answers}\\n   127\\t\\n   128\\t\\n   129\\tdef without_nulls(calc):\\n   130\\t    clean = lambda d: {k: v for k, v in d.items() if v is not None}\\n   131\\t    answers = []\\n   132\\t    for a in calc['answers']:\\n   133\\t        a2 = clean(a)\\n   134\\t        if 'reference' in a2:\\n   135\\t            a2['reference'] = clean(a2['reference'])\\n   136\\t        answers.append(a2)\\n   137\\t    return {'figures': [clean(f) for f in calc['figures']], 'answers': answers}\\n   138\\t\\n   139\\t\\n   140\\tdef main():\\n   141\\t    archive = REPO / 'poc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/old-2/prod/archive.sqlite'\\n   142\\t    system = (HERE / 'judging-v13-draft.txt').read_text()\\n   143\\t    user, evidence_ids, theme_ids = render(archive, [('v14', 8729), ('v9', 8737)], gate.R1_FAMILY)\\n   144\\t    schema = v13_schema(['v14', 'v9'], evidence_ids, theme_ids)\\n   145\\t    calc = gate.r1('c')\\n   146\\t    answer = strict(calc, schema)\\n   147\\t    schema_errors = model.check_schema(answer, schema)\\n   148\\t    for a in answer['answers']:\\n   149\\t        a['cites'] = [e for e in a['cites'] if e in evidence_ids]\\n   150\\t    result = cc.check(gate.R1_FAMILY, gate.R1_PASSAGES, without_nulls(answer))\\n   151\\t    missing = sorted({f['evidence'] for f in calc['figures'] if f.get('evidence')} - set(evidence_ids))\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r45.stream:33:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_16\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \\\"nl -ba src/hivemind/views/judging.py | sed -n '1,435p'\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"     1\\t\\\"\\\"\\\"06-views.md step 7: one re-judging round. Open views whose reading changed are judged in dependency order, each\\n     2\\tonce; a view whose conclusion changed adds its open dependants. The model reads the evidence in force (with each\\n     3\\treplaced predecessor), the dependencies' current conclusions and its own last conclusion (for comparison only).\\n     4\\tCode checks every citation and that a rung move or a first judgement says changed; one retry, then the item fails.\\n     5\\t\\n     6\\tThe request is judging-v7 (D354, frozen with steps 3 and 4), judging-v8 (D694: v7's text with the fuller dependency block) or\\n     7\\tjudging-v12 (D713: v7's text and request; the answer's id fields take only the ids the request lists, and the check reads the same\\n     8\\tlists): no other version is built, and a configuration that names another is refused before any call. Every answer is stored in the\\n     9\\tcanonical vocabulary.\\n    10\\t\\n    11\\tThe theme block (D191, D195): an asset thesis is judged with every open, judged theme thesis in view and answers, in theme_pushes,\\n    12\\twhich way each theme it weighed pushes it; theme theses are judged before asset theses in a round, and a theme judgement that says\\n    13\\tchanged queues every open asset thesis with evidence in force, once. The round's queue is derived from the ledger (the day's changed\\n    14\\tviews, the dependants of views judged at this sequence number with a changed conclusion, and the asset theses a changed theme queues),\\n    15\\tso a resumed round recovers what an earlier commit had queued.\\n    16\\t\\n    17\\tThe evidence in view (D198): a judgement reads the arrivals and the basis among the evidence in force, not everything in force.\\n    18\\t\\n    19\\tThe reference (D260): the rung is the forecast the evidence in force makes most likely, judged against what the market expects\\n    20\\t(consensus, guidance, the stated plan); the answer states the reference and the outcome the evidence implies, both stored beside the\\n    21\\trung, and an empty one is refused.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    22\\timport dataclasses\\n    23\\timport json\\n    24\\timport re\\n    25\\t\\n    26\\tfrom .. import config, model, vocabulary\\n    27\\tfrom . import store\\n    28\\t\\n    29\\tPUSHES = vocabulary.PUSHES\\n    30\\tSUPPORTED_VERSIONS = ('judging-v7', 'judging-v8', 'judging-v12')   # D354: the frozen judging prompt; D694: v8 = v7's text with the fuller dependency block; D712/D713: v12 = v7's text and request with closed id lists\\n    31\\tFULL_DEPENDENCY_BLOCK = ('judging-v8',)\\n    32\\tCLOSED_LISTS = ('judging-v12',)   # the answer's id fields take the ids the request lists (D713)\\n    33\\tREADINGS = 5                      # a piece is shown in the thesis's first five judgements after it arrives\\n    34\\tBASIS = 10                        # and while one of the last ten judgements cited it\\n    35\\tTHEME_REASONS_CHARS = 300\\n    36\\tUPDATED_MARK = 'updated since this thesis was last judged'\\n    37\\t\\n    38\\t\\n    39\\tdef require_supported(prompt_version):\\n    40\\t    \\\"\\\"\\\"Refuses a judging prompt version this code does not build, before any request is made.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    41\\t    if prompt_version not in SUPPORTED_VERSIONS:\\n    42\\t        raise ValueError(f'judging {prompt_version!r} is not built; this code builds only {\\\", \\\".join(SUPPORTED_VERSIONS)} (D354)')\\n    43\\t\\n    44\\t\\n    45\\tdef evidence_in_view(conn, view_id):\\n    46\\t    \\\"\\\"\\\"(the pieces a judgement of this thesis reads, how many pieces in force are not shown): the arrivals (linked after the\\n    47\\t    READINGS-th most recent judgement, or all when there are fewer) and the basis (cited by one of the last BASIS judgements),\\n    48\\t    both among the evidence in force.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    49\\t    in_force = store.evidence_in_force(conn, view_id)\\n    50\\t    recent = store.recent_judgements(conn, view_id, BASIS)\\n    51\\t    arrivals_after = recent[READINGS - 1]['seq'] if len(recent) >= READINGS else -1\\n    52\\t    basis = {evidence_id for j in recent for evidence_id in j['cites']}\\n    53\\t    linked_at = {r['evidence_id']: r['seq'] for r in conn.execute('select evidence_id, seq from evidence_links where view_id=?', (view_id,))}\\n    54\\t    shown = [p for p in in_force if linked_at.get(p['evidence_id'], -1) > arrivals_after or p['evidence_id'] in basis]\\n    55\\t    return shown, len(in_force) - len(shown)\\n    56\\t\\n    57\\t\\n    58\\tdef schema_for(prompt_version, lists=None):\\n    59\\t    \\\"\\\"\\\"The answer's format. Under judging-v12 (D713) its four id fields take the ids the request lists (`lists`, from\\n    60\\t    `request_parts`): one shared enum of the evidence ids for cites and push ids, the dependency ids for cites_views, the theme ids\\n    61\\t    for theme pushes; a field with no id allowed is an array with maxItems 0. Other versions ignore `lists`.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    62\\t    schema = _open_format(prompt_version)\\n    63\\t    if prompt_version not in CLOSED_LISTS:\\n    64\\t        return schema\\n    65\\t    if lists is None:\\n    66\\t        raise ValueError(f'{prompt_version} builds its answer format from the ids its request lists')\\n    67\\t    properties = schema['properties']\\n    68\\t    evidence, dependencies, themes = (sorted(set(lists[key])) for key in ('evidence', 'dependencies', 'themes'))\\n    69\\t    if evidence:\\n    70\\t        schema['$defs'] = {'evidence_id': {'type': 'string', 'enum': evidence}}\\n    71\\t        properties['cites'] = {'type': 'array', 'items': {'$ref': '#/$defs/evidence_id'}}\\n    72\\t        push_item = properties['pushes']['items']\\n    73\\t        properties['pushes'] = {'type': 'array', 'items': dict(push_item, properties=dict(push_item['properties'], evidence_id={'$ref': '#/$defs/evidence_id'}))}\\n    74\\t    else:\\n    75\\t        properties['cites'] = dict(properties['cites'], maxItems=0)\\n    76\\t        properties['pushes'] = dict(properties['pushes'], maxItems=0)\\n    77\\t    if dependencies:\\n    78\\t        properties['cites_views'] = {'type': 'array', 'items': {'type': 'string', 'enum': dependencies}}\\n    79\\t    else:\\n    80\\t        properties['cites_views'] = dict(properties['cites_views'], maxItems=0)\\n    81\\t    theme_item = properties['theme_pushes']['items']\\n    82\\t    if themes:\\n    83\\t        properties['theme_pushes'] = {'type': 'array', 'items': dict(theme_item, properties=dict(theme_item['properties'], view_id={'type': 'string', 'enum': themes}))}\\n    84\\t    else:\\n    85\\t        properties['theme_pushes'] = dict(properties['theme_pushes'], maxItems=0)\\n    86\\t    return schema\\n    87\\t\\n    88\\t\\n    89\\tdef _open_format(prompt_version):\\n    90\\t    require_supported(prompt_version)\\n    91\\t    pushes = PUSHES\\n    92\\t    schema = {\\n    93\\t        'type': 'object', 'additionalProperties': False,\\n    94\\t        'required': ['rung', 'reasons', 'cites', 'cites_views', 'pushes', 'changed', 'why_changed'],\\n    95\\t        'properties': {\\n    96\\t            'rung': {'type': 'integer'}, 'reasons': {'type': 'string'},\\n    97\\t            'cites': {'type': 'array', 'items': {'type': 'string'}}, 'cites_views': {'type': 'array', 'items': {'type': 'string'}},\\n    98\\t            'pushes': {'type': 'array', 'items': {'type': 'object', 'additionalProperties': False, 'required': ['evidence_id', 'push'],\\n    99\\t                                                  'properties': {'evidence_id': {'type': 'string'}, 'push': {'type': 'string', 'enum': pushes}}}},\\n   100\\t            'changed': {'type': 'boolean'}, 'why_changed': {'type': 'string'},\\n   101\\t        },\\n   102\\t    }\\n   103\\t    schema['required'].append('theme_pushes')\\n   104\\t    schema['properties']['theme_pushes'] = {'type': 'array', 'items': {'type': 'object', 'additionalProperties': False, 'required': ['view_id', 'push'],\\n   105\\t                                                                       'properties': {'view_id': {'type': 'string'}, 'push': {'type': 'string', 'enum': pushes}}}}\\n   106\\t    schema['required'][1:1] = STANCE_FIELDS           # after rung: the reference and the implied outcome are written before the reasons\\n   107\\t    schema['properties'].update({field: {'type': 'string'} for field in STANCE_FIELDS})\\n   108\\t    return schema\\n   109\\t\\n   110\\t\\n   111\\tdef themes_in_force(conn, view_id):\\n   112\\t    \\\"\\\"\\\"The theme block of an asset thesis: every open theme thesis with a current state, with its rung label and whether a\\n   113\\t    changed conclusion was recorded after this thesis's last judgement. Empty for a theme thesis.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n   114\\t    if store.view(conn, view_id)['object_kind'] == 'theme':\\n   115\\t        return []\\n   116\\t    last = store.current_state(conn, view_id)\\n   117\\t    out = []\\n   118\\t    for row in conn.execute(\\\"select view_id from views where object_kind='theme' order by view_id\\\"):\\n   119\\t        theme_id = row['view_id']\\n   120\\t        state = store.current_state(conn, theme_id)\\n   121\\t        if not state or not store.is_open(conn, theme_id):\\n   122\\t            continue\\n   123\\t        updated = bool(last) and bool(conn.execute('select 1 from judgements where view_id=? and changed=1 and judgement_id>? limit 1',\\n   124\\t                                                   (theme_id, last['judgement_id'])).fetchone())\\n   125\\t        rung = store.rungs_of(conn, theme_id)[state['rung'] - 1]\\n   126\\t        out.append({'view_id': theme_id, 'view': store.view(conn, theme_id), 'state': state, 'rung_label': rung['label'], 'updated': updated})\\n   127\\t    return out\\n   128\\t\\n   129\\t\\n   130\\tSTANCE_FIELDS = ['reference', 'implied_outcome']   # D260: what the market expects, and the figure or date the evidence implies\\n   131\\t\\n   132\\t\\n   133\\tclass JudgementRefused(Exception):\\n   134\\t    pass\\n   135\\t\\n   136\\t\\n   137\\tdef topological(conn, view_ids):\\n   138\\t    \\\"\\\"\\\"Dependencies first: a view comes after every view it depends on that is also in the set.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n   139\\t    remaining = list(dict.fromkeys(view_ids))\\n   140\\t    ordered, placed = [], set()\\n   141\\t    while remaining:\\n   142\\t        progressed = False\\n   143\\t        for view_id in list(remaining):\\n   144\\t            deps = {d['resolved_to'] for d in store.dependencies_of(conn, view_id) if d['resolved_to']}\\n   145\\t            if deps.isdisjoint(set(remaining) - {view_id}) or deps <= placed:\\n   146\\t                ordered.append(view_id)\\n   147\\t                placed.add(view_id)\\n   148\\t                remaining.remove(view_id)\\n   149\\t                progressed = True\\n   150\\t        if not progressed:                 # a cycle slipped through: keep going in the given order\\n   151\\t            ordered.extend(remaining)\\n   152\\t            break\\n   153\\t    return ordered\\n   154\\t\\n   155\\t\\n   156\\tdef _indented(text, indent='        '):\\n   157\\t    \\\"\\\"\\\"A stored value inside a block: every continuation line indented, so no physical line can read as a header or a listed id.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n   158\\t    return str(text).replace('\\\\r\\\\n', '\\\\n').replace('\\\\n', '\\\\n' + indent)\\n   159\\t\\n   160\\t\\n   161\\tdef _dependency_lines_full(conn, target, dependency, state, rung_label, target_view, flag):\\n   162\\t    \\\"\\\"\\\"judging-v8 (D694, design §3): the read judgement's comparison point and the system's forecast in full, labelled as ours, beside\\n   163\\t    the reasons excerpt; the read question not judged yet shows only that.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n   164\\t    if not state:\\n   165\\t        return [f'- {target} ({flag}; {dependency[\\\"direction\\\"]}) {target_view[\\\"question\\\"]}: now not judged yet']\\n   166\\t    return [f'- {target} ({flag}; {dependency[\\\"direction\\\"]}) {target_view[\\\"question\\\"]}: now rung {state[\\\"rung\\\"]} {rung_label}, judged {state[\\\"publication_day\\\"]}',\\n   167\\t            f'    Comparison point stated by that judgement: {_indented(state.get(\\\"reference\\\") or \\\"not stated\\\")}',\\n   168\\t            f'    The system\\\\'s forecast for it (our own judgement, not evidence): {_indented(state.get(\\\"implied_outcome\\\") or \\\"not stated\\\")}',\\n   169\\t            f'    Reasons (excerpt): {_indented((state.get(\\\"reasons\\\") or \\\"\\\")[:600])}']\\n   170\\t\\n   171\\t\\n   172\\tdef _lines_english(conn, view_id, v, rungs, pieces, deps, last, themes=(), hidden=0, full_dependencies=False):\\n   173\\t    \\\"\\\"\\\"hidden: how many pieces in force are not shown. full_dependencies: the judging-v8 dependency block.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n   174\\t    lines = [f'Thesis {view_id} ({v[\\\"object_id\\\"]}, {v[\\\"kind\\\"]}, focus \\\"{v[\\\"looks_at\\\"]}\\\", {v[\\\"year\\\"] or \\\"\\\"}, due {v[\\\"due_day\\\"]}): {v[\\\"question\\\"]}',\\n   175\\t             'Ladder: ' + ' / '.join(f'rung {r[\\\"position\\\"]} {r[\\\"label\\\"]}: {r[\\\"condition\\\"]}' for r in rungs), '',\\n   176\\t             f'[Evidence in view under this thesis, {len(pieces)} items]']\\n   177\\t    if hidden:\\n   178\\t        lines.append(f'[Not shown: {hidden} more pieces in force, read in earlier judgements; the previous conclusion carries them]')\\n   179\\t    for p in pieces:\\n   180\\t        src = p['sources'][0] if p['sources'] else {}\\n   181\\t        lines.append(f'- {p[\\\"evidence_id\\\"]} [{p[\\\"tier\\\"]}; {p[\\\"speaker\\\"]}; original source {p[\\\"original_who\\\"]} {p[\\\"original_day\\\"]}; from {src.get(\\\"input_id\\\")} {src.get(\\\"publication_day\\\")}] {p[\\\"one_line\\\"]}\\\\n    Quote: {p[\\\"quote\\\"][:400]}')\\n   182\\t        if p.get('replaced'):\\n   183\\t            lines.append(f'    It replaces {p[\\\"replaced\\\"][\\\"evidence_id\\\"]} ({p[\\\"replaced\\\"][\\\"original_day\\\"]}): {p[\\\"replaced\\\"][\\\"one_line\\\"]}')\\n   184\\t        if p.get('same_as'):\\n   185\\t            lines.append(f'    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as {\\\", \\\".join(p[\\\"same_as\\\"])}; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.')\\n   186\\t        if p.get('revises'):\\n   187\\t            lines.append(f'    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read it as a later version of {p[\\\"revises\\\"][\\\"evidence_id\\\"]} ({p[\\\"revises\\\"][\\\"original_day\\\"]}); both are in force: {p[\\\"revises\\\"][\\\"one_line\\\"]}')\\n   188\\t    if deps:\\n   189\\t        lines.append('\\\\n[Current conclusions of the theses it depends on]')\\n   190\\t        for d in deps:\\n   191\\t            target = d['resolved_to']\\n   192\\t            if not target:\\n   193\\t                lines.append(f'- the {d[\\\"wait_year\\\"]} thesis on chain {d[\\\"wait_chain_view_id\\\"]}: not yet created ({d[\\\"direction\\\"]})')\\n   194\\t                continue\\n   195\\t            tv = store.view(conn, target)\\n   196\\t            state = store.current_state(conn, target)\\n   197\\t            flag = 'historical only' if d['resolution'] == 'history_only' else ('closed' if not store.is_open(conn, target) else 'open')\\n   198\\t            rung_label = store.rungs_of(conn, target)[state['rung'] - 1]['label'] if state else 'not judged yet'\\n   199\\t            if full_dependencies:\\n   200\\t                lines.extend(_dependency_lines_full(conn, target, d, state, rung_label, tv, flag))\\n   201\\t                continue\\n   202\\t            lines.append(f'- {target} ({flag}; {d[\\\"direction\\\"]}) {tv[\\\"question\\\"]}: now rung {state[\\\"rung\\\"] if state else \\\"-\\\"} {rung_label}; reasons: {(state or {}).get(\\\"reasons\\\", \\\"\\\")[:600]}')\\n   203\\t    if themes:\\n   204\\t        lines.append(f'\\\\n[Themes in force, {len(themes)}]')\\n   205\\t        for theme in themes:\\n   206\\t            tv, state = theme['view'], theme['state']\\n   207\\t            mark = f'; {UPDATED_MARK}' if theme['updated'] else ''\\n   208\\t            lines.append(f'- {theme[\\\"view_id\\\"]} ({tv[\\\"object_id\\\"]}, due {tv[\\\"due_day\\\"]}) {tv[\\\"question\\\"]}: now rung {state[\\\"rung\\\"]} {theme[\\\"rung_label\\\"]}; '\\n   209\\t                         f'judged {state[\\\"publication_day\\\"]}{mark}; reasons: {(state[\\\"reasons\\\"] or \\\"\\\")[:THEME_REASONS_CHARS]}')\\n   210\\t    if last:\\n   211\\t        lines.append(f'\\\\n[Previous conclusion, for comparison only] rung {last[\\\"rung\\\"]}; reasons: {last[\\\"reasons\\\"][:800]}')\\n   212\\t    else:\\n   213\\t        lines.append('\\\\n[Previous conclusion] none: this is the first judgement, so changed must be true.')\\n   214\\t    lines.append('\\\\nAnswer per the JSON schema. cites may name only the evidence ids listed above; '\\n   215\\t                 + ('cites_views only the dependency thesis ids listed above' if deps else 'cites_views must be empty: this thesis depends on no other thesis')\\n   216\\t                 + ('; theme_pushes only the theme ids listed above; a theme id goes only in theme_pushes, never in cites or cites_views' if themes else '') + '.')\\n   217\\t    return lines\\n   218\\t\\n   219\\t\\n   220\\tdef build_prompt(conn, view_id, prompt_version):\\n   221\\t    system, user, _ = request_parts(conn, view_id, prompt_version)\\n   222\\t    return system, user\\n   223\\t\\n   224\\t\\n   225\\tdef request_parts(conn, view_id, prompt_version):\\n   226\\t    \\\"\\\"\\\"(system text, user text, the ids the request lists), all from the same rows at the same ledger state: the evidence pieces it\\n   227\\t    prints, the dependencies it gives an entry (resolved ones; a dependency still waiting has no id to cite) and the themes it prints.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n   228\\t    require_supported(prompt_version)\\n   229\\t    v = store.view(conn, view_id)\\n   230\\t    rungs = store.rungs_of(conn, view_id)\\n   231\\t    pieces, hidden = evidence_in_view(conn, view_id)\\n   232\\t    deps = store.dependencies_of(conn, view_id)\\n   233\\t    last = store.current_state(conn, view_id)\\n   234\\t    themes = themes_in_force(conn, view_id)\\n   235\\t    lines = _lines_english(conn, view_id, v, rungs, pieces, deps, last, themes, hidden=hidden,\\n   236\\t                           full_dependencies=prompt_version in FULL_DEPENDENCY_BLOCK)\\n   237\\t    lists = {'evidence': sorted({p['evidence_id'] for p in pieces}), 'dependencies': sorted({d['resolved_to'] for d in deps if d['resolved_to']}),\\n   238\\t             'themes': sorted({theme['view_id'] for theme in themes})}\\n   239\\t    with open(config.prompt_path(prompt_version + '.txt'), encoding='utf-8') as handle:\\n   240\\t        return handle.read(), '\\\\n'.join(lines), lists\\n   241\\t\\n   242\\t\\n   243\\tdef retry_note(errors):\\n   244\\t    return '\\\\n\\\\nThe code returned the previous answer because: ' + '; '.join(errors) + '\\\\nCorrect it and answer again, citing only the listed ids.'\\n   245\\t\\n   246\\t\\n   247\\tdef themes_shown_in(request_text):\\n   248\\t    \\\"\\\"\\\"The theme ids of the block a request carried: the ids the answer may name, whatever the ledger says now.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n   249\\t    block = request_text.split('\\\\n[Themes in force, ', 1)\\n   250\\t    return set(re.findall(r'^- (v\\\\d+) \\\\(', block[1].split('\\\\n\\\\n[', 1)[0], re.M)) if len(block) == 2 else set()\\n   251\\t\\n   252\\t\\n   253\\tdef evidence_shown_in(request_text):\\n   254\\t    \\\"\\\"\\\"The evidence ids the request listed: the ids the answer may cite and push.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n   255\\t    block = request_text.split('\\\\n[Evidence in ', 1)\\n   256\\t    return set(re.findall(r'^- (e\\\\d+) \\\\[', block[1].split('\\\\n\\\\n[', 1)[0], re.M)) if len(block) == 2 else set()\\n   257\\t\\n   258\\t\\n   259\\tdef check_answer(conn, view_id, data, request_text=None, lists=None):\\n   260\\t    \\\"\\\"\\\"request_text: the user message that was sent, so theme and evidence ids are checked against what it carried (a theme may have\\n   261\\t    closed or opened since); without it, against what the ledger would show now. lists (judging-v12, D713): the ids the request\\n   262\\t    listed, from the rows that rendered it, the same lists its answer format closed; membership is checked against them.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n   263\\t    errors = []\\n   264\\t    if lists is not None:\\n   265\\t        shown = set(lists['themes'])\\n   266\\t    else:\\n   267\\t        shown = themes_shown_in(request_text) if request_text is not None else {theme['view_id'] for theme in themes_in_force(conn, view_id)}\\n   268\\t    named = []\\n   269\\t    for entry in data.get('theme_pushes', []):\\n   270\\t        if entry['view_id'] in named:\\n   271\\t            errors.append(f'{entry[\\\"view_id\\\"]} is named twice in theme_pushes')\\n   272\\t        elif entry['view_id'] not in shown:\\n   273\\t            errors.append(f'{entry[\\\"view_id\\\"]} is not a theme in force shown to {view_id}')\\n   274\\t        named.append(entry['view_id'])\\n   275\\t    # the closed set is what the request showed (D198), read from the text that was sent, else computed from the ledger\\n   276\\t    if lists is not None:\\n   277\\t        allowed, deps = set(lists['evidence']), set(lists['dependencies'])\\n   278\\t    else:\\n   279\\t        allowed = evidence_shown_in(request_text) if request_text is not None else {p['evidence_id'] for p in evidence_in_view(conn, view_id)[0]}\\n   280\\t        deps = {d['resolved_to'] for d in store.dependencies_of(conn, view_id) if d['resolved_to']}\\n   281\\t    not_allowed = lambda e: f'{e} is not among the evidence shown to {view_id}'\\n   282\\t    bad_push = lambda e: f'push on {e} which was not shown to {view_id}'\\n   283\\t    rungs = store.rungs_of(conn, view_id)\\n   284\\t    if not 1 <= data['rung'] <= len(rungs):\\n   285\\t        errors.append(f'rung {data[\\\"rung\\\"]} outside 1..{len(rungs)}')\\n   286\\t    for cited in data['cites']:\\n   287\\t        if cited not in allowed:\\n   288\\t            errors.append(not_allowed(cited))\\n   289\\t    for cited in data['cites_views']:\\n   290\\t        if cited not in deps:\\n   291\\t            errors.append(f'{cited} is not a dependency of {view_id}')\\n   292\\t    for push in data['pushes']:\\n   293\\t        if push['evidence_id'] not in allowed:\\n   294\\t            errors.append(bad_push(push['evidence_id']))\\n   295\\t    for field in STANCE_FIELDS:\\n   296\\t        if not str(data.get(field) or '').strip():\\n   297\\t            errors.append(f'{field} is empty: state what the market expects and the figure or date the evidence implies')\\n   298\\t    last = store.current_state(conn, view_id)\\n   299\\t    if last is None and not data['changed']:\\n   300\\t        errors.append('first judgement must say changed')\\n   301\\t    if last is not None and last['rung'] != data['rung'] and not data['changed']:\\n   302\\t        errors.append(f'rung moved from {last[\\\"rung\\\"]} to {data[\\\"rung\\\"]} but changed is false')\\n   303\\t    return errors\\n   304\\t\\n   305\\t\\n   306\\tdef _record(conn, cfg, view_id, seq, item, answer):\\n   307\\t    data = vocabulary.judgement_answer(answer.data)\\n   308\\t    judgement_id = store.insert(conn, 'judgements', view_id=view_id, seq=seq, input_id=item['input_id'], rung=data['rung'],\\n   309\\t                                reasons=data['reasons'], cited_evidence_json=json.dumps(data['cites']), cited_views_json=json.dumps(data['cites_views']),\\n   310\\t                                pushes_json=json.dumps(data['pushes'], ensure_ascii=False), changed=1 if data['changed'] else 0,\\n   311\\t                                theme_pushes_json=json.dumps(data.get('theme_pushes', []), ensure_ascii=False),\\n   312\\t                                reference=data.get('reference'), implied_outcome=data.get('implied_outcome'),\\n   313\\t                                why_changed=data['why_changed'], config_checksum=cfg.checksum, call_id=answer.call_id,\\n   314\\t                                request_sha256=answer.request_sha256, publication_day=item['publication_day'])\\n   315\\t    conn.commit()\\n   316\\t    return {'view_id': view_id, 'judgement_id': judgement_id, 'rung': data['rung'], 'changed': data['changed'], 'cost': answer.cost_usd, 'cached': answer.cached}\\n   317\\t\\n   318\\t\\n   319\\tJUDGE_WORKERS = 32     # a day's round is up to 40 judgements of about 16 s each in two dependency levels (themes, then assets); 32 at a time makes a round about two calls long (2026-11-02)\\n   320\\t\\n   321\\t\\n   322\\tdef upstream(conn, view_id):\\n   323\\t    \\\"\\\"\\\"Every view this one depends on, directly or through its dependencies.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n   324\\t    seen, stack = set(), [view_id]\\n   325\\t    while stack:\\n   326\\t        for dep in store.dependencies_of(conn, stack.pop()):\\n   327\\t            target = dep['resolved_to']\\n   328\\t            if target and target not in seen:\\n   329\\t                seen.add(target)\\n   330\\t                stack.append(target)\\n   331\\t    return seen\\n   332\\t\\n   333\\t\\n   334\\tdef open_asset_views(conn):\\n   335\\t    return [v for v in store.open_views(conn) if store.view(conn, v)['object_kind'] != 'theme']\\n   336\\t\\n   337\\t\\n   338\\tdef queued_by_change(conn, view_id):\\n   339\\t    \\\"\\\"\\\"What a changed conclusion of this view queues: its dependants and, for a theme thesis, every open asset thesis. The one rule,\\n   340\\t    read for a live judgement and for the judgements a resumed round finds committed.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n   341\\t    queued = store.dependants_of(conn, view_id)\\n   342\\t    if store.view(conn, view_id)['object_kind'] == 'theme':\\n   343\\t        queued = queued + open_asset_views(conn)\\n   344\\t    return queued\\n   345\\t\\n   346\\t\\n   347\\tdef queued_by_ledger(conn, seq):\\n   348\\t    \\\"\\\"\\\"What the judgements already committed at this sequence number queued; a fresh round finds nothing here, a resumed round\\n   349\\t    finds what the interrupted one had queued in memory.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n   350\\t    queued = []\\n   351\\t    for row in conn.execute('select view_id from judgements where seq=? and changed=1 order by judgement_id', (seq,)):\\n   352\\t        queued.extend(queued_by_change(conn, row['view_id']))\\n   353\\t    return queued\\n   354\\t\\n   355\\t\\n   356\\tdef round_of_judgements(archive, cfg, conn, changed_views, seq, item, *, transport=None):\\n   357\\t    \\\"\\\"\\\"Judge the open views in changed_views, dependencies first; a changed conclusion queues open dependants.\\n   358\\t\\n   359\\t    Views that do not depend on each other are judged at the same time: each level of the dependency order is sent\\n   360\\t    to the model concurrently (the prompts are built and the answers checked and written in this thread, so the\\n   361\\t    database connection never crosses threads). A view waits while anything upstream of it is still pending, so a\\n   362\\t    dependant always reads this round's conclusion of its dependency. A view with no evidence in force stays\\n   363\\t    unjudged (D59), and a view already judged at this sequence number (a resumed round) is not judged twice.\\n   364\\t\\n   365\\t    Among the views ready to be judged, theme theses go first, so an asset thesis reads this round's theme conclusions; a theme judgement that says changed queues every open asset thesis with\\n   366\\t    evidence in force. The starting queue adds what the ledger says earlier commits at this sequence number queued.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n   367\\t    import concurrent.futures\\n   368\\t\\n   369\\t    version = cfg.rejudging.prompt_version\\n   370\\t    closed = version in CLOSED_LISTS\\n   371\\t    open_schema = None if closed else schema_for(version)\\n   372\\t\\n   373\\t    def eligible(view_id):\\n   374\\t        return store.is_open(conn, view_id) and not store.has_judgement(conn, view_id, seq) and bool(store.evidence_in_force(conn, view_id))\\n   375\\t\\n   376\\t    def is_theme(view_id):\\n   377\\t        return store.view(conn, view_id)['object_kind'] == 'theme'\\n   378\\t\\n   379\\t    pending = [v for v in topological(conn, list(changed_views) + queued_by_ledger(conn, seq)) if eligible(v)]\\n   380\\t    done, results = set(), []\\n   381\\t    while pending:\\n   382\\t        ready = [v for v in pending if upstream(conn, v).isdisjoint(set(pending) - {v})] or pending[:1]\\n   383\\t        level = [v for v in ready if is_theme(v)] or ready\\n   384\\t        if closed:                                         # D713: the format's lists and the check's lists come from the rows that render the text\\n   385\\t            parts = {v: request_parts(conn, v, version) for v in level}\\n   386\\t            prompts = {v: parts[v][:2] for v in level}\\n   387\\t            lists = {v: parts[v][2] for v in level}\\n   388\\t            schemas = {v: schema_for(version, lists[v]) for v in level}\\n   389\\t        else:                                              # judging-v7/v8: through build_prompt, which harnesses wrap\\n   390\\t            prompts = {v: build_prompt(conn, v, version) for v in level}\\n   391\\t            lists = {v: None for v in level}\\n   392\\t            schemas = {v: open_schema for v in level}\\n   393\\t\\n   394\\t        def ask(view_id, note=''):\\n   395\\t            system, user = prompts[view_id]\\n   396\\t            return model.call(archive, cfg, cfg.rejudging, system, user + note, schemas[view_id], 'judgement', 'judge', transport=transport)\\n   397\\t\\n   398\\t        with concurrent.futures.ThreadPoolExecutor(max_workers=JUDGE_WORKERS) as pool_:\\n   399\\t            answers = dict(zip(level, pool_.map(ask, level)))\\n   400\\t        for view_id in level:\\n   401\\t            answer = answers[view_id]\\n   402\\t            errors = check_answer(conn, view_id, answer.data, prompts[view_id][1], lists[view_id])\\n   403\\t            if errors:\\n   404\\t                archive.retire(answer.call_id)                 # a refused answer never answers the same request again (a resume re-samples)\\n   405\\t                answer = ask(view_id, retry_note(errors))\\n   406\\t                errors = check_answer(conn, view_id, answer.data, prompts[view_id][1], lists[view_id])\\n   407\\t                if errors:\\n   408\\t                    archive.retire(answer.call_id)\\n   409\\t                    raise JudgementRefused(f'{view_id}: ' + '; '.join(errors))\\n   410\\t            result = _record(conn, cfg, view_id, seq, item, answer)\\n   411\\t            done.add(view_id)\\n   412\\t            results.append(result)\\n   413\\t            if result['changed']:\\n   414\\t                for dependant in queued_by_change(conn, view_id):\\n   415\\t                    if dependant not in done and dependant not in pending and eligible(dependant):\\n   416\\t                        pending.append(dependant)\\n   417\\t        pending = [v for v in topological(conn, pending) if v not in done and eligible(v)]\\n   418\\t    return results\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r45.stream:58:{\"type\":\"item.started\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_30\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \\\"python3 -B -c 'import sqlite3,json,pathlib,re,collections,decimal\\nD=decimal.Decimal\\ndef db(i,name='\\\\\\\\''views'\\\\\\\\''):\\n c=sqlite3.connect((pathlib.Path(f'\\\\\\\\''poc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/old-{i}/prod'\\\\\\\\'')/(name+'\\\\\\\\''.sqlite'\\\\\\\\'')).resolve().as_uri()+'\\\\\\\\''?mode=ro'\\\\\\\\'',uri=True)\\n c.row_factory=sqlite3.Row\\n return c\\ndef req(a,j):\\n c=a.execute('\\\\\\\\''select * from model_calls where call_id=?'\\\\\\\\'',(j['\\\\\\\\''call_id'\\\\\\\\''],)).fetchone()\\n assert c and c['\\\\\\\\''request_sha256'\\\\\\\\'']==j['\\\\\\\\''request_sha256'\\\\\\\\''] and c['\\\\\\\\''purpose'\\\\\\\\'']=='\\\\\\\\''judge'\\\\\\\\'',dict(j)\\n d=json.loads(c['\\\\\\\\''request_json'\\\\\\\\''])\\n return d,json.loads(c['\\\\\\\\''answer_json'\\\\\\\\''])\\nEVID=re.compile(r'\\\\\\\\''\\\"'^- (e'\\\"\\\\\\\\d+) \\\\\\\\[.*?(?=\\\"'^- e'\\\"\\\\\\\\d+ \\\\\\\\[|\\\\\\\\Z)'\\\\\\\\'',re.M|re.S)\\ndef evidence(t):\\n b=t.split('\\\\\\\\''[Evidence in view under this thesis, '\\\\\\\\'',1)[1].split('\\\\\\\\''\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n['\\\\\\\\'',1)[0]\\n m=dict((x.group(1),x.group(0).strip()) for x in EVID.finditer(b))\\n assert len(m)==int(b.split()[0]),(len(m),b[:20])\\n return m\\ndef user(d):\\n return next(m['\\\\\\\\''content'\\\\\\\\''] for m in d['\\\\\\\\''messages'\\\\\\\\''] if m['\\\\\\\\''role'\\\\\\\\'']=='\\\\\\\\''user'\\\\\\\\'')\\nUNIT=r'\\\\\\\\''(?:trillion(?:s)?|billions?|millions?|bn|mm|[BTM]|%|percent(?:age points?)?)'\\\\\\\\''\\nNUM=r'\\\\\\\\''\\\\\\\\d+(?:,\\\\\\\\d{3})*(?:\\\\\\\\.\\\\\\\\d+)?'\\\\\\\\''\\nFIG=re.compile(rf'\\\\\\\\''(?<\\\"'!['\\\"\\\\\\\\w.])(?P<sign>[+−-])?\\\\\\\\\\\"'$?'\\\"\\\\\\\\s*(?P<lo>{NUM})(?:\\\\\\\\s*[-–—]\\\\\\\\s*\\\\\\\\\\\"'$?'\\\"\\\\\\\\s*(?P<hi>{NUM}))?\\\\\\\\s*(?P<unit>{UNIT})(?\\\"'![a-zA-Z0-9])'\\\"'\\\\\\\\'',re.I)\\nMULT={'\\\\\\\\''trillion'\\\\\\\\'':1000,'\\\\\\\\''trillions'\\\\\\\\'':1000,'\\\\\\\\''t'\\\\\\\\'':1000,'\\\\\\\\''billion'\\\\\\\\'':1,'\\\\\\\\''billions'\\\\\\\\'':1,'\\\\\\\\''bn'\\\\\\\\'':1,'\\\\\\\\''b'\\\\\\\\'':1,'\\\\\\\\''million'\\\\\\\\'':D('\\\\\\\\''.001'\\\\\\\\''),'\\\\\\\\''millions'\\\\\\\\'':D('\\\\\\\\''.001'\\\\\\\\''),'\\\\\\\\''mm'\\\\\\\\'':D('\\\\\\\\''.001'\\\\\\\\''),'\\\\\\\\''m'\\\\\\\\'':D('\\\\\\\\''.001'\\\\\\\\'')}\\ndef figures(t,unit):\\n out=[]\\n for m in FIG.finditer(t or '\\\\\\\\'''\\\\\\\\''):\\n  u=m['\\\\\\\\''unit'\\\\\\\\''].lower()\\n  if (u in MULT)\\\"'!=(unit=='\\\"'\\\\\\\\''USD'\\\\\\\\''):continue\\n  mult=MULT.get(u,1)\\n  if m['\\\\\\\\''sign'\\\\\\\\''] in ('\\\\\\\\''-'\\\\\\\\'','\\\\\\\\''−'\\\\\\\\''):mult=-mult\\n  for g in ('\\\\\\\\''lo'\\\\\\\\'','\\\\\\\\''hi'\\\\\\\\''):\\n   if m[g]:out.append(D(m[g].replace('\\\\\\\\'','\\\\\\\\'','\\\\\\\\'''\\\\\\\\''))*mult)\\n return out\\ndef snippets(ed):\\n return [re.split(r'\\\\\\\\''\\\\\\\\n    (?:It replaces|Opinion, not verified:)'\\\\\\\\'',b,1)[0].split('\\\\\\\\''] '\\\\\\\\'',1)[1] for b in ed.values()]\\ndef prior_text(t):\\n return t.split('\\\\\\\\''[Previous conclusion'\\\\\\\\'',1)[1].split('\\\\\\\\''\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nAnswer per'\\\\\\\\'',1)[0].split('\\\\\\\\''] '\\\\\\\\'',1)[1]\\ndef tag(x,pattern): return bool(re.search(pattern,x or '\\\\\\\\'''\\\\\\\\'',re.I))\\ndef record(i):\\n v=db(i);a=db(i,'\\\\\\\\''archive'\\\\\\\\'')\\n return (v,a,v.execute(\\\\\\\"select j.*,k.unit from judgements j join view_keys k using(view_id) where k.unit in ('\\\\\\\\''USD'\\\\\\\\'','\\\\\\\\''percent'\\\\\\\\'') order by judgement_id\\\\\\\"))\\nfor i in (1,2,3):\\n v,a,rows=record(i)\\n C=collections.Counter(); first={}; prior={}; explicit=[]; matches={}\\n def tick(k,day):\\n  C[k]+=1\\n  first.setdefault(k,day)\\n def near(x,ys):\\n  return any(abs(x-y)<=D('\\\\\\\\''.005'\\\\\\\\'')*max(abs(x),abs(y),D('\\\\\\\\''.00000001'\\\\\\\\'')) for y in ys)\\n for j in rows:\\n  d,raw=req(a,j);t=user(d);e=evidence(t);u=j['\\\\\\\\''unit'\\\\\\\\'']; dy=j['\\\\\\\\''publication_day'\\\\\\\\''];id=j['\\\\\\\\''view_id'\\\\\\\\'']; key=(id,dy)\\n  assert all(raw[k]==j[k] for k in ('\\\\\\\\''rung'\\\\\\\\'','\\\\\\\\''reference'\\\\\\\\'','\\\\\\\\''implied_outcome'\\\\\\\\'')) and set(raw['\\\\\\\\''cites'\\\\\\\\''])<=set(e), (i,j['\\\\\\\\''call_id'\\\\\\\\''])\\n  vals=figures(j['\\\\\\\\''implied_outcome'\\\\\\\\''],u); ref=figures(j['\\\\\\\\''reference'\\\\\\\\''],u)\\n  s=snippets(e); shown=figures('\\\\\\\\''\\\\\\\\n'\\\\\\\\''.join(s),u); quotes=figures('\\\\\\\\''\\\\\\\\n'\\\\\\\\''.join(s1.split('\\\\\\\\''\\\\\\\\n    Quote: '\\\\\\\\'',1)[1] for s1 in s),u)\\n  tick('\\\\\\\\''all-'\\\\\\\\''+u,dy)\\n  if '\\\\\\\\''[Not shown:'\\\\\\\\'' in t:tick('\\\\\\\\''hidden'\\\\\\\\'',dy)\\n  if vals:\\n   tick('\\\\\\\\''parsed-'\\\\\\\\''+u,dy)\\n   if not near(vals[0],shown):tick('\\\\\\\\''lead no nearby-'\\\\\\\\''+u,dy)\\n   if not near(vals[0],quotes):tick('\\\\\\\\''lead no quote nearby-'\\\\\\\\''+u,dy)\\n   if not any(near(x,shown) for x in vals):tick('\\\\\\\\''no nearby at all-'\\\\\\\\''+u,dy)\\n   if any(not near(x,shown) for x in vals):tick('\\\\\\\\''at least one new-'\\\\\\\\''+u,dy)\\n  if id in prior:\\n   tick('\\\\\\\\''previous'\\\\\\\\'',dy)\\n   if ref:\\n    tick('\\\\\\\\''parsed-ref'\\\\\\\\'',dy)\\n    own=bool(prior[id]) and near(ref[0],prior[id][:1])\\n    no=not near(ref[0],shown)\\n    carried=tag(j['\\\\\\\\''reference'\\\\\\\\''],r'\\\\\\\\''\\\\\\\\b(?:previous|prior|carried)\\\\\\\\b'\\\\\\\\'')\\n    prev=near(ref[0],figures(prior_text(t),u))\\n    if own and no:tick('\\\\\\\\''own and no evidence'\\\\\\\\'',dy)\\n    if carried and no:tick('\\\\\\\\''carried and no evidence'\\\\\\\\'',dy)\\n    if carried and prev and no:\\n     tick('\\\\\\\\''carried prev no evidence'\\\\\\\\'',dy)\\n     explicit.append((id,dy,j['\\\\\\\\''call_id'\\\\\\\\''],j['\\\\\\\\''reference'\\\\\\\\'']))\\n    if carried and own and no:tick('\\\\\\\\''carried own no evidence'\\\\\\\\'',dy)\\n    if i==2 and id=='\\\\\\\\''v9'\\\\\\\\'' and dy in ('\\\\\\\\''2026-09-15'\\\\\\\\'','\\\\\\\\''2026-09-20'\\\\\\\\''):assert no and prev and (own if dy.endswith('\\\\\\\\''15'\\\\\\\\'') else carried)\\n  prior[id]=vals\\n  if (i,id,dy) in ((2,'\\\\\\\\''v9'\\\\\\\\'','\\\\\\\\''2026-09-20'\\\\\\\\''),(2,'\\\\\\\\''v14'\\\\\\\\'','\\\\\\\\''2026-09-20'\\\\\\\\''),(2,'\\\\\\\\''v29'\\\\\\\\'','\\\\\\\\''2026-09-20'\\\\\\\\''),(2,'\\\\\\\\''v6'\\\\\\\\'','\\\\\\\\''2026-09-19'\\\\\\\\''),(3,'\\\\\\\\''v41'\\\\\\\\'','\\\\\\\\''2026-09-20'\\\\\\\\'')):\\n   print('\\\\\\\\''control'\\\\\\\\'',i,id,dy,vals,[(str(x),near(x,shown)) for x in vals],ref)\\n print(i,dict(C),first)\\n print('\\\\\\\\''carried'\\\\\\\\'',explicit[:14],explicit[-4:])\\n'\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"\",\"exit_code\":null,\"status\":\"in_progress\"}}\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r45.stream:59:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_30\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \\\"python3 -B -c 'import sqlite3,json,pathlib,re,collections,decimal\\nD=decimal.Decimal\\ndef db(i,name='\\\\\\\\''views'\\\\\\\\''):\\n c=sqlite3.connect((pathlib.Path(f'\\\\\\\\''poc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/old-{i}/prod'\\\\\\\\'')/(name+'\\\\\\\\''.sqlite'\\\\\\\\'')).resolve().as_uri()+'\\\\\\\\''?mode=ro'\\\\\\\\'',uri=True)\\n c.row_factory=sqlite3.Row\\n return c\\ndef req(a,j):\\n c=a.execute('\\\\\\\\''select * from model_calls where call_id=?'\\\\\\\\'',(j['\\\\\\\\''call_id'\\\\\\\\''],)).fetchone()\\n assert c and c['\\\\\\\\''request_sha256'\\\\\\\\'']==j['\\\\\\\\''request_sha256'\\\\\\\\''] and c['\\\\\\\\''purpose'\\\\\\\\'']=='\\\\\\\\''judge'\\\\\\\\'',dict(j)\\n d=json.loads(c['\\\\\\\\''request_json'\\\\\\\\''])\\n return d,json.loads(c['\\\\\\\\''answer_json'\\\\\\\\''])\\nEVID=re.compile(r'\\\\\\\\''\\\"'^- (e'\\\"\\\\\\\\d+) \\\\\\\\[.*?(?=\\\"'^- e'\\\"\\\\\\\\d+ \\\\\\\\[|\\\\\\\\Z)'\\\\\\\\'',re.M|re.S)\\ndef evidence(t):\\n b=t.split('\\\\\\\\''[Evidence in view under this thesis, '\\\\\\\\'',1)[1].split('\\\\\\\\''\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n['\\\\\\\\'',1)[0]\\n m=dict((x.group(1),x.group(0).strip()) for x in EVID.finditer(b))\\n assert len(m)==int(b.split()[0]),(len(m),b[:20])\\n return m\\ndef user(d):\\n return next(m['\\\\\\\\''content'\\\\\\\\''] for m in d['\\\\\\\\''messages'\\\\\\\\''] if m['\\\\\\\\''role'\\\\\\\\'']=='\\\\\\\\''user'\\\\\\\\'')\\nUNIT=r'\\\\\\\\''(?:trillion(?:s)?|billions?|millions?|bn|mm|[BTM]|%|percent(?:age points?)?)'\\\\\\\\''\\nNUM=r'\\\\\\\\''\\\\\\\\d+(?:,\\\\\\\\d{3})*(?:\\\\\\\\.\\\\\\\\d+)?'\\\\\\\\''\\nFIG=re.compile(rf'\\\\\\\\''(?<\\\"'!['\\\"\\\\\\\\w.])(?P<sign>[+−-])?\\\\\\\\\\\"'$?'\\\"\\\\\\\\s*(?P<lo>{NUM})(?:\\\\\\\\s*[-–—]\\\\\\\\s*\\\\\\\\\\\"'$?'\\\"\\\\\\\\s*(?P<hi>{NUM}))?\\\\\\\\s*(?P<unit>{UNIT})(?\\\"'![a-zA-Z0-9])'\\\"'\\\\\\\\'',re.I)\\nMULT={'\\\\\\\\''trillion'\\\\\\\\'':1000,'\\\\\\\\''trillions'\\\\\\\\'':1000,'\\\\\\\\''t'\\\\\\\\'':1000,'\\\\\\\\''billion'\\\\\\\\'':1,'\\\\\\\\''billions'\\\\\\\\'':1,'\\\\\\\\''bn'\\\\\\\\'':1,'\\\\\\\\''b'\\\\\\\\'':1,'\\\\\\\\''million'\\\\\\\\'':D('\\\\\\\\''.001'\\\\\\\\''),'\\\\\\\\''millions'\\\\\\\\'':D('\\\\\\\\''.001'\\\\\\\\''),'\\\\\\\\''mm'\\\\\\\\'':D('\\\\\\\\''.001'\\\\\\\\''),'\\\\\\\\''m'\\\\\\\\'':D('\\\\\\\\''.001'\\\\\\\\'')}\\ndef figures(t,unit):\\n out=[]\\n for m in FIG.finditer(t or '\\\\\\\\'''\\\\\\\\''):\\n  u=m['\\\\\\\\''unit'\\\\\\\\''].lower()\\n  if (u in MULT)\\\"'!=(unit=='\\\"'\\\\\\\\''USD'\\\\\\\\''):continue\\n  mult=MULT.get(u,1)\\n  if m['\\\\\\\\''sign'\\\\\\\\''] in ('\\\\\\\\''-'\\\\\\\\'','\\\\\\\\''−'\\\\\\\\''):mult=-mult\\n  for g in ('\\\\\\\\''lo'\\\\\\\\'','\\\\\\\\''hi'\\\\\\\\''):\\n   if m[g]:out.append(D(m[g].replace('\\\\\\\\'','\\\\\\\\'','\\\\\\\\'''\\\\\\\\''))*mult)\\n return out\\ndef snippets(ed):\\n return [re.split(r'\\\\\\\\''\\\\\\\\n    (?:It replaces|Opinion, not verified:)'\\\\\\\\'',b,1)[0].split('\\\\\\\\''] '\\\\\\\\'',1)[1] for b in ed.values()]\\ndef prior_text(t):\\n return t.split('\\\\\\\\''[Previous conclusion'\\\\\\\\'',1)[1].split('\\\\\\\\''\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nAnswer per'\\\\\\\\'',1)[0].split('\\\\\\\\''] '\\\\\\\\'',1)[1]\\ndef tag(x,pattern): return bool(re.search(pattern,x or '\\\\\\\\'''\\\\\\\\'',re.I))\\ndef record(i):\\n v=db(i);a=db(i,'\\\\\\\\''archive'\\\\\\\\'')\\n return (v,a,v.execute(\\\\\\\"select j.*,k.unit from judgements j join view_keys k using(view_id) where k.unit in ('\\\\\\\\''USD'\\\\\\\\'','\\\\\\\\''percent'\\\\\\\\'') order by judgement_id\\\\\\\"))\\nfor i in (1,2,3):\\n v,a,rows=record(i)\\n C=collections.Counter(); first={}; prior={}; explicit=[]; matches={}\\n def tick(k,day):\\n  C[k]+=1\\n  first.setdefault(k,day)\\n def near(x,ys):\\n  return any(abs(x-y)<=D('\\\\\\\\''.005'\\\\\\\\'')*max(abs(x),abs(y),D('\\\\\\\\''.00000001'\\\\\\\\'')) for y in ys)\\n for j in rows:\\n  d,raw=req(a,j);t=user(d);e=evidence(t);u=j['\\\\\\\\''unit'\\\\\\\\'']; dy=j['\\\\\\\\''publication_day'\\\\\\\\''];id=j['\\\\\\\\''view_id'\\\\\\\\'']; key=(id,dy)\\n  assert all(raw[k]==j[k] for k in ('\\\\\\\\''rung'\\\\\\\\'','\\\\\\\\''reference'\\\\\\\\'','\\\\\\\\''implied_outcome'\\\\\\\\'')) and set(raw['\\\\\\\\''cites'\\\\\\\\''])<=set(e), (i,j['\\\\\\\\''call_id'\\\\\\\\''])\\n  vals=figures(j['\\\\\\\\''implied_outcome'\\\\\\\\''],u); ref=figures(j['\\\\\\\\''reference'\\\\\\\\''],u)\\n  s=snippets(e); shown=figures('\\\\\\\\''\\\\\\\\n'\\\\\\\\''.join(s),u); quotes=figures('\\\\\\\\''\\\\\\\\n'\\\\\\\\''.join(s1.split('\\\\\\\\''\\\\\\\\n    Quote: '\\\\\\\\'',1)[1] for s1 in s),u)\\n  tick('\\\\\\\\''all-'\\\\\\\\''+u,dy)\\n  if '\\\\\\\\''[Not shown:'\\\\\\\\'' in t:tick('\\\\\\\\''hidden'\\\\\\\\'',dy)\\n  if vals:\\n   tick('\\\\\\\\''parsed-'\\\\\\\\''+u,dy)\\n   if not near(vals[0],shown):tick('\\\\\\\\''lead no nearby-'\\\\\\\\''+u,dy)\\n   if not near(vals[0],quotes):tick('\\\\\\\\''lead no quote nearby-'\\\\\\\\''+u,dy)\\n   if not any(near(x,shown) for x in vals):tick('\\\\\\\\''no nearby at all-'\\\\\\\\''+u,dy)\\n   if any(not near(x,shown) for x in vals):tick('\\\\\\\\''at least one new-'\\\\\\\\''+u,dy)\\n  if id in prior:\\n   tick('\\\\\\\\''previous'\\\\\\\\'',dy)\\n   if ref:\\n    tick('\\\\\\\\''parsed-ref'\\\\\\\\'',dy)\\n    own=bool(prior[id]) and near(ref[0],prior[id][:1])\\n    no=not near(ref[0],shown)\\n    carried=tag(j['\\\\\\\\''reference'\\\\\\\\''],r'\\\\\\\\''\\\\\\\\b(?:previous|prior|carried)\\\\\\\\b'\\\\\\\\'')\\n    prev=near(ref[0],figures(prior_text(t),u))\\n    if own and no:tick('\\\\\\\\''own and no evidence'\\\\\\\\'',dy)\\n    if carried and no:tick('\\\\\\\\''carried and no evidence'\\\\\\\\'',dy)\\n    if carried and prev and no:\\n     tick('\\\\\\\\''carried prev no evidence'\\\\\\\\'',dy)\\n     explicit.append((id,dy,j['\\\\\\\\''call_id'\\\\\\\\''],j['\\\\\\\\''reference'\\\\\\\\'']))\\n    if carried and own and no:tick('\\\\\\\\''carried own no evidence'\\\\\\\\'',dy)\\n    if i==2 and id=='\\\\\\\\''v9'\\\\\\\\'' and dy in ('\\\\\\\\''2026-09-15'\\\\\\\\'','\\\\\\\\''2026-09-20'\\\\\\\\''):assert no and prev and (own if dy.endswith('\\\\\\\\''15'\\\\\\\\'') else carried)\\n  prior[id]=vals\\n  if (i,id,dy) in ((2,'\\\\\\\\''v9'\\\\\\\\'','\\\\\\\\''2026-09-20'\\\\\\\\''),(2,'\\\\\\\\''v14'\\\\\\\\'','\\\\\\\\''2026-09-20'\\\\\\\\''),(2,'\\\\\\\\''v29'\\\\\\\\'','\\\\\\\\''2026-09-20'\\\\\\\\''),(2,'\\\\\\\\''v6'\\\\\\\\'','\\\\\\\\''2026-09-19'\\\\\\\\''),(3,'\\\\\\\\''v41'\\\\\\\\'','\\\\\\\\''2026-09-20'\\\\\\\\'')):\\n   print('\\\\\\\\''control'\\\\\\\\'',i,id,dy,vals,[(str(x),near(x,shown)) for x in vals],ref)\\n print(i,dict(C),first)\\n print('\\\\\\\\''carried'\\\\\\\\'',explicit[:14],explicit[-4:])\\n'\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"1 {'all-USD': 737, 'parsed-USD': 736, 'lead no nearby-USD': 345, 'lead no quote nearby-USD': 389, 'no nearby at all-USD': 27, 'at least one new-USD': 524, 'previous': 821, 'parsed-ref': 798, 'hidden': 611, 'all-percent': 103, 'parsed-percent': 103, 'at least one new-percent': 66, 'own and no evidence': 4, 'lead no nearby-percent': 42, 'lead no quote nearby-percent': 42, 'carried and no evidence': 17, 'carried prev no evidence': 16, 'carried own no evidence': 1} {'all-USD': '2026-07-01', 'parsed-USD': '2026-07-01', 'lead no nearby-USD': '2026-07-01', 'lead no quote nearby-USD': '2026-07-01', 'no nearby at all-USD': '2026-07-01', 'at least one new-USD': '2026-07-01', 'previous': '2026-07-02', 'parsed-ref': '2026-07-02', 'hidden': '2026-07-07', 'all-percent': '2026-07-08', 'parsed-percent': '2026-07-08', 'at least one new-percent': '2026-07-08', 'own and no evidence': '2026-07-16', 'lead no nearby-percent': '2026-07-18', 'lead no quote nearby-percent': '2026-07-18', 'carried and no evidence': '2026-07-26', 'carried prev no evidence': '2026-07-26', 'carried own no evidence': '2026-08-02'}\\ncarried [('v2', '2026-07-26', 1919, 'No market consensus or NVIDIA guidance for the FY2027 outstanding total is supplied. The closest quantified disclosed baseline is $8.38 billion from the $3.5 billion added guarantee and Sharon AI’s $4.88 billion backstop, which sits in rung 4; the previous carried estimate including Firmus was about $11.5 billion, rung 5.'), ('v8', '2026-07-27', 2159, 'The carried-forward market-reference proxy is about $372.5 billion, in rung 2 ($350 billion to below $400 billion).'), ('v8', '2026-07-28', 2315, 'The carried-forward estimate is about $372.5 billion, in rung 2 ($350 billion to below $400 billion).'), ('v8', '2026-07-29', 2429, 'The carried-forward market estimate is about $372.5 billion, which is rung 2 ($350 billion to below $400 billion).'), ('v8', '2026-07-30', 2541, 'The carried-forward market estimate is about $372.5 billion, in rung 2 ($350 billion to less than $400 billion).'), ('v8', '2026-07-31', 2630, 'The carried-forward market estimate is about $372.5 billion, which sits in rung 2 ($350 billion to less than $400 billion).'), ('v1', '2026-08-02', 2692, 'No aggregate market consensus or NVIDIA guidance is supplied, so there is no external reference figure to place on the ladder. The carried base case of roughly $10–11 billion is in rung 4.'), ('v8', '2026-08-02', 2694, 'Analyst consensus is the reference; no numeric consensus is supplied in the current evidence. The carried comparison places it below the implied outcome, most consistently on rung 2 ($350bn to below $400bn).'), ('v1', '2026-08-03', 2728, 'No aggregate market consensus or NVIDIA guidance for total FY2027 credit-support obligations is supplied. The carried base estimate of about $10–11 billion is the available reference and sits in rung 4; the reported $250 billion Ohio proposal is not itself an established reference for committed obligations.'), ('v1', '2026-08-05', 2808, 'No aggregate market consensus or NVIDIA guidance for total FY2027 credit-support commitments is supplied. The carried base estimate of about $10–11 billion is rung 4; the reported $250 billion Ohio guarantee headline, if fully committed, would be in rung 5, but is not the most reliable reference for the committed amount by the due date.'), ('v8', '2026-08-05', 2805, 'Analyst consensus; no numeric figure is supplied in this view. The carried comparison places the reference most consistently in rung 2 ($350bn to below $400bn).'), ('v1', '2026-08-06', 2871, 'No explicit market consensus or aggregate NVIDIA guidance is supplied. The carried non-Ohio estimate of about $10–11 billion is rung 4; the carried estimate including a discounted Ohio contribution is about $20–21 billion, rung 5. The reported $250 billion Ohio figure, if taken in full, would also be rung 5 but is not the reference forecast used here.'), ('v8', '2026-08-09', 2975, 'Analyst consensus, as described in the previous conclusion, is $350bn to below $400bn: rung 2. No exact consensus estimate is supplied.'), ('v8', '2026-08-25', 4589, \\\"The carried-forward analyst-consensus reference is $350 billion to below $400 billion, rung 2. Morningstar's FY2027 estimate of $361 billion is likewise rung 2.\\\")] [('v8', '2026-08-09', 2975, 'Analyst consensus, as described in the previous conclusion, is $350bn to below $400bn: rung 2. No exact consensus estimate is supplied.'), ('v8', '2026-08-25', 4589, \\\"The carried-forward analyst-consensus reference is $350 billion to below $400 billion, rung 2. Morningstar's FY2027 estimate of $361 billion is likewise rung 2.\\\"), ('v8', '2026-08-26', 5093, \\\"Analyst consensus carried forward from the previous judgement is $350 billion to below $400 billion, rung 2. Morningstar's $361 billion FY2027 estimate is also in rung 2.\\\"), ('v8', '2026-08-27', 5304, \\\"The carried-forward market consensus is $350 billion to below $400 billion, which is rung 2; Morningstar's specific $361 billion FY2027 estimate is also rung 2.\\\")]\\ncontrol 2 v6 2026-09-19 [Decimal('1190.00'), Decimal('730'), Decimal('800'), Decimal('1300.0')] [('1190.00', False), ('730', True), ('800', True), ('1300.0', True)] [Decimal('1080.00'), Decimal('900'), Decimal('1100.0')]\\ncontrol 2 v14 2026-09-20 [Decimal('419'), Decimal('81.6'), Decimal('96.2'), Decimal('113.5'), Decimal('110.16'), Decimal('127')] [('419', False), ('81.6', True), ('96.2', True), ('113.5', True), ('110.16', True), ('127', False)] [Decimal('411'), 