ng run-rate is above \\nPAIR 2026-09-11 7915 7909  billion Q3 guidance and a 12% sequential Q4 carry imply about $406.8 billion before incremental upside. SemiAnalysis’s  ///  Center mix, plus roughly $112 billion for Q4 by carrying forward the guided 12.3% sequential growth.\\nPAIR 2026-09-12 8046 8045 8 billion and a 12% sequential carry into Q4, implies about $406.8 billion before the SemiAnalysis forecast of second-h  ///  h forward implies roughly $112 billion in Q4.\\nPAIR 2026-09-13 8146 8148 ide and approximately $120.96 billion for Q4 using the 12% sequential carry, gives about $406.8 billion before the disc  ///  g the guided 12.3% sequential growth into Q4 gives about $112.2 billion.\\nPAIR 2026-09-14 8311 8314 rst-half total plus the Q3 midpoint and a Q4 carry-forward of Q3's 12% sequential growth imply about $406.8 billion bef  ///  al growth implies about $112.2 billion in Q4.\\nPAIR 2026-09-15 8463 8456 beat evidence, and about $127 billion for Q4 if the 12% sequential growth assumption carries forward yield roughly $418  ///  l outlook at a 92.5% Data Center mix, and Q4 is approximately $112.2 billion carrying forward 12.3% sequential growth. |carrying forward 12.3% sequential growth. Q4 reacceleration and customer demand warrant a modest qualitative uplift, gi\\nPAIR 2026-09-16 8633 8629 4 billion Q3 and roughly $127–128 billion Q4 using 12% sequential growth yields about $418–420 billion. A discounted up  ///  ta Center mix) + about $112.2 billion for Q4 carrying forward 12.3% sequential growth. Q4 reacceleration supports a mod|carrying forward 12.3% sequential growth. Q4 reacceleration supports a modest qualitative uplift toward roughly $380 bi\\nPAIR 2026-09-17 8757 8750 114 billion Q3 and roughly 12% sequential Q4 growth implies about $418–420 billion before the second-half Data Center c  ///   guided 12.3% sequential growth rate into Q4 implies about $112.2 billion, with only a modest allowance for the stated |th only a modest allowance for the stated Q4 hyperscaler reacceleration.\\nPAIR 2026-09-18 8969 8967 ), then roughly 12% sequential growth for Q4, gives about $418–420 billion before the second-half data-center-compute a  ///  te forward implies about $112 billion for Q4, for roughly $376 billion in FY2027. The flat annualization of the first h\\nPAIR 2026-09-19 9077 9082 over guidance, and about $127 billion for Q4 carrying forward 12% sequential growth, plus approximately $27–28 billion   ///   is e3455), plus roughly $110 billion for Q4 as growth reaccelerates. This is an estimate, not a reported FY2027 outcom\\nPAIR 2026-09-20 9183 9177  beat, and approximately $127 billion for Q4 by carrying forward 12% sequential growth, then adding about $27–28 billio  ///  Center mix, plus roughly $110 billion for Q4 given expected reacceleration and the forecast of more than $100 billion.\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r45.stream:62:{\"type\":\"item.started\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_32\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \\\"python3 -B -c 'import sqlite3,json,pathlib,re,collections,decimal\\nD=decimal.Decimal\\ndef db(i,name='\\\\\\\\''views'\\\\\\\\''):\\n c=sqlite3.connect((pathlib.Path(f'\\\\\\\\''poc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/old-{i}/prod'\\\\\\\\'')/(name+'\\\\\\\\''.sqlite'\\\\\\\\'')).resolve().as_uri()+'\\\\\\\\''?mode=ro'\\\\\\\\'',uri=True)\\n c.row_factory=sqlite3.Row\\n return c\\ndef req(a,j):\\n c=a.execute('\\\\\\\\''select * from model_calls where call_id=?'\\\\\\\\'',(j['\\\\\\\\''call_id'\\\\\\\\''],)).fetchone()\\n assert c and c['\\\\\\\\''request_sha256'\\\\\\\\'']==j['\\\\\\\\''request_sha256'\\\\\\\\''] and c['\\\\\\\\''purpose'\\\\\\\\'']=='\\\\\\\\''judge'\\\\\\\\'',dict(j)\\n d=json.loads(c['\\\\\\\\''request_json'\\\\\\\\''])\\n return d,json.loads(c['\\\\\\\\''answer_json'\\\\\\\\''])\\nEVID=re.compile(r'\\\\\\\\''\\\"'^- (e'\\\"\\\\\\\\d+) \\\\\\\\[.*?(?=\\\"'^- e'\\\"\\\\\\\\d+ \\\\\\\\[|\\\\\\\\Z)'\\\\\\\\'',re.M|re.S)\\ndef evidence(t):\\n b=t.split('\\\\\\\\''[Evidence in view under this thesis, '\\\\\\\\'',1)[1].split('\\\\\\\\''\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n['\\\\\\\\'',1)[0]\\n m=dict((x.group(1),x.group(0).strip()) for x in EVID.finditer(b))\\n assert len(m)==int(b.split()[0]),(len(m),b[:20])\\n return m\\ndef user(d):\\n return next(m['\\\\\\\\''content'\\\\\\\\''] for m in d['\\\\\\\\''messages'\\\\\\\\''] if m['\\\\\\\\''role'\\\\\\\\'']=='\\\\\\\\''user'\\\\\\\\'')\\nUNIT=r'\\\\\\\\''(?:trillion(?:s)?|billions?|millions?|bn|mm|[BTM]|%|percent(?:age points?)?)'\\\\\\\\''\\nNUM=r'\\\\\\\\''\\\\\\\\d+(?:,\\\\\\\\d{3})*(?:\\\\\\\\.\\\\\\\\d+)?'\\\\\\\\''\\nFIG=re.compile(rf'\\\\\\\\''(?<\\\"'!['\\\"\\\\\\\\w.])(?P<sign>[+−-])?\\\\\\\\\\\"'$?'\\\"\\\\\\\\s*(?P<lo>{NUM})(?:\\\\\\\\s*[-–—]\\\\\\\\s*\\\\\\\\\\\"'$?'\\\"\\\\\\\\s*(?P<hi>{NUM}))?\\\\\\\\s*(?P<unit>{UNIT})(?\\\"'![a-zA-Z0-9])'\\\"'\\\\\\\\'',re.I)\\nMULT={'\\\\\\\\''trillion'\\\\\\\\'':1000,'\\\\\\\\''trillions'\\\\\\\\'':1000,'\\\\\\\\''t'\\\\\\\\'':1000,'\\\\\\\\''billion'\\\\\\\\'':1,'\\\\\\\\''billions'\\\\\\\\'':1,'\\\\\\\\''bn'\\\\\\\\'':1,'\\\\\\\\''b'\\\\\\\\'':1,'\\\\\\\\''million'\\\\\\\\'':D('\\\\\\\\''.001'\\\\\\\\''),'\\\\\\\\''millions'\\\\\\\\'':D('\\\\\\\\''.001'\\\\\\\\''),'\\\\\\\\''mm'\\\\\\\\'':D('\\\\\\\\''.001'\\\\\\\\''),'\\\\\\\\''m'\\\\\\\\'':D('\\\\\\\\''.001'\\\\\\\\'')}\\ndef figures(t,unit):\\n out=[]\\n for m in FIG.finditer(t or '\\\\\\\\'''\\\\\\\\''):\\n  u=m['\\\\\\\\''unit'\\\\\\\\''].lower()\\n  if (u in MULT)\\\"'!=(unit=='\\\"'\\\\\\\\''USD'\\\\\\\\''):continue\\n  mult=MULT.get(u,1)\\n  if m['\\\\\\\\''sign'\\\\\\\\''] in ('\\\\\\\\''-'\\\\\\\\'','\\\\\\\\''−'\\\\\\\\''):mult=-mult\\n  for g in ('\\\\\\\\''lo'\\\\\\\\'','\\\\\\\\''hi'\\\\\\\\''):\\n   if m[g]:out.append(D(m[g].replace('\\\\\\\\'','\\\\\\\\'','\\\\\\\\'''\\\\\\\\''))*mult)\\n return out\\ndef snippets(ed):\\n return [re.split(r'\\\\\\\\''\\\\\\\\n    (?:It replaces|Opinion, not verified:)'\\\\\\\\'',b,1)[0].split('\\\\\\\\''] '\\\\\\\\'',1)[1] for b in ed.values()]\\ndef prior_text(t):\\n return t.split('\\\\\\\\''[Previous conclusion'\\\\\\\\'',1)[1].split('\\\\\\\\''\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nAnswer per'\\\\\\\\'',1)[0].split('\\\\\\\\''] '\\\\\\\\'',1)[1]\\ndef tag(x,pattern): return bool(re.search(pattern,x or '\\\\\\\\'''\\\\\\\\'',re.I))\\ndef record(i):\\n v=db(i);a=db(i,'\\\\\\\\''archive'\\\\\\\\'')\\n return (v,a,v.execute(\\\\\\\"select j.*,k.unit from judgements j join view_keys k using(view_id) where k.unit in ('\\\\\\\\''USD'\\\\\\\\'','\\\\\\\\''percent'\\\\\\\\'') order by judgement_id\\\\\\\"))\\nfamilies={1:('\\\\\\\\''v28'\\\\\\\\'','\\\\\\\\''v7'\\\\\\\\'','\\\\\\\\''v44'\\\\\\\\''),2:('\\\\\\\\''v29'\\\\\\\\'','\\\\\\\\''v6'\\\\\\\\'',None),3:('\\\\\\\\''v33'\\\\\\\\'','\\\\\\\\''v7'\\\\\\\\'','\\\\\\\\''v41'\\\\\\\\'')}\\nfor i,ids in families.items():\\n v,a,_=record(i)\\n for id,f in zip(ids,('\\\\\\\\''equity'\\\\\\\\'','\\\\\\\\''capex'\\\\\\\\'','\\\\\\\\''vera'\\\\\\\\'')):\\n  if not id:continue\\n  rows=list(v.execute('\\\\\\\\''select * from judgements where view_id=? order by judgement_id'\\\\\\\\'',(id,)))\\n  hits=[]\\n  for j in rows:\\n   texts=[j[k] for k in ('\\\\\\\\''implied_outcome'\\\\\\\\'','\\\\\\\\''reference'\\\\\\\\'','\\\\\\\\''reasons'\\\\\\\\'')]\\n   if f=='\\\\\\\\''equity'\\\\\\\\'':\\n    hit=any(set([D(18),D(25),D(43)])<=set(figures(t,'\\\\\\\\''USD'\\\\\\\\'')) and tag(t,r'\\\\\\\\''(?:plus|add|sum|combin|\\\\\\\\+)'\\\\\\\\'') for t in texts)\\n   elif f=='\\\\\\\\''capex'\\\\\\\\'':\\n    hit=any(set([D(730),D(800),D(1300)])<=set(figures(t,'\\\\\\\\''USD'\\\\\\\\'')) and tag(t,r'\\\\\\\\''proxy|share|ratio|scal'\\\\\\\\'') for t in texts)\\n   else:\\n    hit=any(tag(t,r'\\\\\\\\''discount|haircut|trim'\\\\\\\\'') and bool(set(D(n) for n in (35,36,37,38,39,39.5))&set(figures(t,'\\\\\\\\''USD'\\\\\\\\''))) for t in texts)\\n   if hit:hits.append(j)\\n  print(i,id,f,len(rows),len(hits), '\\\\\\\\''dates'\\\\\\\\'',[j['\\\\\\\\''publication_day'\\\\\\\\''][5:] for j in hits])\\n  for j in hits[:1]+hits[-1:]:\\n   d,raw=req(a,j); t=user(d); ed=evidence(t)\\n   print(j['\\\\\\\\''call_id'\\\\\\\\''],j['\\\\\\\\''publication_day'\\\\\\\\''],j['\\\\\\\\''implied_outcome'\\\\\\\\''],j['\\\\\\\\''reference'\\\\\\\\''])\\n   for k in raw['\\\\\\\\''cites'\\\\\\\\'']:\\n    e=ed[k]\\n    if (f=='\\\\\\\\''equity'\\\\\\\\'' and any(x in figures(e,'\\\\\\\\''USD'\\\\\\\\'') for x in (D(18),D(25)))) or (f=='\\\\\\\\''capex'\\\\\\\\'' and any(x in figures(e,'\\\\\\\\''USD'\\\\\\\\'') for x in (D(730),D(1300)))) or (f=='\\\\\\\\''vera'\\\\\\\\'' and tag(e,'\\\\\\\\''doubl'\\\\\\\\'')):print(e[:440])\\n'\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"\",\"exit_code\":null,\"status\":\"in_progress\"}}\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r45.stream:63:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_32\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \\\"python3 -B -c 'import sqlite3,json,pathlib,re,collections,decimal\\nD=decimal.Decimal\\ndef db(i,name='\\\\\\\\''views'\\\\\\\\''):\\n c=sqlite3.connect((pathlib.Path(f'\\\\\\\\''poc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/old-{i}/prod'\\\\\\\\'')/(name+'\\\\\\\\''.sqlite'\\\\\\\\'')).resolve().as_uri()+'\\\\\\\\''?mode=ro'\\\\\\\\'',uri=True)\\n c.row_factory=sqlite3.Row\\n return c\\ndef req(a,j):\\n c=a.execute('\\\\\\\\''select * from model_calls where call_id=?'\\\\\\\\'',(j['\\\\\\\\''call_id'\\\\\\\\''],)).fetchone()\\n assert c and c['\\\\\\\\''request_sha256'\\\\\\\\'']==j['\\\\\\\\''request_sha256'\\\\\\\\''] and c['\\\\\\\\''purpose'\\\\\\\\'']=='\\\\\\\\''judge'\\\\\\\\'',dict(j)\\n d=json.loads(c['\\\\\\\\''request_json'\\\\\\\\''])\\n return d,json.loads(c['\\\\\\\\''answer_json'\\\\\\\\''])\\nEVID=re.compile(r'\\\\\\\\''\\\"'^- (e'\\\"\\\\\\\\d+) \\\\\\\\[.*?(?=\\\"'^- e'\\\"\\\\\\\\d+ \\\\\\\\[|\\\\\\\\Z)'\\\\\\\\'',re.M|re.S)\\ndef evidence(t):\\n b=t.split('\\\\\\\\''[Evidence in view under this thesis, '\\\\\\\\'',1)[1].split('\\\\\\\\''\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n['\\\\\\\\'',1)[0]\\n m=dict((x.group(1),x.group(0).strip()) for x in EVID.finditer(b))\\n assert len(m)==int(b.split()[0]),(len(m),b[:20])\\n return m\\ndef user(d):\\n return next(m['\\\\\\\\''content'\\\\\\\\''] for m in d['\\\\\\\\''messages'\\\\\\\\''] if m['\\\\\\\\''role'\\\\\\\\'']=='\\\\\\\\''user'\\\\\\\\'')\\nUNIT=r'\\\\\\\\''(?:trillion(?:s)?|billions?|millions?|bn|mm|[BTM]|%|percent(?:age points?)?)'\\\\\\\\''\\nNUM=r'\\\\\\\\''\\\\\\\\d+(?:,\\\\\\\\d{3})*(?:\\\\\\\\.\\\\\\\\d+)?'\\\\\\\\''\\nFIG=re.compile(rf'\\\\\\\\''(?<\\\"'!['\\\"\\\\\\\\w.])(?P<sign>[+−-])?\\\\\\\\\\\"'$?'\\\"\\\\\\\\s*(?P<lo>{NUM})(?:\\\\\\\\s*[-–—]\\\\\\\\s*\\\\\\\\\\\"'$?'\\\"\\\\\\\\s*(?P<hi>{NUM}))?\\\\\\\\s*(?P<unit>{UNIT})(?\\\"'![a-zA-Z0-9])'\\\"'\\\\\\\\'',re.I)\\nMULT={'\\\\\\\\''trillion'\\\\\\\\'':1000,'\\\\\\\\''trillions'\\\\\\\\'':1000,'\\\\\\\\''t'\\\\\\\\'':1000,'\\\\\\\\''billion'\\\\\\\\'':1,'\\\\\\\\''billions'\\\\\\\\'':1,'\\\\\\\\''bn'\\\\\\\\'':1,'\\\\\\\\''b'\\\\\\\\'':1,'\\\\\\\\''million'\\\\\\\\'':D('\\\\\\\\''.001'\\\\\\\\''),'\\\\\\\\''millions'\\\\\\\\'':D('\\\\\\\\''.001'\\\\\\\\''),'\\\\\\\\''mm'\\\\\\\\'':D('\\\\\\\\''.001'\\\\\\\\''),'\\\\\\\\''m'\\\\\\\\'':D('\\\\\\\\''.001'\\\\\\\\'')}\\ndef figures(t,unit):\\n out=[]\\n for m in FIG.finditer(t or '\\\\\\\\'''\\\\\\\\''):\\n  u=m['\\\\\\\\''unit'\\\\\\\\''].lower()\\n  if (u in MULT)\\\"'!=(unit=='\\\"'\\\\\\\\''USD'\\\\\\\\''):continue\\n  mult=MULT.get(u,1)\\n  if m['\\\\\\\\''sign'\\\\\\\\''] in ('\\\\\\\\''-'\\\\\\\\'','\\\\\\\\''−'\\\\\\\\''):mult=-mult\\n  for g in ('\\\\\\\\''lo'\\\\\\\\'','\\\\\\\\''hi'\\\\\\\\''):\\n   if m[g]:out.append(D(m[g].replace('\\\\\\\\'','\\\\\\\\'','\\\\\\\\'''\\\\\\\\''))*mult)\\n return out\\ndef snippets(ed):\\n return [re.split(r'\\\\\\\\''\\\\\\\\n    (?:It replaces|Opinion, not verified:)'\\\\\\\\'',b,1)[0].split('\\\\\\\\''] '\\\\\\\\'',1)[1] for b in ed.values()]\\ndef prior_text(t):\\n return t.split('\\\\\\\\''[Previous conclusion'\\\\\\\\'',1)[1].split('\\\\\\\\''\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nAnswer per'\\\\\\\\'',1)[0].split('\\\\\\\\''] '\\\\\\\\'',1)[1]\\ndef tag(x,pattern): return bool(re.search(pattern,x or '\\\\\\\\'''\\\\\\\\'',re.I))\\ndef record(i):\\n v=db(i);a=db(i,'\\\\\\\\''archive'\\\\\\\\'')\\n return (v,a,v.execute(\\\\\\\"select j.*,k.unit from judgements j join view_keys k using(view_id) where k.unit in ('\\\\\\\\''USD'\\\\\\\\'','\\\\\\\\''percent'\\\\\\\\'') order by judgement_id\\\\\\\"))\\nfamilies={1:('\\\\\\\\''v28'\\\\\\\\'','\\\\\\\\''v7'\\\\\\\\'','\\\\\\\\''v44'\\\\\\\\''),2:('\\\\\\\\''v29'\\\\\\\\'','\\\\\\\\''v6'\\\\\\\\'',None),3:('\\\\\\\\''v33'\\\\\\\\'','\\\\\\\\''v7'\\\\\\\\'','\\\\\\\\''v41'\\\\\\\\'')}\\nfor i,ids in families.items():\\n v,a,_=record(i)\\n for id,f in zip(ids,('\\\\\\\\''equity'\\\\\\\\'','\\\\\\\\''capex'\\\\\\\\'','\\\\\\\\''vera'\\\\\\\\'')):\\n  if not id:continue\\n  rows=list(v.execute('\\\\\\\\''select * from judgements where view_id=? order by judgement_id'\\\\\\\\'',(id,)))\\n  hits=[]\\n  for j in rows:\\n   texts=[j[k] for k in ('\\\\\\\\''implied_outcome'\\\\\\\\'','\\\\\\\\''reference'\\\\\\\\'','\\\\\\\\''reasons'\\\\\\\\'')]\\n   if f=='\\\\\\\\''equity'\\\\\\\\'':\\n    hit=any(set([D(18),D(25),D(43)])<=set(figures(t,'\\\\\\\\''USD'\\\\\\\\'')) and tag(t,r'\\\\\\\\''(?:plus|add|sum|combin|\\\\\\\\+)'\\\\\\\\'') for t in texts)\\n   elif f=='\\\\\\\\''capex'\\\\\\\\'':\\n    hit=any(set([D(730),D(800),D(1300)])<=set(figures(t,'\\\\\\\\''USD'\\\\\\\\'')) and tag(t,r'\\\\\\\\''proxy|share|ratio|scal'\\\\\\\\'') for t in texts)\\n   else:\\n    hit=any(tag(t,r'\\\\\\\\''discount|haircut|trim'\\\\\\\\'') and bool(set(D(n) for n in (35,36,37,38,39,39.5))&set(figures(t,'\\\\\\\\''USD'\\\\\\\\''))) for t in texts)\\n   if hit:hits.append(j)\\n  print(i,id,f,len(rows),len(hits), '\\\\\\\\''dates'\\\\\\\\'',[j['\\\\\\\\''publication_day'\\\\\\\\''][5:] for j in hits])\\n  for j in hits[:1]+hits[-1:]:\\n   d,raw=req(a,j); t=user(d); ed=evidence(t)\\n   print(j['\\\\\\\\''call_id'\\\\\\\\''],j['\\\\\\\\''publication_day'\\\\\\\\''],j['\\\\\\\\''implied_outcome'\\\\\\\\''],j['\\\\\\\\''reference'\\\\\\\\''])\\n   for k in raw['\\\\\\\\''cites'\\\\\\\\'']:\\n    e=ed[k]\\n    if (f=='\\\\\\\\''equity'\\\\\\\\'' and any(x in figures(e,'\\\\\\\\''USD'\\\\\\\\'') for x in (D(18),D(25)))) or (f=='\\\\\\\\''capex'\\\\\\\\'' and any(x in figures(e,'\\\\\\\\''USD'\\\\\\\\'') for x in (D(730),D(1300)))) or (f=='\\\\\\\\''vera'\\\\\\\\'' and tag(e,'\\\\\\\\''doubl'\\\\\\\\'')):print(e[:440])\\n'\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"1 v28 equity 35 8 dates ['09-07', '09-09', '09-15', '09-16', '09-17', '09-18', '09-19', '09-20']\\n7204 2026-09-07 Approximately $43 billion outstanding at the FY2027 annual report: carry forward the prior roughly $40 billion estimate based on the $25 billion disclosed balance and the $18 billion committed for the rest of FY2027, then modestly increase it for the newly reported $3 billion SB Energy investment, without counting the contingent lease assumption. The disclosed $25 billion of equity-investment commitments outstanding as of July 26, 2026; this is rung 1 (below $35 billion).\\n- e2766 [party_statement; NVIDIA Corporation; original source NVIDIA Corporation 2026-08-26; from edgar:NVDA:0001045810-26-000075:nvda-20260726.htm 2026-08-26] NVIDIA reported $99 billion of equity investments and $25 billion of equity investment commitments as of July 26, 2026.\\n    Quote: These include equity investments of $99 billion and equity investment commitments of $25 billion as of July 26, 2026.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the \\n- e3044 [party_statement; Business Insider; original source NVIDIA 2026-08-26; from gnews:aec1fae1b903de5c43ba7fdf 2026-08-26] NVIDIA said it had $18 billion committed to equity investments for the rest of FY2027, in addition to $47.9 billion already held in private companies.\\n    Quote: The company said Wednesday that it has $18 billion committed to equity investments for the rest of its fiscal year, on top of $47.9 billion it already \\n9016 2026-09-20 About $75 billion outstanding at the FY2027 annual report: use Bank of America’s approximately $70 billion commitment estimate as the anchor and allow a modest net increase for later disclosed deals, discounted for overlap and funding before the report. The company-based reference is about $43 billion ($25 billion of commitments as of July 26 plus $18 billion committed for the rest of FY2027), which is rung 2. No dated market consensus is supplied.\\n- e2766 [party_statement; NVIDIA Corporation; original source NVIDIA Corporation 2026-08-26; from edgar:NVDA:0001045810-26-000075:nvda-20260726.htm 2026-08-26] NVIDIA reported $99 billion of equity investments and $25 billion of equity investment commitments as of July 26, 2026.\\n    Quote: These include equity investments of $99 billion and equity investment commitments of $25 billion as of July 26, 2026.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the \\n- e3044 [party_statement; Business Insider; original source NVIDIA 2026-08-26; from gnews:aec1fae1b903de5c43ba7fdf 2026-08-26] NVIDIA said it had $18 billion committed to equity investments for the rest of FY2027, in addition to $47.9 billion already held in private companies.\\n    Quote: The company said Wednesday that it has $18 billion committed to equity investments for the rest of its fiscal year, on top of $47.9 billion it already \\n- e3481 [party_statement; ifre.com; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:3c6f653cbcaeacf9f11fa1fc 2026-08-28] NVIDIA expects to invest $25 billion of equity in suppliers and customers over the next few years.\\n    Quote: Nvidia said it expects to inject US$25bn of equity into its suppliers and customers over the next few years.\\n1 v7 capex 46 0 dates []\\n1 v44 vera 11 9 dates ['09-12', '09-13', '09-14', '09-15', '09-16', '09-17', '09-18', '09-19', '09-20']\\n7876 2026-09-12 About $35 billion for FY2028: take the stated $20 billion FY2027 potential times more than 2 as a nominal $40 billion-plus reference, then discount it because the evidence does not show the FY2028 volume in hand. No absolute-dollar market consensus is supplied. Management's stated potential—$20 billion in FY2027 and more than double that in FY2028—implies at least $40 billion, placing the reference at rung 1.\\n- e4641 [party_statement; fool.com (analyst); original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:3c5c71e12ed2a7001ce14f1a 2026-09-10] NVIDIA expects Vera CPU revenue in FY2028 to be double its FY2027 Vera CPU revenue.\\n    Quote: What's more, Nvidia expects its Vera CPU revenue to double next year.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e4712; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\n- e4712 [party_statement; fool.com (analyst), reporting Jensen Huang's Q2 investor conference call remarks; original source Jensen Huang, NVIDIA CEO 2026-08-26; from gnews:0ba93692dc5df4b999fe3729 2026-09-11] Jensen Huang expected NVIDIA CPU revenue to more than double in FY2028.\\n    Quote: Huang expects CPU revenue to more than double next fiscal year, making Nvidia one of the leading suppliers in the server CPU market.\\n    Opinion, no\\n- e4805 [party_statement; fool.com (Bram Berkowitz); original source NVIDIA management ; from gnews:c70bc12967b9b53426b5fb10 2026-09-12] NVIDIA management reiterated potential Vera CPU revenue of $20 billion in FY2027 and said it could more than double in FY2028.\\n    Quote: Management also reiterated that it still sees $20 billion in potential revenue from Vera CPUs in its current fiscal year, with the potential to more than double that\\n9020 2026-09-20 About $35 billion for FY2028: discount the management-stated $40 billion-plus potential for the absence of disclosed shipment volumes or realized Vera CPU revenue; full production and standalone sales support execution, while AMD’s reported benchmarks are a competitive risk. NVIDIA management’s potential $20 billion of Vera CPU revenue in FY2027 and potential to more than double it in FY2028 implies $40 billion-plus, which is rung 1.\\n- e4805 [party_statement; fool.com (Bram Berkowitz); original source NVIDIA management ; from gnews:c70bc12967b9b53426b5fb10 2026-09-12] NVIDIA management reiterated potential Vera CPU revenue of $20 billion in FY2027 and said it could more than double in FY2028.\\n    Quote: Management also reiterated that it still sees $20 billion in potential revenue from Vera CPUs in its current fiscal year, with the potential to more than double that\\n2 v29 equity 37 17 dates ['08-26', '08-27', '08-28', '08-29', '08-30', '08-31', '09-07', '09-08', '09-09', '09-10', '09-11', '09-12', '09-13', '09-14', '09-15', '09-19', '09-20']\\n4938 2026-08-26 About $43 billion: the $25 billion of commitments reported as of July 26 plus the $18 billion NVIDIA said was committed for the remainder of FY2027, treating the latter as incremental. This is an indicated gross total; the evidence does not establish that every earlier commitment remains outstanding at the annual-report date. Bank of America’s approximately $70 billion equity-investment estimate is the market-facing reference and sits at rung 3 ($50 billion to below $75 billion).\\n- e2620 [fact; NVIDIA Corporation; original source NVIDIA Corporation 2026-08-26; from edgar:NVDA:0001045810-26-000075:nvda-20260726.htm 2026-08-26] NVIDIA reported $99 billion of equity investments and $25 billion of equity investment commitments as of 2026-07-26.\\n    Quote: These include equity investments of $99 billion and equity investment commitments of $25 billion as of July 26, 2026.\\n- e2889 [party_statement; Business Insider, reporting NVIDIA's statement; original source NVIDIA 2026-08-26; from gnews:aec1fae1b903de5c43ba7fdf 2026-08-26] NVIDIA said on Wednesday that it has $18 billion committed to equity investments for the remainder of its fiscal year, in addition to $47.9 billion held in private companies.\\n    Quote: The company said Wednesday that it has $18 billion committed to equity investments for the rest o\\n8734 2026-09-20 About $53 billion: $25 billion of commitments reported as of July 26 plus $18 billion committed for the remainder of FY2027, then the $3.5 billion MediaTek investment announced after that remainder-of-year figure and a risk-adjusted contribution from the $10 billion Anthropic and $2.5 billion Thinking Machines discussions. Bank of America's roughly $70 billion estimate of NVIDIA's equity investments in ecosystem partners; this is rung 3 ($50 billion to below $75 billion). Its period and whether it measures outstanding commitments are unclear.\\n- e2620 [fact; NVIDIA Corporation; original source NVIDIA Corporation 2026-08-26; from edgar:NVDA:0001045810-26-000075:nvda-20260726.htm 2026-08-26] NVIDIA reported $99 billion of equity investments and $25 billion of equity investment commitments as of 2026-07-26.\\n    Quote: These include equity investments of $99 billion and equity investment commitments of $25 billion as of July 26, 2026.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read t\\n- e2889 [party_statement; Business Insider, reporting NVIDIA's statement; original source NVIDIA 2026-08-26; from gnews:aec1fae1b903de5c43ba7fdf 2026-08-26] NVIDIA said on Wednesday that it has $18 billion committed to equity investments for the remainder of its fiscal year, in addition to $47.9 billion held in private companies.\\n    Quote: The company said Wednesday that it has $18 billion committed to equity investments for the rest o\\n2 v6 capex 43 18 dates ['08-26', '08-28', '08-29', '08-30', '08-31', '09-01', '09-03', '09-04', '09-05', '09-06', '09-08', '09-09', '09-10', '09-11', '09-12', '09-15', '09-18', '09-19']\\n4915 2026-08-26 About $1.19 trillion for the four largest in calendar 2027: scale NVIDIA's $1.3 trillion top-five forecast by the approximate four-to-five-company ratio in the disclosed 2026 figures ($730 billion / $800 billion, or about 91%). This is a rough scope adjustment because the cited figures do not use perfectly identical spending definitions. Bank of America's reported $1.08 trillion calendar-2027 hyperscaler spending consensus is the market reference and sits in rung 3 ($900 billion to below $1.1 trillion).\\n- e1786 [third_party_view; Patrick Sanders, The Motley Fool; original source Amazon, Meta Platforms, Microsoft, and Alphabet ; from gnews:c8ac167e2356a75994ebc26f 2026-08-13] Amazon, Meta Platforms, Microsoft, and Alphabet indicated they expect combined AI-infrastructure spending to exceed $730 billion in calendar 2026 and increase in calendar 2027.\\n    Quote: Amazon , Meta Platforms , Microsoft , and Alphabet have indicated they will s\\n- e2535 [party_statement; Colette Kress; original source NVIDIA 2026-08-26; from truenorth:transcript:NVDA:2026-08-26 2026-08-26] NVIDIA said cloud-industry backlog exceeded $2 trillion and top-five hyperscaler capital expenditures were expected to approach $800 billion in 2026 and $1.3 trillion in 2027.\\n    Quote: With cloud industry backlog now greater than $2 trillion, CapEx by the top 5 hyperscalers is expected to reach nearly $800 \\n8595 2026-09-19 About $1.19 trillion for the four named hyperscalers: apply the prior approximate $730 billion/$800 billion four-to-five share proxy to NVIDIA’s $1.3 trillion top-five calendar-2027 CapEx estimate (e2535; repeated in e4756 and later reports). Calendar-2027 hyperscaler spending consensus is about $1.08 trillion (e1926), in rung 3 ($900 billion to below $1.1 trillion).\\n- e2535 [party_statement; Colette Kress; original source NVIDIA 2026-08-26; from truenorth:transcript:NVDA:2026-08-26 2026-08-26] NVIDIA said cloud-industry backlog exceeded $2 trillion and top-five hyperscaler capital expenditures were expected to approach $800 billion in 2026 and $1.3 trillion in 2027.\\n    Quote: With cloud industry backlog now greater than $2 trillion, CapEx by the top 5 hyperscalers is expected to reach nearly $800 \\n- e4756 [party_statement; barchart.com (analyst); original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:5adb2372d28f9339f479435d 2026-09-15] NVIDIA said the top five hyperscalers are expected to spend nearly $800 billion on capital expenditures in calendar 2026 and $1.3 trillion in calendar 2027.\\n    Quote: Nvidia's own earnings call also highlighted the scale of the spending cycle. The company said the top five hyperscalers are expected to spend nearly \\n- e4789 [party_statement; finance.yahoo.com author; original source NVIDIA management ; from gnews:3f21db1f9791e20f80909da8 2026-09-16] NVIDIA management pegged the top five hyperscalers' CapEx at nearly $800 billion in calendar 2026 and $1.3 trillion in calendar 2027.\\n    Quote: top-five hyperscaler CapEx management pegged at nearly $800 billion in 2026 and $1.3 trillion in 2027\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the s\\n- e4857 [party_statement; fool.com; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:4fbadb3b4cb5846297a34b0a 2026-09-16] NVIDIA estimates top-five hyperscaler capex could reach $1.3 trillion in calendar 2027, up from $800 billion in calendar 2026.\\n    Quote: Nvidia, for instance, estimates that the capex of the top five hyperscalers could increase to $1.3 trillion in 2027, up from $800 billion this year.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read \\n- e4990 [party_statement; fool.com (analyst); original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:ad94c78d09fe41fc3f29bbca 2026-09-18] NVIDIA projects the top five U.S. hyperscalers’ capital expenditure will reach $1.3 trillion in 2027.\\n    Quote: Nvidia projects that this figure will jump to $1.3 trillion in 2027.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e4756; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\n3 v33 equity 37 25 dates ['08-26', '08-27', '08-28', '08-29', '08-30', '08-31', '09-01', '09-03', '09-04', '09-05', '09-06', '09-07', '09-08', '09-09', '09-10', '09-11', '09-12', '09-13', '09-14', '09-15', '09-16', '09-17', '09-18', '09-19', '09-20']\\n5199 2026-08-26 About $43 billion: $25 billion of equity investment commitments reported as of July 26, 2026, plus the separately stated $18 billion committed for the rest of FY2027. This falls in rung 3, assuming those commitments remain reportable as outstanding or committed at the annual filing. No market consensus is supplied. NVIDIA’s stated $18 billion committed for the remainder of FY2027 is the company-plan reference and, taken alone, sits in rung 2. Bank of America’s approximately $70 billion estimate is a third-party view, not a consensus reference for outstanding commitments, and would sit in rung 5 if applied directly.\\n- e2841 [fact; NVIDIA Corporation; original source NVIDIA Corporation 2026-08-26; from edgar:NVDA:0001045810-26-000075:nvda-20260726.htm 2026-08-26] NVIDIA reported $99 billion of equity investments and $25 billion of equity investment commitments as of July 26, 2026.\\n    Quote: We have made, and may continue to make, investments and commitments in our ecosystem to enhance our growth opportunities, cultivate our ecosystem, and strengthe\\n- e3123 [party_statement; Business Insider, reporting NVIDIA's statement; original source NVIDIA 2026-08-26; from gnews:aec1fae1b903de5c43ba7fdf 2026-08-26] NVIDIA said it has $18 billion committed to equity investments for the remainder of FY2027, in addition to $47.9 billion in existing private-company holdings.\\n    Quote: The company said Wednesday that it has $18 billion committed to equity investments for the rest of its fiscal yea\\n9175 2026-09-20 Approximately $40–45 billion, centered near $43 billion: carry forward the reported $25 billion commitment balance together with the stated $18 billion remainder-of-FY2027 commitment, without adding later deal headlines that may overlap or count unfulfilled obligations as completed investments. This remains below the $50 billion rung-4 threshold. The company-based reference is approximately $43 billion: $25 billion of commitments as of July 26 plus $18 billion committed for the rest of FY2027. That reference sits in rung 3 ($30 billion to less than $50 billion).\\n- e2841 [fact; NVIDIA Corporation; original source NVIDIA Corporation 2026-08-26; from edgar:NVDA:0001045810-26-000075:nvda-20260726.htm 2026-08-26] NVIDIA reported $99 billion of equity investments and $25 billion of equity investment commitments as of July 26, 2026.\\n    Quote: We have made, and may continue to make, investments and commitments in our ecosystem to enhance our growth opportunities, cultivate our ecosystem, and strengthe\\n- e3123 [party_statement; Business Insider, reporting NVIDIA's statement; original source NVIDIA 2026-08-26; from gnews:aec1fae1b903de5c43ba7fdf 2026-08-26] NVIDIA said it has $18 billion committed to equity investments for the remainder of FY2027, in addition to $47.9 billion in existing private-company holdings.\\n    Quote: The company said Wednesday that it has $18 billion committed to equity investments for the rest of its fiscal yea\\n3 v7 capex 44 0 dates []\\n3 v41 vera 21 7 dates ['09-13', '09-15', '09-16', '09-17', '09-18', '09-19', '09-20']\\n8134 2026-09-13 High-$30 billions (roughly $38–39 billion): the more-than-$40-billion management target is discounted because the evidence does not show Vera shipment volume in hand. That estimate remains below the $40 billion rung-2 boundary. NVIDIA management's expectation that FY2028 CPU revenue will more than double FY2027's $20 billion level implies more than $40 billion, which is rung 2. No separate market consensus is supplied.\\n- e3660 [party_statement; Bram Berkowitz, fool.com, reporting Colette Kress's statement; original source NVIDIA CFO Colette Kress ; from gnews:fd25a8ea6f60290264bfbe55 2026-08-30] NVIDIA CFO Colette Kress said NVIDIA still expects $20 billion of CPU revenue in FY2027 and expects FY2028 CPU revenue to more than double that amount.\\n    Quote: The bad news for AMD and Intel is that Kress said Nvidia not only still expects $20 billion in CP\\n- e4691 [party_statement; fool.com (analyst); original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:3c5c71e12ed2a7001ce14f1a 2026-09-10] NVIDIA expects Vera CPU revenue in FY2028 to be double its FY2027 level.\\n    Quote: What's more, Nvidia expects its Vera CPU revenue to double next year.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e3660, e4764; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\n- e4764 [party_statement; fool.com (Keith Noonan); original source Jensen Huang ; from gnews:0ba93692dc5df4b999fe3729 2026-09-11] Jensen Huang forecast that NVIDIA CPU revenue would more than double in FY2028.\\n    Quote: Huang expects CPU revenue to more than double next fiscal year\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e4691; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\n- e4856 [party_statement; fool.com (analyst); original source NVIDIA management ; from gnews:c70bc12967b9b53426b5fb10 2026-09-12] NVIDIA management said Vera CPU revenue in FY2028 could be more than double the $20 billion potential it cited for FY2027.\\n    Quote: with the potential to more than double that number in fiscal year 2028.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e3660; the argument counts one cla\\n9166 2026-09-20 Roughly $38–39 billion for FY2028: the stated more-than-double expectation points above $40 billion, but is discounted for a forward Vera target without shipment volume in hand, with the competitive evidence adding execution risk. NVIDIA management’s stated expectation that FY2028 CPU revenue will more than double the $20 billion FY2027 expectation implies more than $40 billion, which is rung 2.\\n- e3660 [party_statement; Bram Berkowitz, fool.com, reporting Colette Kress's statement; original source NVIDIA CFO Colette Kress ; from gnews:fd25a8ea6f60290264bfbe55 2026-08-30] NVIDIA CFO Colette Kress said NVIDIA still expects $20 billion of CPU revenue in FY2027 and expects FY2028 CPU revenue to more than double that amount.\\n    Quote: The bad news for AMD and Intel is that Kress said Nvidia not only still expects $20 billion in CP\\n- e4691 [party_statement; fool.com (analyst); original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:3c5c71e12ed2a7001ce14f1a 2026-09-10] NVIDIA expects Vera CPU revenue in FY2028 to be double its FY2027 level.\\n    Quote: What's more, Nvidia expects its Vera CPU revenue to double next year.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e3660, e4764; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\n- e4764 [party_statement; fool.com (Keith Noonan); original source Jensen Huang ; from gnews:0ba93692dc5df4b999fe3729 2026-09-11] Jensen Huang forecast that NVIDIA CPU revenue would more than double in FY2028.\\n    Quote: Huang expects CPU revenue to more than double next fiscal year\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e4691; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\n- e4856 [party_statement; fool.com (analyst); original source NVIDIA management ; from gnews:c70bc12967b9b53426b5fb10 2026-09-12] NVIDIA management said Vera CPU revenue in FY2028 could be more than double the $20 billion potential it cited for FY2027.\\n    Quote: with the potential to more than double that number in fiscal year 2028.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e3660; the argument counts one cla\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r45.stream:72:{\"type\":\"item.started\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_37\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \\\"python3 -B -c 'import sqlite3,json,pathlib,re,collections,decimal\\nD=decimal.Decimal\\ndef db(i,name='\\\\\\\\''views'\\\\\\\\''):\\n c=sqlite3.connect((pathlib.Path(f'\\\\\\\\''poc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/old-{i}/prod'\\\\\\\\'')/(name+'\\\\\\\\''.sqlite'\\\\\\\\'')).resolve().as_uri()+'\\\\\\\\''?mo