ds_only:\n  f={f['\\\\''id'\\\\''] for f in d['\\\\''figures'\\\\'']}\n  for k,v,obj in fields(d):\n   if v is not None and v not in allowed(k,f,q): print('\\\\''BAD FIELD'\\\\'',k,repr(v),obj.get('\\\\''id'\\\\'',obj.get('\\\\''view_id'\\\\'')))\nshow('\\\\''answers'\\\\'',2,('\\\\''f_fy27_q3_guide'\\\\'','\\\\''f_fy27_q4_growth'\\\\'','\\\\''f_fy27_q4_est'\\\\'','\\\\''f_fy26_q4_est'\\\\'','\\\\''f_fy27_total_est'\\\\'','\\\\''f_fy27_q1'\\\\'','\\\\''f_fy27_q2'\\\\'','\\\\''f_fy27_dc_total_est'\\\\''),('\\\\''e2652'\\\\'','\\\\''e5162'\\\\'','\\\\''e4333'\\\\'','\\\\''e5204'\\\\'','\\\\''e111'\\\\'','\\\\''e2649'\\\\'','\\\\''e3346'\\\\'','\\\\''e4273'\\\\'')) \nshow('\\\\''answers'\\\\'',12,('\\\\''total_fy27_q3_guidance'\\\\'','\\\\''total_fy27_q4_implied'\\\\'','\\\\''dc_mix_latest'\\\\'','\\\\''dc_fy27_q3_forecast'\\\\'','\\\\''dc_fy27_q4_forecast'\\\\''),('\\\\''e2499'\\\\'','\\\\''e4333'\\\\'','\\\\''e2656'\\\\''))\nshow('\\\\''answers'\\\\'',24,(),('\\\\''e3660'\\\\'',))\nshow('\\\\''answers'\\\\'',22,(),('\\\\''e1926'\\\\'','\\\\''e2535'\\\\'','\\\\''e1786'\\\\''))'\"","aggregated_output":"\n answers 2 pair-old-1 joint 1 ERRORS [['C7', 'f_fy27_q3_guide: a figure needs either a value or a complete range with low at most high'], ['C7', 'f_fy26_q1_est refers to Estimate the prior-year quarter by dividing reported FY2027 Q1 revenue by 1 plus its reported year-over-year growth., which is not defined'], ['C7', 'f_fy26_q2_est refers to Estimate the prior-year quarter by dividing reported FY2027 Q2 revenue by 1 plus its reported year-over-year growth., which is not defined'], ['C7', 'f_fy26_q4_est refers to Estimate FY2026 Q4 as FY2026 full-year revenue less the three reconstructed or reported FY2026 Q1–Q3 amounts., which is not defined'], ['C7', 'f_fy27_q4_est refers to Apply the analyst-stated 65% year-over-year Q4 growth expectation to the estimated FY2026 Q4 base., which is not defined'], ['C7', 'f_fy27_total_est refers to Sum reported FY2027 Q1 and Q2, the Q3 guidance midpoint, and the estimated FY2027 Q4 amount., which is not defined'], ['C7', 'f_fy27_dc_q3_est refers to Multiply the Q3 total-revenue guidance midpoint by the latest reported Data Center share of total revenue., which is not defined'], ['C7', \"f_dc_q4_mix_est refers to Estimate a modest 0.5 percentage-point increase from the latest 92.5% Data Center mix, reflecting its recent upward trend and management's expectation of stronger hyperscale growth in Q4., which is not defined\"], ['C7', 'f_fy27_dc_q4_est refers to Multiply estimated FY2027 Q4 company revenue by the estimated 93% Data Center share., which is not defined']]\n{'id': 'f_fy27_q1', 'what': {'population': 'NVIDIA', 'measure': 'revenue', 'scope': 'company', 'period': 'FY2027 Q1'}, 'basis': 'reported', 'scenario': 'reported', 'kind': 'source', 'value': 81.62, 'unit': 'USD billions', 'evidence': 'NVIDIA reported fiscal Q1 2027 revenue of $81.62 billion.', 'expression': '$81.62 billion', 'component': 'value'}\n{'id': 'f_fy27_q2', 'what': {'population': 'NVIDIA', 'measure': 'revenue', 'scope': 'company', 'period': 'FY2027 Q2'}, 'basis': 'reported', 'scenario': 'reported', 'kind': 'source', 'value': 96.2, 'unit': 'USD billions', 'evidence': 'NVIDIA reported Q2 FY2027 revenue of $96.2 billion.', 'expression': '$96.2 billion', 'component': 'value'}\n{'id': 'f_fy27_q3_guide', 'what': {'population': 'NVIDIA', 'measure': 'revenue', 'scope': 'company', 'period': 'FY2027 Q3'}, 'basis': 'guidance', 'scenario': 'company guidance midpoint', 'kind': 'source', 'value': 108, 'low': 105.84, 'high': 110.16, 'bound': 'approx', 'unit': 'USD billions', 'evidence': 'NVIDIA guided Q3 FY2027 revenue to $108.0 billion, plus or minus 2%.', 'expression': '$108.0 billion, plus or minus 2%', 'component': 'midpoint'}\n{'id': 'f_fy26_q4_est', 'what': {'population': 'NVIDIA', 'measure': 'revenue', 'scope': 'company', 'period': 'FY2026 Q4'}, 'basis': 'forecast', 'scenario': 'reconstructed prior-year quarter', 'kind': 'estimate', 'value': 68.1, 'bound': 'approx', 'unit': 'USD billions', 'component': 'value', 'inputs': ['f_fy26_total', 'f_fy26_q1_est', 'f_fy26_q2_est', 'f_fy26_q3'], 'operation': 'sum', 'signs': [1, -1, -1, -1], 'relation': 'time_aggregation', 'bridge': 'Estimate FY2026 Q4 as FY2026 full-year revenue less the three reconstructed or reported FY2026 Q1–Q3 amounts.', 'basis_text': 'Residual of the FY2026 annual total after the first three quarters.', 'rests_on': ['e4273', 'e111', 'e2649', 'e3346']}\n{'id': 'f_fy27_q4_growth', 'what': {'population': 'NVIDIA', 'measure': 'revenue growth', 'scope': 'company', 'period': 'FY2027 Q4 year over year'}, 'basis': 'third_party', 'scenario': 'analyst expectation', 'kind': 'source', 'value': 65, 'unit': 'percent', 'evidence': 'Wall Street analysts expect NVIDIA revenue to grow 65% year over year in FY2027 Q4.', 'expression': '65% growth in Q4', 'component': 'value'}\n{'id': 'f_fy27_q4_est', 'what': {'population': 'NVIDIA', 'measure': 'revenue', 'scope': 'company', 'period': 'FY2027 Q4'}, 'basis': 'forecast', 'scenario': 'analyst growth carried forward', 'kind': 'estimate', 'value': 112.3, 'bound': 'approx', 'unit': 'USD billions', 'component': 'value', 'inputs': ['f_fy26_q4_est', 'f_fy27_q4_growth'], 'operation': 'apply_growth', 'bridge': 'Apply the analyst-stated 65% year-over-year Q4 growth expectation to the estimated FY2026 Q4 base.', 'basis_text': 'Family estimate using the Q4 analyst growth expectation and reconstructed prior-year-quarter base.', 'rests_on': ['e5162']}\n{'id': 'f_fy27_total_est', 'what': {'population': 'NVIDIA', 'measure': 'revenue', 'scope': 'company', 'period': 'FY2027'}, 'basis': 'forecast', 'scenario': 'reported first half, Q3 guidance midpoint, Q4 analyst growth', 'kind': 'estimate', 'value': 398.1, 'bound': 'approx', 'unit': 'USD billions', 'component': 'value', 'inputs': ['f_fy27_q1', 'f_fy27_q2', 'f_fy27_q3_guide', 'f_fy27_q4_est'], 'operation': 'sum', 'signs': [1, 1, 1, 1], 'relation': 'time_aggregation', 'bridge': 'Sum reported FY2027 Q1 and Q2, the Q3 guidance midpoint, and the estimated FY2027 Q4 amount.', 'basis_text': 'Family estimate. The quarter-based run-rate is given more weight than the reported 70% full-year growth characterization because the reported first-half results, Q3 guidance, and Q4 analyst growth assumption imply a higher annual total.', 'rests_on': ['e111', 'e2649', 'e2652', 'e5162', 'e3280']}\n{'id': 'f_fy27_dc_total_est', 'what': {'population': 'NVIDIA', 'measure': 'revenue', 'scope': 'Data Center', 'period': 'FY2027'}, 'basis': 'forecast', 'scenario': 'reported first half plus estimated second half', 'kind': 'estimate', 'value': 368.6, 'bound': 'approx', 'unit': 'USD billions', 'component': 'value', 'inputs': ['f_fy27_dc_h1', 'f_fy27_dc_q3_est', 'f_fy27_dc_q4_est'], 'operation': 'sum', 'signs': [1, 1, 1], 'relation': 'time_aggregation', 'basis_text': 'Family estimate. The Data Center forecast is calculated once from the reported first half and the estimated Q3 and Q4 segment amounts.', 'rests_on': ['e109', 'e2650', 'e3401', 'e3399', 'e3406', 'e5162']}\nANS {'view_id': 'v4', 'outcome': '$398.1 billion', 'reference': {'figure': 'Analyst consensus of $411 billion for FY2027 (e4333, e5204); it sits in rung 2 ($392 billion to below $431.2 billion).', 'unavailable': None}, 'cites': ['e4273', 'e111', 'e2649', 'e2652', 'e3346', 'e3280', 'e5162', 'e4333', 'e5204', 'e3399', 'e3406'], 'rung': 2}\nANS {'view_id': 'v8', 'outcome': '$368.6 billion', 'reference': {'figure': \"Morningstar's FY2027 Data Center estimate of $361 billion (e2295); it sits in rung 2 ($350 billion to below $400 billion). This is an analyst estimate, not a supplied consensus or company guidance figure.\", 'unavailable': None}, 'cites': ['e2295', 'e109', 'e2650', 'e2721', 'e2882', 'e3399', 'e3401', 'e3406', 'e5061', 'e5162'], 'rung': 2}\ne2652 QUOTE Revenue is expected to be $108.0 billion, plus or minus 2%. NVIDIA is not assuming any Data Center compute revenue from China in its outlook.\n  HEADER - e2652 [party_statement; NVIDIA Corporation; original source NVIDIA Corporation 2026-08-26; from nvidianews:nvidia-announces-financial-results-for-second-quarter-fiscal-2027 2026-08-26] NVIDIA guided Q3 FY2027 revenue to $108.0 billion, plus or minus 2%, with no Data Center compute revenue from China assumed.\ne5162 QUOTE and 65% growth in Q4.\n  HEADER - e5162 [third_party_view; fool.com author; original source Wall Street analysts ; from gnews:ea4633ed3e4ad9d71383673f 2026-09-17] Wall Street analysts expect NVIDIA revenue to grow 65% year over year in FY2027 Q4.\ne4333 QUOTE For FY 2027 (ending in January 2027), Wall Street analysts expect $411 billion in revenue.\n  HEADER - e4333 [third_party_view; fool.com (Keithen Drury); original source Wall Street analysts ; from gnews:7bf2e552fe4c58c4aeaf5b2e 2026-09-06] Wall Street analysts expect NVIDIA total revenue of $411 billion in FY2027.\ne5204 QUOTE financial analysts on average estimate will make $411 billion in revenue for its current fiscal year, according to Yahoo Finance\n  HEADER - e5204 [third_party_view; CRN, citing Yahoo Finance; original source Financial analysts surveyed by Yahoo Finance ; from gnews:3a284e233d8b31c62dc66b33 2026-09-18] Yahoo Finance's analyst consensus estimated NVIDIA FY2027 revenue at $411 billion.\ne111 QUOTE First-quarter fiscal 2027 revenues climbed 85% year over year to $81.62 billion, while non-GAAP earnings per share jumped 140% to $1.87.\n  HEADER - e111 [fact; tradingview.com; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:25d0b1d2a9dfe0bb99432e1a 2026-07-06] NVIDIA reported fiscal Q1 2027 revenue of $81.62 billion, up 85% year over year.\ne2649 QUOTE NVIDIA (NASDAQ: NVDA) today reported revenue for the second quarter ended July 26, 2026, of $96.2 billion, up 18% from the previous quarter and up 106% from a year ago.\n  HEADER - e2649 [fact; NVIDIA Corporation; original source NVIDIA Corporation 2026-08-26; from nvidianews:nvidia-announces-financial-results-for-second-quarter-fiscal-2027 2026-08-26] NVIDIA reported Q2 FY2027 revenue of $96.2 billion, up 18% quarter over quarter and 106% year over year.\ne3346 QUOTE For the third quarter, Nvidia expects revenue between $105.84 billion and $110.16 billion, representing year-over-year growth of 85.7% to 93.2% from the $57.01 billion reported in the same quarter last year.\n  HEADER - e3346 [party_statement; Benzinga; original source Nvidia ; from gnews:871ea3cb33e5728421ec2d5e 2026-08-28] Nvidia guided third-quarter revenue to $105.84 billion–$110.16 billion, implying 85.7%–93.2% year-over-year growth from $57.01 billion.\ne4273 QUOTE In fiscal 2026, which ended in January 2026, the growth rate moderated to 65%, while revenue reached $215.9 billion.\n  HEADER - e4273 [fact; calcalistech.com; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:478c25b436f87e8f421d54ed 2026-09-06] NVIDIA reported FY2026 revenue of $215.9 billion, up 65% year over year.\n\n answers 12 pair-old-2 separate-v9 1 ERRORS [['C7', 'total_fy27_q3_guidance: a figure needs either a value or a complete range with low at most high'], ['C7', 'total_fy27_q4_implied: difference takes 2 operands, not 4'], ['C7', 'total_fy27_q4_implied: signs must give one +1 or -1 per operand of a sum or roll_forward'], ['C7', 'dc_fy27_q3_forecast refers to Estimate Q3 Data Center revenue by applying the latest reported 92.5% Data Center share to the $108 billion Q3 total-revenue guidance., which is not defined'], ['C7', 'dc_fy27_q4_forecast refers to Estimate Q4 Data Center revenue by applying the latest reported 92.5% Data Center share to the $125.2 billion Q4 company-revenue residual., which is not defined']]\n{'id': 'total_fy27_q3_guidance', 'what': {'population': 'NVIDIA', 'measure': 'revenue', 'scope': 'company', 'period': 'FY2027 Q3'}, 'basis': 'guidance', 'scenario': 'base', 'kind': 'source', 'value': 108, 'low': 105.84, 'high': 110.16, 'bound': 'approx', 'unit': 'USD billions', 'evidence': 'NVIDIA guided Q3 FY2027 revenue to $108.0 billion, plus or minus 2%.', 'expression': '$108.0 billion, plus or minus 2%', 'component': 'value'}\n{'id': 'total_fy27_q4_implied', 'what': {'population': 'NVIDIA', 'measure': 'revenue', 'scope': 'company', 'period': 'FY2027 Q4'}, 'basis': 'forecast', 'scenario': 'base', 'kind': 'computed', 'value': 125.2, 'unit': 'USD billions', 'evidence': 'Implied residual from FY2027 total-revenue consensus less reported Q1 and Q2 revenue and Q3 guidance.', 'component': 'value', 'inputs': ['total_fy27_consensus', 'total_fy27_q1_reported', 'total_fy27_q2_reported', 'total_fy27_q3_guidance'], 'operation': 'difference', 'signs': [1, -1, -1, -1], 'relation': 'time_aggregation'}\n{'id': 'dc_mix_latest', 'what': {'population': 'NVIDIA', 'measure': 'share of company revenue', 'scope': 'Data Center', 'period': 'FY2027 Q2'}, 'basis': 'third_party', 'scenario': 'base', 'kind': 'source', 'value': 92.5, 'unit': 'percent', 'evidence': 'Data Center revenue rose to 92.5% of NVIDIA total revenue in FY2027 Q2.', 'expression': '92.5%', 'component': 'value'}\n{'id': 'dc_fy27_q3_forecast', 'what': {'population': 'NVIDIA', 'measure': 'revenue', 'scope': 'Data Center', 'period': 'FY2027 Q3'}, 'basis': 'forecast', 'scenario': 'base', 'kind': 'estimate', 'value': 99.9, 'unit': 'USD billions', 'evidence': 'Estimate: applying the latest reported Data Center mix to Q3 revenue guidance gives approximately $99.9 billion; the mix is an assumption, not Q3 reported fact.', 'component': 'value', 'inputs': ['total_fy27_q3_guidance', 'dc_mix_latest'], 'operation': 'share', 'bridge': 'Estimate Q3 Data Center revenue by applying the latest reported 92.5% Data Center share to the $108 billion Q3 total-revenue guidance.'}\n{'id': 'dc_fy27_q4_forecast', 'what': {'population': 'NVIDIA', 'measure': 'revenue', 'scope': 'Data Center', 'period': 'FY2027 Q4'}, 'basis': 'forecast', 'scenario': 'base', 'kind': 'estimate', 'value': 115.8, 'unit': 'USD billions', 'evidence': 'Estimate: apply the latest reported Data Center mix to the implied Q4 company-revenue residual.', 'component': 'value', 'inputs': ['total_fy27_q4_implied', 'dc_mix_latest'], 'operation': 'share', 'bridge': 'Estimate Q4 Data Center revenue by applying the latest reported 92.5% Data Center share to the $125.2 billion Q4 company-revenue residual.'}\nANS {'view_id': 'v9', 'outcome': 'Approximately $380 billion of FY2027 Data Center segment revenue', 'reference': {'figure': 'Morningstar estimated NVIDIA FY2027 Data Center revenue would be “well over $300 billion”; that lower threshold is rung 4, though the wording does not pin down a more precise rung.', 'unavailable': None}, 'cites': ['e4995', 'e3216', 'e3219', 'e2499', 'e4097', 'e238', 'e2497', 'e3222', 'e2572', 'e2562', 'e2705'], 'rung': 3}\ne2499 QUOTE Revenue is expected to be $108.0 billion, plus or minus 2%. NVIDIA is not assuming any Data Center compute revenue from China in its outlook.\n  HEADER - e2499 [party_statement; NVIDIA Corporation; original source NVIDIA Corporation 2026-08-26; from nvidianews:nvidia-announces-financial-results-for-second-quarter-fiscal-2027 2026-08-26] NVIDIA guided Q3 FY2027 revenue to $108.0 billion, plus or minus 2%, assuming no Data Center compute revenue from China.\n\n answers 24 single-E single 1 ERRORS [['C7', 'f4: a figure needs either a value or a complete range with low at most high']]\n{'id': 'f1', 'what': {'population': 'NVIDIA', 'measure': 'revenue', 'scope': 'Vera CPU', 'period': 'FY2027'}, 'basis': 'guidance', 'scenario': \"NVIDIA's stated FY2027 base for its Vera CPU revenue expectation\", 'kind': 'source', 'value': 20, 'bound': 'approx', 'unit': 'USD billions', 'evidence': 'NVIDIA expects $20 billion in FY2027 CPU revenue; management also describes this as the FY2027 potential for Vera CPU.', 'expression': '$20 billion', 'component': 'value', 'basis_text': 'e3660 and e4856'}\n{'id': 'f2', 'what': {'population': 'NVIDIA', 'measure': 'revenue growth multiplier', 'scope': 'Vera CPU', 'period': 'FY2028 relative to FY2027'}, 'basis': 'guidance', 'scenario': \"NVIDIA's stated FY2028 growth expectation\", 'kind': 'source', 'value': 2, 'bound': '>', 'unit': 'times', 'evidence': 'Management said FY2028 Vera CPU revenue could be more than double the FY2027 potential.', 'expression': 'more than double the $20 billion potential', 'component': 'multiplier', 'basis_text': 'e4856'}\n{'id': 'f3', 'what': {'population': 'NVIDIA', 'measure': 'revenue', 'scope': 'Vera CPU', 'period': 'FY2028'}, 'basis': 'guidance', 'scenario': 'Revenue floor implied by the stated FY2027 base and FY2028 multiplier', 'kind': 'computed', 'value': 40, 'bound': '>', 'unit': 'USD billions', 'component': 'bound', 'inputs': ['f1', 'f2'], 'operation': 'product'}\n{'id': 'f4', 'what': {'population': 'NVIDIA', 'measure': 'revenue', 'scope': 'Vera CPU', 'period': 'FY2028'}, 'basis': 'forecast', 'scenario': 'Most likely outcome, allowing for some execution discount to the forward-looking potential', 'kind': 'estimate', 'value': 42, 'low': 40, 'high': 50, 'bound': 'approx', 'unit': 'USD billions', 'component': 'value', 'rests_on': ['f3'], 'adjusts': {'figure': 'f3', 'type': 'discount'}}\nANS {'view_id': 'v41', 'outcome': 'Approximately $42 billion of NVIDIA Vera CPU revenue in FY2028.', 'reference': {'figure': \"NVIDIA's expectation to more than double the FY2027 $20 billion base implies more than $40 billion for FY2028, which places the stated reference at rung 2 (e3660, e4856). No analyst consensus figure is supplied.\", 'unavailable': None}, 'cites': ['e3660', 'e4687', 'e4689', 'e4691', 'e4692', 'e4856', 'e4857', 'e5044', 'e5399', 'e5400', 'e5401', 'e5402', 'e5403', 'e5404'], 'rung': 2}\ne3660 QUOTE The bad news for AMD and Intel is that Kress said Nvidia not only still expects $20 billion in CPU revenue in its fiscal 2027, but expects that number to more than double in fiscal 2028.\n  HEADER - e3660 [party_statement; Bram Berkowitz, fool.com, reporting Colette Kress's statement; original source NVIDIA CFO Colette Kress ; from gnews:fd25a8ea6f60290264bfbe55 2026-08-30] NVIDIA CFO Colette Kress said NVIDIA still expects $20 billion of CPU revenue in FY2027 and expects FY2028 CPU revenue to more than double that amount.\n\n answers 22 single-S single 1 ERRORS [['C7', 'fig_v6_forecast refers to My estimate translates the top-five all-capex estimate to the four-largest-hyperscaler data-center-capex question. It allows for the fifth company and for the difference between total capital expenditures and data-center capital expenditures; the evidence does not quantify either adjustment precisely., which is not defined']]\n{'id': 'fig_consensus_2027', 'what': {'population': 'hyperscalers', 'measure': 'capital expenditures', 'scope': 'combined', 'period': 'CY2027'}, 'basis': 'consensus', 'scenario': 'market reference', 'kind': 'source', 'value': 1080, 'bound': 'approx', 'unit': 'USD billions', 'evidence': 'Bank of America reported analyst consensus for hyperscalers’ calendar 2027 spending.', 'expression': '$1.08 trillion', 'component': 'value', 'basis_text': 'Analyst consensus as reported by Bank of America.'}\n{'id': 'fig_nvidia_top_five_2027', 'what': {'population': 'top five hyperscalers', 'measure': 'capital expenditures', 'scope': 'combined', 'period': 'CY2027'}, 'basis': 'third_party', 'scenario': 'NVIDIA estimate', 'kind': 'source', 'value': 1300, 'bound': 'approx', 'unit': 'USD billions', 'evidence': 'NVIDIA said the top five hyperscalers are expected to spend nearly $800 billion on capital expenditures in calendar 2026 and $1.3 trillion in calendar 2027.', 'expression': '$1.3 trillion', 'component': 'value', 'basis_text': 'NVIDIA estimate, not a reported outcome.'}\n{'id': 'fig_v6_forecast', 'what': {'population': 'four largest AI hyperscalers', 'measure': 'data-center capex', 'scope': 'combined', 'period': 'CY2027'}, 'basis': 'forecast', 'scenario': 'most likely outcome', 'kind': 'estimate', 'value': 1110, 'bound': 'approx', 'unit': 'USD billions', 'inputs': ['fig_consensus_2027', 'fig_nvidia_top_five_2027'], 'bridge': 'My estimate translates the top-five all-capex estimate to the four-largest-hyperscaler data-center-capex question. It allows for the fifth company and for the difference between total capital expenditures and data-center capital expenditures; the evidence does not quantify either adjustment precisely.', 'basis_text': 'My forecast is approximately $1.11 trillion.', 'rests_on': ['fig_consensus_2027', 'fig_nvidia_top_five_2027'], 'adjusts': {'figure': 'fig_nvidia_top_five_2027', 'type': 'trim'}, 'converts': ['top-five hyperscaler capital expenditures', \"four largest hyperscalers' data-center capital expenditures\"]}\nANS {'view_id': 'v6', 'outcome': 'About $1.11 trillion in combined data-center capital expenditures in CY2027.', 'reference': {'figure': 'fig_consensus_2027: approximately $1.08 trillion, which is rung 3 on this ladder.', 'unavailable': None}, 'cites': ['e1926', 'e2535', 'e1076', 'e1366', 'e3391', 'e3645', 'e3646', 'e46'], 'rung': 4}\ne1926 QUOTE What analysts expect the hyperscalers to spend in 2027 alone has more than doubled in the space of a year, from a consensus of $480 billion (€416bn) in August 2025 to $1.08 trillion (€943bn) this month, a rise of about 127%, according to Bank of America.\n  HEADER - e1926 [third_party_view; uk.finance.yahoo.com, citing Bank of America; original source Bank of America ; from gnews:1219126db2e6631aa1264142 2026-08-16] Bank of America said analyst consensus for hyperscalers’ calendar 2027 spending rose from $480 billion in August 2025 to $1.08 trillion in August 2026, an increase of about 127%.\ne2535 QUOTE With cloud industry backlog now greater than $2 trillion, CapEx by the top 5 hyperscalers is expected to reach nearly $800 billion in 2026 and $1.3 trillion in 2027.\n  HEADER - e2535 [party_statement; Colette Kress; original source NVIDIA 2026-08-26; from truenorth:transcript:NVDA:2026-08-26 2026-08-26] NVIDIA said cloud-industry backlog exceeded $2 trillion and top-five hyperscaler capital expenditures were expected to approach $800 billion in 2026 and $1.3 trillion in 2027.\ne1786 QUOTE Amazon , Meta Platforms , Microsoft , and Alphabet have indicated they will spend more than $730 billion combined on AI infrastructure this year, and they expect that number to increase next year.\n  HEADER - e1786 [third_party_view; Patrick Sanders, The Motley Fool; original source Amazon, Meta Platforms, Microsoft, and Alphabet ; from gnews:c8ac167e2356a75994ebc26f 2026-08-13] Amazon, Meta Platforms, Microsoft, and Alphabet indicated they expect combined AI-infrastructure spending to exceed $730 billion in calendar 2026 and increase in calendar 2027.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
