fy27_q3_guidance: a figure needs either a value or a complete range with low at most high'], ['C7', 'total_fy27_q4_implied: difference takes 2 operands, not 4'], ['C7', 'total_fy27_q4_implied: signs must give one +1 or -1 per operand of a sum or roll_forward'], ['C7', 'dc_fy27_q3_forecast refers to Estimate Q3 Data Center revenue by applying the latest reported 92.5% Data Center share to the $108 billion Q3 total-revenue guidance., which is not defined'], ['C7', 'dc_fy27_q4_forecast refers to Estimate Q4 Data Center revenue by applying the latest reported 92.5% Data Center share to the $125.2 billion Q4 company-revenue residual., which is not defined']]\n{'id': 'total_fy27_q1_reported', 'what': {'population': 'NVIDIA', 'measure': 'revenue', 'scope': 'company', 'period': 'FY2027 Q1'}, 'basis': 'reported', 'scenario': 'base', 'kind': 'source', 'value': 81.6, 'unit': 'USD billions', 'evidence': 'NVIDIA reported fiscal Q1 2027 total revenue of $81.6 billion.', 'expression': '$81.6 billion', 'component': 'value'}\n{'id': 'total_fy27_q2_reported', 'what': {'population': 'NVIDIA', 'measure': 'revenue', 'scope': 'company', 'period': 'FY2027 Q2'}, 'basis': 'reported', 'scenario': 'base', 'kind': 'source', 'value': 96.2, 'unit': 'USD billions', 'evidence': 'NVIDIA reported Q2 FY2027 revenue of $96.2 billion.', 'expression': '$96.2 billion', 'component': 'value'}\n{'id': 'total_fy27_q3_guidance', 'what': {'population': 'NVIDIA', 'measure': 'revenue', 'scope': 'company', 'period': 'FY2027 Q3'}, 'basis': 'guidance', 'scenario': 'base', 'kind': 'source', 'value': 108, 'low': 105.84, 'high': 110.16, 'bound': 'approx', 'unit': 'USD billions', 'evidence': 'NVIDIA guided Q3 FY2027 revenue to $108.0 billion, plus or minus 2%.', 'expression': '$108.0 billion, plus or minus 2%', 'component': 'value'}\n{'id': 'total_fy27_consensus', 'what': {'population': 'NVIDIA', 'measure': 'revenue', 'scope': 'company', 'period': 'FY2027'}, 'basis': 'consensus', 'scenario': 'market reference', 'kind': 'source', 'value': 411, 'unit': 'USD billions', 'evidence': 'Wall Street analysts expect NVIDIA total revenue of $411 billion in FY2027.', 'expression': '$411 billion', 'component': 'value'}\nANS {'view_id': 'v9', 'outcome': 'Approximately $380 billion of FY2027 Data Center segment revenue', 'reference': {'figure': 'Morningstar estimated NVIDIA FY2027 Data Center revenue would be “well over $300 billion”; that lower threshold is rung 4, though the wording does not pin down a more precise rung.', 'unavailable': None}, 'cites': ['e4995', 'e3216', 'e3219', 'e2499', 'e4097', 'e238', 'e2497', 'e3222', 'e2572', 'e2562', 'e2705'], 'rung': 3}\ne238 QUOTE For the first quarter of fiscal 2027, revenue jumped 85% year-over-year (YOY) to $81.6 billion, easily beating analyst expectations.\n  HEADER - e238 [fact; barchart.com (analyst); original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:82472d26336e1982cf8a3eff 2026-07-12] NVIDIA reported fiscal Q1 2027 total revenue of $81.6 billion, up 85% year over year.\ne2497 QUOTE NVIDIA (NASDAQ: NVDA) today reported revenue for the second quarter ended July 26, 2026, of $96.2 billion, up 18% from the previous quarter and up 106% from a year ago.\n  HEADER - e2497 [fact; NVIDIA Corporation; original source NVIDIA Corporation 2026-08-26; from nvidianews:nvidia-announces-financial-results-for-second-quarter-fiscal-2027 2026-08-26] NVIDIA reported Q2 FY2027 revenue of $96.2 billion, up 18% quarter over quarter and 106% year over year.\ne2499 QUOTE Revenue is expected to be $108.0 billion, plus or minus 2%. NVIDIA is not assuming any Data Center compute revenue from China in its outlook.\n  HEADER - e2499 [party_statement; NVIDIA Corporation; original source NVIDIA Corporation 2026-08-26; from nvidianews:nvidia-announces-financial-results-for-second-quarter-fiscal-2027 2026-08-26] NVIDIA guided Q3 FY2027 revenue to $108.0 billion, plus or minus 2%, assuming no Data Center compute revenue from China.\ne4097 QUOTE For FY 2027 (ending in January 2027), Wall Street analysts expect $411 billion in revenue.\n  HEADER - e4097 [third_party_view; Keithen Drury, fool.com; original source Wall Street analysts ; from gnews:7bf2e552fe4c58c4aeaf5b2e 2026-09-06] Wall Street analysts expect NVIDIA total revenue of $411 billion in FY2027.\n\n answers 4 pair-old-1 separate-v4 1 ERRORS [['C7', 'q3_fy2027_guidance: a figure needs either a value or a complete range with low at most high']]\n{'id': 'q4_fy2026_actual', 'what': {'population': 'NVIDIA', 'measure': 'revenue', 'scope': 'company', 'period': 'FY2026 Q4'}, 'basis': 'reported', 'scenario': 'reported actual', 'kind': 'source', 'value': 68, 'unit': 'USD billions', 'evidence': 'e2452', 'expression': '$68 billion', 'component': 'value'}\n{'id': 'q4_fy2027_yoy_growth', 'what': {'population': 'NVIDIA', 'measure': 'revenue year-over-year growth', 'scope': 'company', 'period': 'FY2027 Q4'}, 'basis': 'third_party', 'scenario': 'analyst expectation', 'kind': 'source', 'value': 65, 'unit': 'percent', 'evidence': 'e5162', 'expression': '65% growth in Q4.', 'component': 'value'}\n{'id': 'q4_fy2027_estimate', 'what': {'population': 'NVIDIA', 'measure': 'revenue', 'scope': 'company', 'period': 'FY2027 Q4'}, 'basis': 'forecast', 'scenario': 'family base case', 'kind': 'computed', 'value': 112.2, 'unit': 'USD billions', 'component': 'value', 'inputs': ['q4_fy2026_actual', 'q4_fy2027_yoy_growth'], 'operation': 'apply_growth'}\nANS {'view_id': 'v4', 'outcome': 'About $403.6 billion in FY2027 total revenue.', 'reference': {'figure': '$411 billion FY2027 revenue consensus (e5204), in rung 2', 'unavailable': None}, 'cites': ['e111', 'e2649', 'e2652', 'e2452', 'e3406', 'e5054', 'e5055', 'e5056', 'e5162', 'e5204', 'e2870', 'e3115', 'e1040', 'e1041', 'e2635'], 'rung': 2}\ne2452 QUOTE For Q4 FY 2026, Nvidia expected $65 billion in revenue; it ended up producing $68 billion.\n  HEADER - e2452 [party_statement; fool.com (analyst); original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:835fa8a6ac898ca3973d586c 2026-08-23] NVIDIA guided to $65 billion in Q4 FY2026 revenue and reported actual revenue of $68 billion.\ne5162 QUOTE and 65% growth in Q4.\n  HEADER - e5162 [third_party_view; fool.com author; original source Wall Street analysts ; from gnews:ea4633ed3e4ad9d71383673f 2026-09-17] Wall Street analysts expect NVIDIA revenue to grow 65% year over year in FY2027 Q4.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_33","type":"agent_message","text":"I reproduced every recorded refusal. Two small replays confirmed separate problems: changing “first six months” to `H1` cleared the period refusal, and declaring the percentage calculation as `share` cleared the 100× arithmetic error. Other replies still have real problems, including a forecast that depends on itself."}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_34","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"python3 -B -c 'import json,pathlib,collections,re,sys,importlib.util\nD=pathlib.Path('\\\\''docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers'\\\\'')\nR=pathlib.Path('\\\\''poc/data/judging-v13-paid-gate-2026-11-22'\\\\'')\nP={(q['\\\\''unit'\\\\''],q['\\\\''arm'\\\\'']):q for q in json.loads((D/'\\\\''paid-plan.json'\\\\'').read_text())}\nJ={n:[(i,r) for i,l in enumerate((R/(n+'\\\\''.jsonl'\\\\'')).open(),1) if (r:=json.loads(l))['\\\\''status'\\\\'']\"'!='\"'\\\\''started'\\\\''] for n in ['\\\\''answers'\\\\'','\\\\''retries'\\\\'']}\ndef arm(r): return r['\\\\''arm'\\\\''] if r['\\\\''arm'\\\\''] in ('\\\\''joint'\\\\'','\\\\''single'\\\\'') else '\\\\''separate'\\\\''\ndef cat(e):\n c,s=e\n if c=='\\\\''C7'\\\\'':\n  if '\\\\''not defined'\\\\'' in s:return c+'\\\\'': dangling'\\\\''\n  if '\\\\''needs either a value'\\\\'' in s:return c+'\\\\'': point/range'\\\\''\n  if '\\\\''signs must'\\\\'' in s:return c+'\\\\'': signs'\\\\''\n  if '\\\\'' operands, not '\\\\'' in s:return c+'\\\\'': arity'\\\\''\n  if '\\\\''is not a figure'\\\\'' in s:return c+'\\\\'': outcome missing'\\\\''\n  if '\\\\'': outcome '\\\\'' in s and '\\\\'' measures '\\\\'' in s:return c+'\\\\'': outcome key'\\\\''\n  return c+'\\\\'': '\\\\''+s\n if c=='\\\\''C1'\\\\'':\n  if '\\\\''was not shown'\\\\'' in s:return c+'\\\\'': evidence'\\\\''\n  if '\\\\''not a complete'\\\\'' in s:return c+'\\\\'': expression'\\\\''\n  return c+'\\\\'': value/unit/etc'\\\\''\n if c=='\\\\''C2'\\\\'':\n  if '\\\\''cannot be evaluated'\\\\'' in s:return c+'\\\\'': eval'\\\\''\n  if '\\\\''gives'\\\\'' in s:return c+'\\\\'': arithmetic'\\\\''\n  return c+'\\\\'': bound'\\\\''\n if c=='\\\\''C8'\\\\'':\n  if '\\\\''time aggregation'\\\\'' in s:return c+'\\\\'': time'\\\\''\n  if '\\\\''roll_forward'\\\\'' in s:return c+'\\\\'': roll_forward'\\\\''\n  if '\\\\''with no bridge'\\\\'' in s:return c+'\\\\'': bridge'\\\\''\n  if '\\\\''states no relation'\\\\'' in s:return c+'\\\\'': relation'\\\\''\n  if '\\\\''share needs'\\\\'' in s:return c+'\\\\'': share'\\\\''\n  return c+'\\\\'': '\\\\''+s\n return c\ndef fields(d):\n for f in d['\\\\''figures'\\\\'']:\n  for k in ('\\\\''evidence'\\\\'','\\\\''bridge'\\\\'','\\\\''disputed'\\\\''):\n   yield k,f.get(k),f\n  for k in ('\\\\''inputs'\\\\'','\\\\''rests_on'\\\\'','\\\\''converts'\\\\''):\n   for v in f.get(k) or []:yield k,v,f\n  yield '\\\\''adjusts.figure'\\\\'',(f.get('\\\\''adjusts'\\\\'') or {}).get('\\\\''figure'\\\\''),f\n for a in d['\\\\''answers'\\\\'']:\n  yield '\\\\''answers[].outcome'\\\\'',a.get('\\\\''outcome'\\\\''),a\n  yield '\\\\''answers[].reference.figure'\\\\'',(a.get('\\\\''reference'\\\\'') or {}).get('\\\\''figure'\\\\''),a\ndef allowed(k,f,p):\n if k=='\\\\''evidence'\\\\'':return p['\\\\''passages'\\\\'']\n if k=='\\\\''rests_on'\\\\'':return set(f)|set(p['\\\\''passages'\\\\''])\n return f\nsys.path.insert(0,str(D))\nimport calc_check as cc\ndef passage(q,k):\n if k in q['\\\\''passages'\\\\'']:\n  print(k,'\\\\''QUOTE'\\\\'',q['\\\\''passages'\\\\''][k]['\\\\''text'\\\\''][:460])\n  lead=next((l for l in q['\\\\''user'\\\\''].splitlines() if l.startswith('\\\\''- '\\\\''+k+'\\\\'' ['\\\\'')),None)\n  if lead: print('\\\\''  HEADER'\\\\'',lead)\ndef show(n,l,ids=(),ps=(),fields_only=False):\n r=dict(J[n])[l]; q=P[r['\\\\''unit'\\\\''],r['\\\\''arm'\\\\'']]; d=r['\\\\''data'\\\\'']\n print('\\\\''\\\\n'\\\\'',n,l,r['\\\\''unit'\\\\''],r['\\\\''arm'\\\\''],r['\\\\''draw'\\\\''],'\\\\''ERRORS'\\\\'',r['\\\\''errors'\\\\''])\n for f in d['\\\\''figures'\\\\'']:\n  if ids and f['\\\\''id'\\\\''] not in ids: continue\n  print({k:v for k,v in f.items() if v is not None})\n for a in d['\\\\''answers'\\\\'']:\n  print('\\\\''ANS'\\\\'',{k:a[k] for k in ('\\\\''view_id'\\\\'','\\\\''outcome'\\\\'','\\\\''reference'\\\\'','\\\\''cites'\\\\'','\\\\''rung'\\\\'')})\n for k in ps:passage(q,k)\n if fields_only:\n  f={f['\\\\''id'\\\\''] for f in d['\\\\''figures'\\\\'']}\n  for k,v,obj in fields(d):\n   if v is not None and v not in allowed(k,f,q): print('\\\\''BAD FIELD'\\\\'',k,repr(v),obj.get('\\\\''id'\\\\'',obj.get('\\\\''view_id'\\\\'')))\n\ndef strip(x):\n if isinstance(x,dict):return {k:strip(v) for k,v in x.items() if v is not None}\n if isinstance(x,list):return [strip(y) for y in x]\n return x\nr=dict(J['\\\\''retries'\\\\''])[22]; q=P[r['\\\\''unit'\\\\''],r['\\\\''arm'\\\\'']]; c=strip(r['\\\\''data'\\\\''])\nc['\\\\''answers'\\\\''][0]['\\\\''outcome'\\\\'']='\\\\''fig_v6_forecast'\\\\''\nc['\\\\''figures'\\\\''][-1].pop('\\\\''bridge'\\\\'')\nbefore=cc.check(q['\\\\''family'\\\\''],q['\\\\''passages'\\\\''],c)['\\\\''errors'\\\\'']\nfor f in c['\\\\''figures'\\\\'']:\n if f['\\\\''unit'\\\\'']=='\\\\''USD trillion'\\\\'':f.update(unit='\\\\''USD bn'\\\\'',value=f['\\\\''value'\\\\'']*1000)\nafter=cc.check(q['\\\\''family'\\\\''],q['\\\\''passages'\\\\''],c)['\\\\''errors'\\\\'']\nprint('\\\\''S before'\\\\'',before,'\\\\''after'\\\\'',after)\nr=dict(J['\\\\''answers'\\\\''])[6]\nfor f in r['\\\\''data'\\\\'']['\\\\''figures'\\\\'']:\n if f['\\\\''id'\\\\''] in ('\\\\''dc_fy27_reference'\\\\'','\\\\''q3_total_revenue_third_party'\\\\''):print({k:v for k,v in f.items() if v is not None})\n'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
